helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153191				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/simpress/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Rulers\"\>Rulers\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	gu	You can use vertical and horizontal rulers at the left and upper edges of the $[officename] Impress workspace to assist you in creating your slide. The sections of the rulers that cover the area of the slide are white.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	gu	When you select an object, its dimensions are displayed on the rulers as gray double lines. To precisely resize the object, drag one of the double lines to a new location on the ruler.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3150206				0	gu	When you select a text object on a slide, indents and tabs are displayed on the horizontal ruler. To change the indent or tab settings for the text object, drag an indent or a tab marker to a new location on the ruler.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3150253				0	gu	You can also drag a \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/04030000.xhp\" name=\"snap line\"\>snap line\</link\> from a ruler to help you align objects on your slide. To insert a snap line using a ruler, drag the edge of a ruler into the slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3153820	3			0	gu	To show or hide the rulers, choose \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/03060000.xhp\" name=\"View - Rulers\"\>\<emph\>View - Rulers\</emph\>\</link\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3148609				0	gu	To specify the measurement units for a ruler, right-click the ruler, and then choose a new unit from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3149129				0	gu	To change the origin (0 point) of the rulers, drag the intersection of the two rulers in the top left corner into the workspace. Vertical and horizontal guides appear. Continue to drag until the vertical and horizontal guides are where you want the new origin to be, and then release. To reset the origins of the rulers to the default values, double-click the intersection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0209.xhp	0	help	par_id3154651				0	gu	To change the slide margins, drag the edge of the white areas in the rulers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	$[officename] Impress Features				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	gu	\<variable id=\"main0503\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/main0503.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Impress Features\"\>$[officename] Impress Features\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3151074				0	gu	$[officename] Impress lets you create professional slide shows that can include charts, drawing objects, text, multimedia and a variety of other items. If you want, you can even import and modify Microsoft PowerPoint presentations.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	gu	For on-screen slide shows, animation, slide transitions and multimedia are a few of the techniques you can use to make your presentation more exciting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154016				0	gu	Creating Vector Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3154485				0	gu	Many of the tools for creating vector graphics in $[officename] Draw are available in $[officename] Impress.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150208				0	gu	Creating Slides				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3153247				0	gu	$[officename] Impress provides you with templates to create professional-looking slides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610	14			0	gu	You can also assign a number of  dynamic effects to your slides, including animation and transition  effects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153820				0	gu	Creating Presentations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3153917				0	gu	Several views or pages are available when you design a slide show. For example, the Slide Sorter displays an overview of your slides in thumbnail form, while the Handout page contains both the slide and the text you want to distribute to the audience.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3148608				0	gu	$[officename] Impress also lets you rehearse the timing of your slide show.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154649				0	gu	Publishing Presentations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046				0	gu	You can publish your slides on-screen, as handouts, or as HTML documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146965				0	gu	Giving Presentations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\main0503.xhp	0	help	par_id3145114				0	gu	$[officename] Impress gives you the choice of running a slide show automatically or manually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
