helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153536				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090006.xhp\" name=\"Database\"\>Database\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3154471				0	gu	You can insert fields from any database, for example, address fields, into your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196				0	gu	Field type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149096				0	gu	Any Record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3151257				0	gu	Inserts the contents of the database field that you specify in the \<emph\>Record Number\</emph\> box as a mail merge field if the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"Condition\"\>\<emph\>Condition\</emph\>\</link\> that you enter is met. Only records selected by a multiple selection in the data source view are considered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147100				0	gu	You can use this field to insert several records into a document. Simply insert the \<emph\>Any Record\</emph\> field in front of the form letter fields that use a certain record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	gu	Database Name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3152776	9			0	gu	Inserts the name of the database table selected in the \<emph\>Database selection \</emph\>box. The "Database Name" field is a global field, that is, if you insert a different database name in your document, the contents of all previously inserted "Database Name" fields are updated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149167				0	gu	Mail merge field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3145779				0	gu	Inserts the name of a database field as a placeholder, so that you can create a mail merge document. The field content is automatically inserted when you print the form letter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3151372				0	gu	Next record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114				0	gu	Inserts the contents of the next mail merge field in your document, if the condition that you define is met. The records that you want to include must be selected in the data source view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	gu	You can use the "Next record" field to insert the contents of consecutive records between the mail merge fields in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147495				0	gu	Inserts the number of the selected database record.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	gu	Database Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DB_SELECTION_TLB\"\>Select the database table or the database query that you want the field to refer to.\</ahelp\> You can include fields from more than one database or query in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3147739				0	gu	If you want, you can assign a condition that must be met before the contents of the "Any Record" and "Next Record" fields are inserted. The default condition is "True", that is, the condition is always true if you do not change the condition text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DB:ED_DBSETNUMBER\"\>Enter the number of the record that you want to insert when the condition that you specify is met.\</ahelp\> The record number corresponds to the current selection in the data source view. For example, if you select the last 5 records in a database containing 10 records, the number of the first record will be 1, and not 6.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305				0	gu	If you refer to fields in a different database (or in a different table or query within the same database), $[officename] determines the record number relative to the current selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150904				0	gu	From database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_id3150922				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:TP_FLD_DB:RB_DBOWNFORMAT\"\>Uses the format defined in the selected database.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	par_idN10772				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"878711313\"\>Opens a file open dialog where you can select a database file (*.odb). The selected file is added to the Databases Selection list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090006.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155084				0	gu	User defined				2002-02-02 02:02:02
