helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149806	2			0	gu	\<variable id=\"textmarkeein\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertBookmark\"\>Inserts a bookmark at the cursor position. You can then use the Navigator to quickly jump to the marked location at a later time.\</ahelp\> In an HTML document, bookmarks are converted to anchors that you can jump to from a hyperlink.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153677	3			0	gu	To jump to a specific bookmark, press F5 to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>, click the plus sign (+) next to the\<emph\> Bookmark\</emph\> entry, and then double-click the bookmark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151308				0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>You can also right-click the \<emph\>Page Number\</emph\> field at the left end of the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the document window, and then choose the bookmark that you want to jump to.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
