helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152946				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SORTING:RB_DN3\"\>Sorts in descending order (for example, 9, 8, 7 or z, y, x).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150973				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SORTING:RB_COL\"\>Sorts the columns in the table according to the current sort options.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147526				0	gu	Row				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153677				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SORTING:RB_ROW\"\>Sorts the rows in the table or the paragraphs in the selection according to the current sort options.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150350				0	gu	Paragraphs are separated by nonprinting paragraph marks. You can also specify that tabs or a character act as separators when you sort paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_SORTING:RB_TAB\"\>If the selected paragraphs correspond to a list separated by tabs, select this option.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154190				0	gu	Characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159196				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:DLG_SORTING:ED_TABCH\"\>Enter the character that you want to use as a separator in the selected area.\</ahelp\> By using the separator, $[officename] can determine the position of the sorting key in the selected paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_DLG_SORTING_PB_DELIM\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Special Characters\</emph\> dialog, where you can select the character that you want to use as a separator.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151252				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_SORTING_LB_LANG\"\>Select the language that defines the sorting rules.\</ahelp\> Some languages sort special characters differently than other languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154838				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_DLG_SORTING_CB_CASE\"\>Distinguishes between uppercase and lowercase letters when you sort a table. For asian languages special handling applies.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10895				0	gu	For asian languages, select \<emph\>Match case \</emph\>to apply multi-level collation. In the multi-level collation, the primitive forms of the entries are first compared with the cases of the forms and diacritics ignored. If the forms are the same, the diacritics of the forms are compared. If the forms are still the same, the cases, character widths, and Japanese Kana differences of the forms are compared.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Entries (table of contents)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145827				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120221.xhp\" name=\"Entries (table of contents)\"\>Entries (table of contents)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3150017				0	gu	\<variable id=\"eintraege\"\>Specify the format of the entries in the table of contents. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148774				0	gu	Levels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3147169				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select the level that you want to define.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147569				0	gu	Structure and formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638	7			0	gu	The \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>line displays the table of contents code for the selected heading level. To change the appearance of a heading level you can enter codes or text in the empty boxes on this line. You can also click in an empty box or on a code, and then click a code button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3149292	35			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays the remainder of the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>line.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3147512	8			0	gu	To delete a code from the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>line, click the code, and then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Delete\</item\> key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3149806	9			0	gu	To replace a code from the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>line, click the code, and then click a code button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480	10			0	gu	To replace a code from the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>line, click the code, and then click a code button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153675				0	gu	Chapter number (E#)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3154567	12			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_ENTRY:PB_ENTRYNO\"\>Inserts the complete chapter heading, including, if available, the chapter number. To assign chapter numbering to a heading style, choose\<emph\> Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149691				0	gu	Entry text (E)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3154199				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_ENTRY:PB_ENTRY\"\>Inserts the text of the chapter heading.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143276				0	gu	Tab stop (T)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3149490	16			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_ENTRY:PB_TAB\"\>Inserts a tab stop. To add leader dots to the tab stop, select a character in the \<emph\>Fill character box\</emph\>. To change the position of the tab stop, enter a value in the \<emph\>Tab stop position \</emph\>box, or select the \<emph\>Align right \</emph\>check box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151257				0	gu	Page number (#)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3148981				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_ENTRY:PB_PAGENO\"\>Inserts the page number of the entry.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147212				0	gu	 Hyperlink (LS and LE)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3153631	20			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_ENTRY:PB_HYPERLINK\"\>Creates a hyperlink for the part of the entry that you enclose by the opening (LS) and the closing (LE) hyperlink tags. On the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>line, click in the empty box in front of the part that you want to create a hyperlink for, and then click this button. Click in the empty box after the part that you want to hyperlink, and then click this button again. All hyperlinks must be unique.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3155137				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_ENTRY:PB_ALL_LEVELS\"\>Applies the current settings to all of the table of contents levels.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
