helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150677				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3154020\" src=\"sd/res/imagelst/nv05.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154020\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155539				0	gu	You can jump quickly to index entries with the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110100.xhp\" name=\"Navigation Bar\"\>Navigation Bar\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148768				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>editing; concordance files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>concordance files; definition\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154645				0	gu	To access the Edit Concordance File dialog:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3149292				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables - Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420	21			0	gu	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>box, select "Alphabetical Index".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154107	22			0	gu	In the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Concordance file\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153668				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>File\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\> or \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470	24			0	gu	A concordance file contains the following fields: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3152953				0	gu	"Search term" refers to the index entry that you want to mark in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	gu	"Alternative entry" refers to the index entry that you want to appear in the index.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154194				0	gu	The 1st and 2nd Keys are parent index entries. The "Search term" or the "Alternative entry" appears as a subentry under the 1st and 2nd Keys.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155184				0	gu	"Match case" means that uppercase and lowercase letters are considered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3143282				0	gu	"Word only" searches for the term as a single word.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3147220				0	gu	To enable the "Match case" or "Word only" options, click in the corresponding cell, and then select the check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153629				0	gu	To create a concordance file without the Edit Concordance File dialog:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153644				0	gu	Use the following format guidelines when you create a concordance file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3152770				0	gu	Each entry in the concordance file is on a separate line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	gu	Commented lines start with #.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153354				0	gu	Use the following format for the entries:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3149172				0	gu	Search term;Alternative entry;1st key;2nd key;Match case;Word only				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3156270				0	gu	The entries "Match case" and "Word only" are interpreted as "No" or FALSE if they are empty or zero (0). All other contents are interpreted as "Yes" or TRUE.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	gu	For example, to include the word "Boston" in your alphabetical index under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line in the concordance file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	gu	Boston;Boston;Cities;;0;0 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151383				0	gu	This also finds "Boston" if it is written in lowercase letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155866				0	gu	To include the "Beacon Hill" district in Boston under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3150116	18			0	gu	Beacon Hill;Boston;Cities; 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Web Layout				2002-02-02 02:02:02
