helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145243				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04070100.xhp\" name=\"Envelope\"\>Envelope\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_ENV_ENV\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Enter the delivery and return addresses for the envelope. You can also insert address fields from a database, for example from the Addresses database.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145415	4			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:MULTILINEEDIT:TP_ENV_ENV:EDT_ADDR\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Enter the delivery address.\</ahelp\> You can also click in this box, and select a database, a table, and field, and then click the arrow button to insert the field in the address. If you want, you can apply  formatting, such as bold and underline, to the address text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	6			0	gu	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\"SW:MULTILINEEDIT:TP_ENV_ENV:EDT_SEND\"\>Includes a return address on the envelope. Select the \<emph\>Sender \</emph\>check box, and then enter the return  address.\</ahelp\> $[officename] automatically inserts your user data in the \<emph\>Sender \</emph\>box, but you can also enter the data that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_ENV_ENV:LB_DATABASE\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Select the database containing the address data that you want to insert.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151310				0	gu	Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155898				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_ENV_ENV:LB_TABLE\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Select the database table containing the address data that you want to insert.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155180				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:IMAGEBUTTON:TP_ENV_ENV:BTN_INSERT\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Select the database field containing the address data that you want to insert, and then click the left arrow button. The data is added to the address box containing the cursor.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Current Index				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06160000.xhp\" name=\"Current Index\"\>Current Index\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149499				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:UpdateCurIndex\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Updates the current index.\</ahelp\> The current index is the one that contains the cursor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154763				0	gu	You can also right-click in an index or table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>. The following commands are also available in the context menu:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146967				0	gu	Edit Index/Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:EditCurIndex\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Edits the current index or table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147403				0	gu	Delete Index/Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06160000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155625				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RemoveTableOf\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Deletes the current index or table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Page Formatting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06120000.xhp\" name=\"Page Formatting\"\>Page Formatting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249				0	gu	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\".uno:Repaginate\"\>Updates the page formats in the document and recalculates the total number of pages that is displayed on the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	gu	In long documents, updating the page formatting can take a while.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Functions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149123				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090003.xhp\" name=\"Functions\"\>Functions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150343				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_FUNCVALUE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets additional function parameters for fields. The type of parameter depends on the field type that you select.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	gu	Depending on the field type that you select, you can assign conditions to certain functions. For example, you can define a field that executes a macro when you click the field in the document, or a condition that, when met, hides a field. You can also define placeholder fields that insert graphics, tables, frames and other objects into your document when needed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152999				0	gu	Conditional text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149881	6			0	gu	Inserts text if a certain \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\> is met. For example, enter "sun eq 1" in the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box, and then the text that you want to insert when the variable "sun" equals "1" in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box. If you want, you can also enter the text that you want to display when this condition is not met in the \<emph\>Else\</emph\> box. To define the variable "sun", click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090005.xhp\" name=\"Variables\"\>\<emph\>Variables\</emph\>\</link\> tab, select "Set variable", type "sun" in the\<emph\> Name\</emph\> box, and its value in the\<emph\> Value\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153719				0	gu	Input list				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147564				0	gu	Inserts a text field that displays one item from a list. You can add, edit, and remove items, and change their order in the list. Click an \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> field in your document or press Ctrl+Shift+F9 to display the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090003.xhp\" name=\"Choose Item\"\>\<emph\>Choose Item\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287				0	gu	Inserts a text field that you can open by \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090100.xhp\" name=\"clicking\"\>clicking\</link\> it in the document. You can then change the text that is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154691				0	gu	Execute macro				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515	10			0	gu	Inserts a text field that runs a macro when you click the field in the document. To assign a macro to the field, click the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> button. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	gu	Inserts a placeholder field in the document, for example, for graphics. When you click a placeholder field in the document, you are prompted to insert the item that is missing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	gu	Hidden Paragraph				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154192	39			0	gu	Combine characters 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3159199				0	gu	Combines up to 6 characters, so that they behave as a single character. This feature is only available when Asian fonts are supported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151329				0	gu	For function fields, the format field is only used for fields of the type placeholder. Here, the format determines the object for which the placeholder stands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3143281				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DB:ED_DBCONDITION\"\>For fields linked to a \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090200.xhp\" name=\"condition\"\>condition\</link\>, enter the criteria here.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154830	21			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_FUNCCOND2\"\>Enter the text to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box, and the text to display when the condition is not met in the \<emph\>Else \</emph\>box.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865	22			0	gu	You can also insert database fields in the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>and \<emph\>Else \</emph\>boxes using the format "databasename.tablename.fieldname".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147583				0	gu	If the table or the field name does not exist in a database, nothing is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3152585				0	gu	If you include the quotes in "databasename.tablename.fieldname", the expression is inserted as text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155136				0	gu	References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155149	27			0	gu	Type the text that you want to display in the field. If you are inserting a placeholder field, type the text that you want to display as a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	gu	Select the macro that you want to run when the field is clicked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153351				0	gu	Displays the name of the selected macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3156282				0	gu	Type the text that you want to appear in the placeholder field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149173				0	gu	Type the text that you want to hide if a condition is met.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151028				0	gu	Characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3145771				0	gu	Enter the characters that you want to combine. You can combine a maximum of 6 characters. This option is only available for the \<emph\>Combine characters\</emph\> field type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	gu	Enter a value for the selected field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148877				0	gu	Macros				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155912				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_FLD_FUNC_BT_FUNCMACRO\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Macro Selector\</emph\>, where you can choose the macro that will run when you click the selected field in the document.\</ahelp\> This button is only available for the "Execute macro" function field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150111				0	gu	The following controls are displayed for \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> fields:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155860				0	gu	Item				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150688				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_LISTITEM\"\>Enter a new item.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147473				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_FLD_FUNC_PB_LISTADD\"\>Adds the \<emph\>Item\</emph\> to the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147496				0	gu	Items on list				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FLD_FUNC_LB_LISTITEMS\"\>Lists the items. The topmost item is shown in the document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149558				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_FLD_FUNC_PB_LISTREMOVE\"\>Removes the selected item from the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145126				0	gu	Move Up				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3155970				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_FLD_FUNC_PB_LISTUP\"\>Moves the selected item up in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150549				0	gu	Move Down				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3156221				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_TP_FLD_FUNC_PB_LISTDOWN\"\>Moves the selected item down in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147733				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_EDIT_TP_FLD_FUNC_ED_LISTNAME\"\>Enter a unique name for the \<emph\>Input list\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146332				0	gu	Choose Item				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3147455	65			0	gu	This dialog is shown when you click an \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> field in the document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149837				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_FLD_DROPDOWN_LB_LISTITEMS\"\>Choose the item that you want to display in the document, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3148855				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_DLG_FLD_DROPDOWN_PB_EDIT\"\>Displays the \<emph\>Edit Fields: Functions\</emph\> dialog, where you can edit the \<emph\>Input list\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090003.xhp	0	help	par_id3148434				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_PUSHBUTTON_DLG_FLD_DROPDOWN_PB_NEXT\"\>Closes the current \<emph\>Input list\</emph\> and displays the next, if available.\</ahelp\> You see this button when you open the \<emph\>Choose Item\</emph\> dialog by Ctrl+Shift+F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154478				0	gu	\<variable id=\"umlauftext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:TextWrap\"\>Specify the way you want text to wrap around an object.\</ahelp\> You can also specify the spacing between the text and the object. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151249				0	gu	To wrap text around a table, place the table in a frame, and then wrap the text around the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147100				0	gu	\<variable id=\"keinumlauftext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SW:IMAGERADIOBUTTON:TP_FRM_WRAP:RB_NO_WRAP\"\>Places the object on a separate line in the document. The Text in the document appears above and below the object, but not on the sides of the object.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149171				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:IMAGERADIOBUTTON:TP_FRM_WRAP:RB_WRAP_LEFT\"\>Wraps text on the left side of the object if there is enough space.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:IMAGERADIOBUTTON:TP_FRM_WRAP:RB_WRAP_RIGHT\"\>Wraps text on the right side of the object if there is enough space.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147740				0	gu	\<variable id=\"seitenumlauftext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SW:IMAGERADIOBUTTON:TP_FRM_WRAP:RB_WRAP_PARALLEL\"\>Wraps text on all four sides of the border frame of the object.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154089				0	gu	\<variable id=\"durchlauftext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SW:IMAGERADIOBUTTON:TP_FRM_WRAP:RB_WRAP_THROUGH\"\>Places the object in front of the text.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154716	24			0	gu	\<variable id=\"dynamischertext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:WrapIdeal\"\>Automatically wraps text to the left, to the right, or on all four sides of the border frame of the object. If the distance between the object and the page margin is less than 2 cm, the text is not wrapped. \</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
