helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150912				0	gu	Inserts the keywords as entered in the \<emph\>Description \</emph\>tab of the \<emph\>File Properties \</emph\>dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3146942				0	gu	Inserts the subject as entered in the \<emph\>Description \</emph\>tab of the \<emph\>File Properties \</emph\>dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150033				0	gu	Inserts the title as entered in the \<emph\>Description \</emph\>tab of the \<emph\>File Properties \</emph\>dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	gu	For the "Created", "Modified", and "Last printed" field types, you can include the author, date, and time of the corresponding operation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149608				0	gu	Fixed content				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_FLD_DOKINF:CB_DOKINFFIXEDCONTENT\"\>Inserts the field as static content, that is, the field cannot be updated.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155554				0	gu	Fields with fixed content are only evaluated when you create a new document from a template that contains such a field. For example, a date field with fixed content inserts the date that a new document was created from the template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	gu	\<variable id=\"rahm\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertFrame\"\>Inserts a frame that you can use to create a layout of one or more columns of text and objects.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153678				0	gu	To edit a frame, click the border to select it, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Frame\</emph\>. You can also resize or move a selected frame using special \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04130100.xhp\" name=\"shortcut keys\"\>shortcut keys\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152952				0	gu	To delete a frame, click the border of the frame, and then press Delete.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151311				0	gu	If you see small red arrows at the beginning and the end of text in frame, use the arrow keys to scroll through the remaining text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	gu	In the preview area of the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> dialog, the frame is represented by a green rectangle, and the reference area by a red rectangle.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149694				0	gu	You can also preview the effects when you change the frame anchor to "As Character". The "Baseline" is drawn in red, "Character" is the font height, and "line" is the height of the line, including the frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149107				0	gu	Icon on the Insert toolbar:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	gu	\<variable id=\"syrahmentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertFrameInteract\"\>Draws a frame where you drag in the document. Click the arrow next to the icon to select the number of columns for the frame.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
