helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155182				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>characters; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters; text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>uppercase; formatting text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;cases of text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>initial capitals in titles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155182				0	gu	\<variable id=\"text_capital\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_capital.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Case of Text\"\>Changing the Case of Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916				0	gu	You can change the case of text, format text with small capitals, or capitalize the first letter of each word in a selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	gu	When you apply a formatting to your text by \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, the text stays the same, it is only displayed in another way. On the other hand, when you choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case\</emph\>, the text is permanently changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155861				0	gu	To capitalize text:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3147420				0	gu	Select the text that you want to capitalize.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149644				0	gu	To change text to lowercase:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149964				0	gu	Select the text that you want to change to lowercase.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155183				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; inserting and deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages; inserting/deleting page breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>manual page breaks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155183				0	gu	\<variable id=\"page_break\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/page_break.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks\"\>Inserting and Deleting Page Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	gu	To insert a manual page break:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	gu	Click in your document where you want the new page to begin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	gu	Press Ctrl+Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153135				0	gu	To delete a manual page break:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	gu	Click in front of the first character on the page that follows the manual page break.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3149608				0	gu	Press Backspace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149624				0	gu	To delete a manual page break that occurs before a table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3145111				0	gu	Right-click in the table, and choose \<emph\>Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3156254				0	gu	Click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05090300.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>\<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\page_break.xhp	0	help	par_id3153380				0	gu	Clear the \<emph\>Break\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>sections; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents;inserting linked sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;linked sections, manually\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links;inserting sections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	gu	\<variable id=\"section_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Sections\"\>Inserting Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	gu	You can insert new sections, or links to sections in other documents into the current document. If you insert a section as a link, the content of the link changes when you modify the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	gu	To insert a new section:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	gu	Click in your document where you want to insert a new section, or select the text that you want to convert to a section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156103				0	gu	If you select a text that occurs within a paragraph, the text is automatically converted into a new paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Record\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	gu	Set the options for the section, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149635				0	gu	To insert a section as a link:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648				0	gu	Before you can insert a section as link, you must first create sections in the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	gu	When you open a document that contains linked sections, $[officename] prompts you to update the contents of the sections. To manually update a link, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Links\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149860				0	gu	You can also insert linked sections in HTML documents. When you view the page in a web browsers, the content of the sections corresponds to the content of the sections at the time the HTML document was last saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145104				0	gu	Click in your document where you want to insert the linked section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Record\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Link \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Link \</emph\>check box. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>Under Windows, you can also select the \<emph\>DDE\</emph\> check box to automatically update the contents of the section when the section in the source document is changed. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155882				0	gu	Locate the document containing the section that you want to link to, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150003				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
