helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155855				0	gu	\<variable id=\"indices_form\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_form.xhp\" name=\"Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\"\>Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3154259				0	gu	You can apply different paragraph styles, assign hyperlinks to entries, change the layout of indexes, and change the background color of indexes in the \<emph\>Insert Index\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155888				0	gu	To apply a different paragraph style to an index level:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	gu	Right-click in the index or table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147135	46			0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Styles \</emph\>tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150229	47			0	gu	Click an index level in the \<emph\>Levels \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934	48			0	gu	Click the style that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960				0	gu	Click the assign button \<emph\><\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150516				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146878				0	gu	To assign hyperlinks to entries in a table of contents:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3146890				0	gu	You can assign a cross-reference as a hyperlink to entries in a table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150712				0	gu	Right-click in the table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150738				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148424	53			0	gu	In the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>area, click in the box in front of \<emph\>E#\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3153171				0	gu	Click in the box behind the \<emph\>E\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147060				0	gu	Repeat for each heading level that you want to create hyperlinks for, or click the \<emph\>All levels\</emph\> button to apply the formatting to all levels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
