helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	About Headers and Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155863				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>headers;about\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;about\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	gu	\<variable id=\"header_footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_footer.xhp\" name=\"About Headers and Footers\"\>About Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	gu	Headers and footers are areas in the top and the bottom page margins, where you can add text or graphics. Headers and footers are added to the current page style. Any page that uses the same style automatically receives the header or footer that you add. You can insert \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>, such as page numbers and chapter headings, in headers and footers in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	gu	The page style for the current page is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	gu	To add a header to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147119				0	gu	To add a footer to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3146876				0	gu	To use different headers or footers in your document, you must add them to different \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>, and then apply the styles to the pages where you want the headers or footer to appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150704				0	gu	Headers and Footers in HTML Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C6				0	gu	 Inserting an additional space character 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B03				0	gu	 Select \<emph\>Append space\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B0E				0	gu	 The space character is appended after you type the first character of the next word after the auto-completed word. The space character is suppressed if the next character is a delimiter, such as a full stop or a new line character. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B20				0	gu	 Choose the key to accept the suggested word using the \<emph\>Accept with\</emph\> list box. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B36				0	gu	 Use the \<emph\>Min. word length\</emph\> box to set the minimum number of characters a word must have to be collected into the list. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	gu	 Selecting the scope of collected words 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B53				0	gu	 Now the list is also valid for other documents that you open. When you close the last %PRODUCTNAME document, the word list is deleted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B56				0	gu	 If you do not select the checkbox, the list is only valid as long as the current document is open. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2634968				0	gu	If you want the word list to exist longer than the current %PRODUCTNAME session, save it as a document, as described in the following section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B94				0	gu	 If the automatic spellcheck option is enabled, only the words that are recognized by the spellcheck are collected. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA1				0	gu	 Use the word list to always start with a defined set of technical terms for the word completion feature. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA7				0	gu	 Open the text document that contains the terms that you want to use for word completion. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BAB				0	gu	 The word completion feature collects the words. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	gu	 Select all or some of the words in the list. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BC6				0	gu	 Later you can open the reference list and automatically collect the words, so that the word completion feature starts with a defined set of words. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040600.xhp\"\>Word Completion \</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Templates and Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153396				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>formatting styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>organizing; templates (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; organizing (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153396				0	gu	\<variable id=\"templates_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/templates_styles.xhp\" name=\"Templates and Styles\"\>Templates and Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	gu	A template is a document that contains specific formatting styles, graphics, tables, object, and other information. A template is used as the basis for creating other documents. For example, you can define paragraph and character styles in a document, save the document as a template, and then use the template to create a new document with the same styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149974				0	gu	$[officename] has a number of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"predefined templates\"\>predefined templates\</link\> that you can use to create different types or text documents, such as business letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149613				0	gu	Viewing and Organizing Styles in Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	gu	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Template Management\"\>Template Management\</link\> dialog to copy styles from one document to another.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153377				0	gu	To copy a style, drag it to another template or document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Preventing Hyphenation of Specific Words				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3153658	41			0	gu	Select a dictionary in the \<emph\>User-defined dictionary \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125				0	gu	If the list is empty, click \<emph\>New\</emph\> to create a dictionary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150218	42			0	gu	In the\<emph\> Word\</emph\> box, type the word you want to exclude from hyphenation, followed by an equal sign (=), for example, "pretentious=".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150247				0	gu	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147036	29			0	gu	To quickly exclude a word from hyphenation, select the word, choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Font \</emph\>tab, and select "None" in the \<emph\>Language \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	User Defined Borders in Text Documents 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3614917				0	gu	\<variable id=\"borders\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/borders.xhp\"\>User Defined Borders in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1069368				0	gu	You can apply a variety of different cell borders to selected cells in a Writer table and to the whole table. Other objects in text documents can have user defined borders, too. For example, you can assign borders to page styles, to frames, and to inserted pictures or charts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6527298				0	gu	Select the cell or a block of cells in a Writer table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6129947				0	gu	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table - Table properties\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8141117				0	gu	In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6016418				0	gu	Choose the border options you want to apply and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5282448				0	gu	The options in the \<emph\>Line arrangement\</emph\> area can be used to apply multiple border styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
