helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id570085				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id4776757\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_5.png\" width=\"1.2811inch\" height=\"1.6043inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4776757\"\>block selected border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5044099				0	gu	Default settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id626544				0	gu	Click one of the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icons to set or reset multiple borders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id292062				0	gu	The thin gray lines inside an icon show the borders that will be reset or cleared.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1361735				0	gu	The dark lines inside an icon show the lines that will be set using the selected line style and color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id82399				0	gu	The thick gray lines inside an icon show the lines that will not be changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5528427				0	gu	Select a block of about 8x8 cells, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4194158				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id8221076\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_5.png\" width=\"1.1354inch\" height=\"0.25inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8221076\"\>default icons for borders\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7253028				0	gu	Click the left icon to clear all lines. This removes all outer borders and all inner lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9441206				0	gu	Click the second icon from the left to set an outer border and to remove all other lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7276833				0	gu	Click the rightmost icon to set an outer border. The inner lines are not changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5273293				0	gu	Now you can continue to see which lines the other icons will set or remove.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5110019				0	gu	User defined settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1820734				0	gu	In the \<emph\>User defined\</emph\> area, you can click to set or remove individual lines. The preview shows lines in three different states. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7093111				0	gu	Repeatedly click an edge or a corner to switch through the three different states.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
