helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6485793				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id1237525\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.2709inch\" height=\"1.1354inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1237525\"\>solid line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1454512				0	gu	A black line sets the corresponding line of the selected cells. The line is shown as a dotted line when you choose the 0.05 pt line style. Double lines are shown when you select a double line style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4618671				0	gu	A gray line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1239356				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id2688680\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_7.png\" width=\"1.2709inch\" height=\"1.1457inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2688680\"\>gray line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9474166				0	gu	A gray line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1545457				0	gu	A white line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1681875				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id7340617\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_8.png\" width=\"1.2709inch\" height=\"1.1354inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7340617\"\>white line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2316660				0	gu	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5118564				0	gu	Select a single cell in a Writer table, then choose \<emph\>Table - Table properties - Borders\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id244758				0	gu	Select a thick line style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7741325				0	gu	To set a lower border, click the lower edge repeatedly until you see a thick line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id542313				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id4273506\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.2709inch\" height=\"1.1354inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4273506\"\>setting thick lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2210760				0	gu	All cells in a Writer table have at least a left and a lower line by default. Most cells on the table perimeter have more lines applied by default. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5400860				0	gu	All lines that are shown in white in the preview will be removed from the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Emphasizing Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
