helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	gu	Click the icon of the style category that you want to update.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	gu	Click in the document where you want to copy the style from, for example, in a paragraph that you applied manual formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154411				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153373				0	gu	To create a new style by drag-and-drop:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	gu	Click the icon of the style category that you want to update.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154851				0	gu	Select at least one character, or object, in the style that you want to copy. For page and frame styles, select at least one character or object in the page or frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	gu	Drag the character or object to the Styles and Formatting window and release.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	gu	For Paragraph and Character Styles, you can drag-and-drop onto the respective icon in the Styles and Formatting window. You do not need to open that style category in advance.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B5				0	gu	You can also drag-and-drop a frame into the Styles and Formatting window to create a new frame style: Click the frame, wait a moment with the mouse button pressed down, but without moving the mouse, then drag to the Styles and Formatting window and drop the frame onto the Frame Styles icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Adding Line Numbers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150101				0	gu	\<variable id=\"numbering_lines\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_lines.xhp\" name=\"Adding Line Numbers\"\>Adding Line Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153410				0	gu	To add line numbers to an entire document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	gu	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>, and then select the options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3145101				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156241				0	gu	To add line numbers to specific paragraphs:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3156264				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153385				0	gu	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	gu	Right-click the "Default" paragraph style and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150222				0	gu	All paragraph styles are based on the "Default" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Numbering\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3151077				0	gu	Select the paragraph(s) where you want to add the line numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153733				0	gu	Select \<emph\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153758				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3146864				0	gu	You can also create a paragraph style that includes line numbering, and apply it to the paragraphs that you want to add line numbers to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146880				0	gu	To specify the starting line number:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150703				0	gu	Click in a paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153804				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153934				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06180000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Line Numbering\"\>Tools - Line Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153960				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030800.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Numbering\"\>Format - Paragraph - Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158970				0	gu	To hide text:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5684072				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Find \</emph\>or\<emph\> Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id24109				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Find \</emph\>or\<emph\> Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4679403				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7783745				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Find \</emph\>or\<emph\> Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Indexes Covering Several Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	gu	\<variable id=\"indices_multidoc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_multidoc.xhp\" name=\"Indexes Covering Several Documents\"\>Indexes Covering Several Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	gu	There are several ways to create an index that spans several documents:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	gu	Create an \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120210.xhp\" name=\"index in each individual document\"\>index in each individual document\</link\>, copy and paste the indexes into a single document, and then edit them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150230				0	gu	Create a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010001.xhp\" name=\"master document\"\>master document\</link\>, add the files that you want to include in the index as subdocuments, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting Page Numbers in Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155624				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>footers; with page numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pages; numbers and count of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page numbers; footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering;pages\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155624				0	gu	\<variable id=\"footer_pagenumber\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footer_pagenumber.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\"\>Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3153155				0	gu	If you want, you can align the Page Number field as you would text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3155554				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155919				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>running titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>floating titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; chapter information\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>names; chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919				0	gu	\<variable id=\"header_with_chapter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_chapter.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\"\>Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	gu	Before you can insert chapter information into a header or footer, you must first set the outline numbering options for the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154244				0	gu	To create a paragraph style for chapter titles:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155874				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155898				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Style \</emph\>box, select the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles, for example, "Heading 1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150949				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150505				0	gu	To insert the chapter name and number in a header or a footer:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150527				0	gu	Apply the paragraph style that you defined for chapter titles to the chapter headings in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153762				0	gu	Click in the header or footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147065				0	gu	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147095				0	gu	The header on every page that uses the current page style automatically displays the chapter name and number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Navigating and Selecting With the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159260				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>text; navigating and selecting with keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>navigating; in text, with keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;text, with keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard; navigating and selecting in text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159260				0	gu	\<variable id=\"text_nav_keyb\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_nav_keyb.xhp\" name=\"Navigating and Selecting With the Keyboard\"\>Navigating and Selecting With the Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155179				0	gu	You can navigate through a document and make selections with the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918				0	gu	Key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155870				0	gu	કાર્યક્રમ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3156220	25			0	gu	\<emph\>+\</emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>Command key\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Ctrl key\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	gu	Right, left arrow keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	gu	Moves the cursor one character to the left or to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	gu	Moves the cursor one word to the left or to the right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149629				0	gu	Up, down arrow keys				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	gu	Moves the cursor up or down one line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149871				0	gu	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the current line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	gu	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	gu	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the contents in the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3145409				0	gu	Moves the cursor to the beginning of the contents of the current cell. Press again to move the cursor to the first cell in the table. Press again to move the cursor to the beginning of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3153372				0	gu	Moves the cursor to the end of the current line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154235				0	gu	Moves the cursor to the end of the document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873				0	gu	Moves to the end of the contents in the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155894				0	gu	Moves the cursor to the end of the contents of the current cell. Press again to move the cursor to the last cell in the table. Press again to move the cursor to the end of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3155944				0	gu	PgUp				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3148678				0	gu	Scrolls up one page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3148701				0	gu	Moves the cursor to the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3149998				0	gu	PgDn				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3153018				0	gu	Scroll down one page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_nav_keyb.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949				0	gu	Moves the cursor to the footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>references; inserting cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting and updating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	gu	\<variable id=\"references\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/references.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Cross-References\"\>Inserting Cross-References\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3159263				0	gu	Cross-references allow you to jump to specific text passages and objects in a single document. A cross-reference consists of a target and a reference that are inserted as \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	gu	Objects with captions and bookmarks can be used as targets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	gu	Cross-Referencing Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	gu	Before you can insert a cross-reference, you must first specify the targets in your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	gu	To insert a target:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	gu	Select the text that you want to use as a target for the cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	gu	Type a name for the target in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box. The selected text is displayed in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	gu	Leave the dialog open and proceed to the next section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153370				0	gu	To create a cross-reference to a target:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153392				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select "Insert Reference".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the target that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154856				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, select the format for the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the target text, and "Page" inserts the page number where the target is located.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149980				0	gu	Cross-Referencing an Object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	gu	You can cross-reference most objects in your document, such as graphics, drawing objects, OLE objects, and tables, so long as they have a caption. To add a caption to an object, select the object, and then choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Caption\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	gu	Click in the document where you want to insert the cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150236				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select the caption category of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the caption number of the object that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150968				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, select the format of the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the caption category and caption text of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151115				0	gu	Updating Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153594				0	gu	To manually update the cross-references in a document, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153407				0	gu	\<variable id=\"even_odd_sdw\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/even_odd_sdw.xhp\" name=\"Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\"\>Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	gu	$[officename] can automatically apply alternating page styles on even (left) and odd pages (right) in your document. For example, you can use page styles to display different headers and footers on even and odd pages. The current page style is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the workplace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	gu	In the list of page styles, right-click "Left Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145267				0	gu	Select "Right Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	gu	In the list of page styles, right-click "Right Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	gu	Select "Left Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155561				0	gu	Go to the first page in your document, and double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155588				0	gu	To add a header to one of the page styles, choose\<emph\> Insert - Header\</emph\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the header to. In the header frame, type the text that you want to use as the header.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147772				0	gu	To add a footer to one of the page styles, choose\<emph\> Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the footer to. In the footer frame, type the text that you want to use as a footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\jump2statusbar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Going to Specific Bookmark				2002-02-02 02:02:02
