helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	gu	You can resize the width of table cells and columns, as well as change the height of table rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145109				0	gu	Changing the Width of Columns and Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149574				0	gu	To change the width of a column:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156246				0	gu	Rest the mouse pointer over the column dividing line until the pointer becomes a separator icon, and then drag the line to a new location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3145390				0	gu	Rest the mouse pointer over the column dividing line on the ruler until the pointer becomes a separator icon, and then drag the line to a new location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149993				0	gu	To change the width of a cell:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153014				0	gu	Changing the Height of a Row				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145819				0	gu	\<variable id=\"footnote_usage\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footnote_usage.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes\"\>Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	gu	Footnotes reference more information about a topic at the bottom of a page and endnotes reference information at the end of the document. $[officename] automatically numbers the footnotes and endnotes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155881				0	gu	To insert a footnote or endnote:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155903				0	gu	Click in your document where you want to place the anchor of the note.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147120				0	gu	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Footnote\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150704				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150729				0	gu	Type the note.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3148843				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3148857\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertfootnote.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148857\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3153176				0	gu	You can also insert footnotes by clicking the \<emph\>Insert Footnote Directly\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155543				0	gu	To insert a footnote or endnote:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150167				0	gu	The mouse pointer changes to a hand when you rest it over a footnote or endnote anchor in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155563				0	gu	To edit the text of a footnote or endnote, click in the note, or click the anchor for the note in the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145062				0	gu	To jump from the footnote or endnote text to the note anchor in the text, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>PageUp\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145081				0	gu	To edit the numbering properties of a footnote or endnote anchor, click in front of the anchor, and choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02150000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Footnote\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147776				0	gu	To change the formatting that $[officename] applies to footnotes and endnotes, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Footnotes\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Footnotes\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147813				0	gu	To edit the properties of the text area for footnotes or endnotes, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040600.xhp\" name=\"Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Footnote\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147232				0	gu	To remove a footnote, delete the footnote anchor in the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Adding Bullets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155186				0	gu	\<variable id=\"using_numbered_lists\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_numbered_lists.xhp\" name=\"Adding Bullets\"\>Adding Bullets\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	gu	Select the paragraph(s) that you want to add bullets to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3145403				0	gu	To remove bullets, select the bulleted paragraphs, and then click the \<emph\>Bullets On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3154416				0	gu	To change the formatting of bulleted list, choose \<emph\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Using AutoText				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155521				0	gu	\<variable id=\"autotext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autotext.xhp\" name=\"Using AutoText\"\>Using AutoText\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	gu	In $[officename] Writer, you can store text - also containing graphics, tables, and fields - as AutoText, so that you can quickly insert the text later on. If you want, you can also store formatted text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155539				0	gu	Inserting an AutoText Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155560				0	gu	Select the text, text with graphics, table, or field that you want to save as an AutoText entry. A graphic can only be stored if it is anchored as a character and is preceded and followed by at least one text character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147761				0	gu	Select the category where you want to store the AutoText.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147779				0	gu	Type a name that is longer than four characters. This allows you to use the \<emph\>Display remainder of name as suggestion while typing\</emph\> AutoText option. If you want, you can modify the proposed shortcut.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147807	60			0	gu	Click the \<emph\>AutoText\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_idN10732				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147282				0	gu	Inserting an AutoText Entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145597				0	gu	Click in your document where you want to insert an AutoText entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615				0	gu	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - AutoText\"\>\<emph\>Edit - AutoText\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145668	30			0	gu	You can also type the shortcut for an AutoText entry, and then press F3, or click the arrow next to the \<emph\>AutoText \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> bar, and then choose an AutoText entry. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155090	43			0	gu	To quickly enter a %PRODUCTNAME Math formula, type "FN", and then press F3. If you insert more than one formula, the formulae are sequentially numbered. To insert dummy text, type "DT", and then press F3. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155115				0	gu	To Print a List of AutoText Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155160				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> list, double-click "%PRODUCTNAME Macros - Gimmicks".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	gu	Select "AutoText" and then click \<emph\>Run\</emph\>. A list of the current AutoText entries is generated in a separate text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151304				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151327				0	gu	Using AutoText in Network Installations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151355				0	gu	You can store AutoText entries in different directories on a network.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	gu	For example, you can store "read-only" AutoText entries for your company on a central server, and user-defined AutoText entries in a local directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	gu	The paths for the AutoText directories can be edited in the configuration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154960				0	gu	Two directories are listed here. The first entry is on the server installation and the second entry is in the user directory. If there are two AutoText entries with the same name in both directories, the entry from the user directory is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154995				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - AutoText\"\>Edit - AutoText\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155012				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040600.xhp\" name=\"Word Completion\"\>Word Completion\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147692				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>pasting;results of formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas;pasting results in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147692				0	gu	\<variable id=\"calculate_clipboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_clipboard.xhp\" name=\" Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\"\> Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156366				0	gu	If your text already contains a formula, for example "12+24*2", $[officename] can calculate, and then paste the result of the formula in your document, without using the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	gu	Select the formula in the text. The formula can only contain numbers and operators and cannot contain spaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155496	38			0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Calculate\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Plus Sign (+).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id5172582				0	gu	Place the cursor where you want to insert the result of the formula, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting a Horizontal Line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151178				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>horizontal lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; inserting horizontal lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rulers;horizontal lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; horizontal lines\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151178				0	gu	\<variable id=\"insert_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_line.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Horizontal Line\"\>Inserting a Horizontal Line\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3149691				0	gu	Click in the document where you want to insert the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155186				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Horizontal Ruler\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	83			0	gu	Click the line that you want to insert in the \<emph\>Selection \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5267494				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150217				0	gu	The inserted line is anchored to the current paragraph and centered between the page margins.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150231				0	gu	You can also insert one of these lines by dragging it from the\<emph\> Rulers\</emph\> folder in the \<emph\>Gallery\</emph\> into the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150944				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/gallery.xhp\" name=\"Gallery\"\>Gallery\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Wrapping Text Around Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154486				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>text wrap around objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>contour editor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>contour wrap\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; formatting around objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; contour wrap\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects; contour wrap\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wrapping text;editing contours\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editors;contour editor\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154486				0	gu	\<variable id=\"wrap\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/wrap.xhp\" name=\"Wrapping Text Around Objects\"\>Wrapping Text Around Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Wrap\</emph\>, and then choose the wrapping style that you want to apply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155859				0	gu	The current wrapping style is indicated by a bullet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149834				0	gu	Specifying the Wrapping Properties				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060200.xhp\" name=\"Wrap\"\>\<emph\>Wrap\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153370				0	gu	Set the options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153386				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154247				0	gu	To change the wrapping contour of a graphic:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	gu	You can change the shape that the text wraps around.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	gu	Select the graphic, right-click, and then choose \<emph\>Wrap - Edit Contour\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060201.xhp\" name=\"Contour Editor\"\>Contour Editor\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Changing Page Backgrounds				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	gu	\<variable id=\"pagebackground\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp\"\>Changing Page Background\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10812				0	gu	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the background of the pages in a document. For example, to change the page background of one or more pages in a document to a watermark, you need to create a page style that uses the watermark background, and then apply the page style to the pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10820				0	gu	To Change the Page Background				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10827				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles \</emph\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	gu	In the list of page styles, right-click "Right Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083F				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1085F				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10867				0	gu	In the list box at the top, select whether you want a solid color or a graphic. Then select your options from the tab page. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1086B				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087A				0	gu	To Change the Page Background of All Pages in a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10892				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089A				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles \</emph\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	gu	Double-click the page style that uses the page background that you want to apply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	gu	To Use Different Page Backgrounds in the Same Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BD				0	gu	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph where you want to change the page background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C1				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	gu	If you want to change the page background later on in the document, repeat steps 1 to 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E8				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156377				0	gu	\<variable id=\"table_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Tables\"\>Inserting Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149489				0	gu	There are several ways to create a table in a text document. You can insert a table from a toolbar, through a menu command, or from a spreadsheet. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155908				0	gu	To insert a table from the Insert toolbar				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	gu	Place the cursor in your document where you want to insert the page count.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3147416				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153398				0	gu	In the table grid, drag to select the numbers of rows and columns that you want, and then release.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	gu	To cancel, drag to the other side until \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> appears in the preview area of the grid.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153135				0	gu	To insert a table with a menu command				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149642				0	gu	Place the cursor in your document where you want to insert the page count.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609	37			0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Table - Insert - Table\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149858				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Size\</emph\> area, enter the number of rows and columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145097				0	gu	Select the options that you want, click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149572				0	gu	Inserting a Table From a Calc Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154395				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154420				0	gu	In your text document, do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	gu	વિકલ્પો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154867				0	gu	Is inserted as...				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155893				0	gu	$[officename] $[officeversion] Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	gu	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+B.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148674				0	gu	GDIMetaFile				2002-02-02 02:02:02
