helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting Graphics From the Gallery With Drag-and-Drop				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145083				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; from Gallery into text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting from Gallery into text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;objects from Gallery\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145083				0	gu	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_gallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_gallery.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics From the Gallery With Drag-and-Drop\"\>Inserting Graphics From the Gallery With Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	gu	You can drag-and-drop an object from the gallery into a text document, spreadsheet, drawing, or presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155923				0	gu	To replace a gallery object that you inserted in a document, hold down Shift+Ctrl, and then drag a different gallery object onto the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Conditional Text for Page Counts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153108				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>page counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional text;page counts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153108				0	gu	\<variable id=\"conditional_text2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text2.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text for Page Counts\"\>Conditional Text for Page Counts\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156228				0	gu	You can create a conditional text field that displays the word "pages" instead of "page" in conjunction with a page count field if your document contains more than one page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	gu	Place the cursor in your document where you want to insert the page count.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Field - Page Count\</emph\>, and then enter a space.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	gu	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting a Scanned Image				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156017				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>inserting;scanned images\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; scanning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scanning pictures\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156017				0	gu	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_scan\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_scan.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Scanned Image\"\>Inserting a Scanned Image\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	gu	To insert a scanned image, the scanner must be connected to your system and the scanner software drivers must be installed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182	3			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>The scanner must support the TWAIN standard. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>The Scanner must support the SANE standard. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3155915				0	gu	Click in the document where you want to insert the scanned image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	gu	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Picture - Scan\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Picture - Scan\</emph\>\</link\>, and choose the scanning source from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	gu	Follow the scanning instructions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Modifying Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149291				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>references; modifying cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-references; modifying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149291				0	gu	\<variable id=\"references_modify\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/references_modify.xhp\" name=\"Modifying Cross-References\"\>Modifying Cross-References\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3153132				0	gu	Click in front of the cross-reference that you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3149632				0	gu	If you cannot see the field shading of the cross-reference, choose \<emph\>View - Field Shadings\</emph\> or press \<emph\>Ctrl+F8\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3145101				0	gu	Set the options that you want, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	gu	Use the arrow buttons in the \<emph\>Edit Fields \</emph\>dialog to browse through the cross-references in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
