helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Positioning Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147828				0	gu	\<variable id=\"anchor_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/anchor_object.xhp\" name=\"Positioning Objects\"\>Positioning Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3147251				0	gu	You can use anchors to position an object, graphic, or frame in a document. An anchored item remains in place, or moves when you modify the document. The following anchoring options are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145599				0	gu	એન્કરીંગ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145622				0	gu	અસર				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145650				0	gu	અક્ષરો તરીકે				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151181				0	gu	Anchors the selected item as a character in the current text. If the height of the selected item is greater than the current font size, the height of the line containing the item is increased.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	gu	To center an image on an HTML page, insert the image, anchor it "as character", then center the paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	gu	To character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151235				0	gu	Anchors the selected item to a character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155071				0	gu	ફકરાને				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155094				0	gu	Anchors the selected item to the current paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155122				0	gu	પાનાને				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155144				0	gu	Anchors the selected item to the current page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	gu	ચોકઠાને				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145697				0	gu	Anchors the selected item to the surrounding frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145715				0	gu	When you insert an object, graphic, or frame, an anchor icon appears where the item is anchored. You can position an anchored item by dragging the item to another location. To change the anchoring options of an item, right-click the item, and then choose an option from the \<emph\>Anchor \</emph\>submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145078				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>tab stops; inserting in lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering; changing the level of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;changing levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>levels;changing outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;changing levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lowering outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>raising outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;outline levels\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145078				0	gu	\<variable id=\"insert_tab_innumbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_tab_innumbering.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists\"\>Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155909				0	gu	To move a numbered or bulleted paragraph down one outline level, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155859				0	gu	To move a numbered or bulleted paragraph up one outline level, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press Shift+Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153403	8			0	gu	To insert a tab between the number or bullet and the paragraph text, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Changing the Default Template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155913				0	gu	\<variable id=\"template_default\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/template_default.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Default Template\"\>Changing the Default Template\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3145569				0	gu	The default template contains the default formatting information for new text documents. If you want, you can create a new template and use it as the default template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149838				0	gu	Create a document and the content and formatting styles that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	gu	In the \<emph\>New Template\</emph\> box, type a name for the new template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970				0	gu	Right-click the template that you created, and choose \<emph\>Set as Default Template\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	gu	Click\<emph\> Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149867				0	gu	To reset the default template:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3156245				0	gu	Click\<emph\> Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147407				0	gu	\<variable id=\"auto_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\"\>Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155525				0	gu	$[officename] can automatically apply numbering or bullets as you type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154243				0	gu	To Enable Automatic Numbering and Bulleting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152867				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoFormat\</emph\>, and ensure that \<emph\>While Typing\</emph\> is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id2357860				0	gu	The automatic numbering option is only applied to paragraphs that are formatted with the "Default", "Text body", or "Text body indent" paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152897				0	gu	To Create a Numbered or Bulleted List While You Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	gu	Type 1., i., or I. to start a numbered list. Type * or - to start a bulleted list. You can also type a right parenthesis after the number instead of a period , for example, 1) or i).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147794				0	gu	Enter a space, type your text, and then press Enter. The new paragraph automatically receives the next number or bullet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147814				0	gu	Press Enter again to finish the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	gu	You can start a numbered list with any number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154083				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Numbering/Bullets\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\number_sequence.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Defining Number Ranges				2002-02-02 02:02:02
