helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Printing a Brochure				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	bm_id6743064				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>printing; individual brochures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>booklet printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>brochures; printing individual\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F6				0	gu	\<variable id=\"print_brochure\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/print_brochure.xhp\"\>Printing a Brochure\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	gu	You can print a Writer document as a brochure or a booklet. That is, Writer prints two pages on each side of the paper, so that when you fold the paper, you can read the document as a book.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DE				0	gu	When you create a document that you want to print as a brochure, use portrait orientation for the pages. Writer applies the brochure layout when you print the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	gu	To Print a Brochure				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10621				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B6				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070E				0	gu	In the properties dialog for your printer, set the paper orientation to landscape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10740				0	gu	For a printer that automatically prints on both sides of a page, specify to print right pages and left pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10630				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EA				0	gu	If %PRODUCTNAME prints the pages in the wrong order, open the \<emph\>Printer Options\</emph\> dialog, select \<emph\>Reversed\</emph\>, and then print the document again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2632831				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4313791				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles \</emph\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Animating Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151182				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>text animation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>effects; text animation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animating text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151182				0	gu	\<variable id=\"text_animation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_animation.xhp\" name=\"Animating Text\"\>Animating Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080				0	gu	You can only animate text that is contained in a drawing object, such as rectangles, lines, or text objects. For example, draw a rectangle, then double-click the rectangle and enter your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	gu	Select the drawing object containing the text that you want to animate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	gu	Set the properties of the effect, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Selecting Tables, Rows, and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	bm_id7693411				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>selecting;tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows;selecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F0				0	gu	\<variable id=\"table_select\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_select.xhp\"\>Selecting Tables, Rows, and Columns\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060E				0	gu	You can select a table in a text document with a keyboard or with a mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	gu	To select a table with the keyboard, move the cursor into the table, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A until all the cells are selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10633				0	gu	To select a table with the mouse, move the mouse pointer to a position just above and left of the table. The mouse pointer becomes a diagonal arrow. Click to select the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	gu	To select a row or column with the mouse, point to a position just left of the row or above the column. The mouse pointer becomes an arrow. Click to select the row or column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Calculating Across Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154248				0	gu	\<variable id=\"calculate_multitable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_multitable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Across Tables\"\>Calculating Across Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	gu	You can perform calculations that span across more than one table in a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147795				0	gu	Open a text document, insert two tables, and type numbers in a few cells in both tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147815				0	gu	Place your cursor in an empty cell in one of the tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833				0	gu	Press F2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_multitable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	gu	Click in a cell containing a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
