helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154250				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>turning off automatic correction\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;turning off automatic correction\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>uppercase;changing to lowercase\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters after periods\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>quotation marks;changing automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>words;automatic replacement on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines;automatic drawing on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>underlining;quick\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; automatic drawing on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic changes on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changes;automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;turning off\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147812				0	gu	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Turning Off AutoFormat and AutoCorrect\"\>Turning Off AutoFormat and AutoCorrect\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833	2			0	gu	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	gu	To quickly undo an automatic correction or completion, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	gu	To turn off most AutoFormat features, remove the check mark from the menu \<emph\>Format - AutoFormat - While Typing\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147251				0	gu	To remove a word from the AutoCorrect list:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145620				0	gu	In the \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\> list, select the word pair that you want to remove.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145645				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145668				0	gu	To stop replacing quotation marks:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3151220				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155076				0	gu	To stop capitalizing the first letter of a sentence:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155123				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155148				0	gu	Clear the \<emph\>Capitalize first letter of every sentence\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155401				0	gu	To stop drawing a line when you type three identical characters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155415				0	gu	$[officename] automatically draws a line when you type three of the following characters and press Enter: - _ = * ~ #				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155463				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
