helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	gu	You can insert the current date as a field that updates each time you open the document, or as a field that does not update.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147679				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Document\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Querying User Data in Fields or Conditions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153398				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>fields; user data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user data; querying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditions; user data fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;text, from specific users\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; hiding from specific users, with conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user variables in conditions/fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153398				0	gu	\<variable id=\"fields_userdata\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields_userdata.xhp\" name=\"Querying User Data in Fields or Conditions\"\>Querying User Data in Fields or Conditions\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3154239				0	gu	You can access and compare some user data from conditions or fields. For example, you can compare user data with the following operators:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155889				0	gu	કારક				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	gu	== or EQ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3150531				0	gu	equals				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3150725				0	gu	!= or NEQ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3150748				0	gu	is not equal to				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3153167				0	gu	If you want, you can use a condition to hide specific text in your document from a specific user.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	gu	Select the text in the document that you want to hide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Record\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533	105			0	gu	In the \<emph\>With Condition\</emph\> box, type \<emph\>user_lastname == "Doe"\</emph\>, where "Doe" is the last name of the user that you want to hide the text from. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155573				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then save the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3147760				0	gu	The name of the hidden section can still be seen in the Navigator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
