helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3147344				0	gu	સ્થિતિ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3147392				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"List of operators\"\>List of operators\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Creating a Table of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147104				0	gu	\<variable id=\"indices_toc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_toc.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Table of Contents\"\>Creating a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	gu	The best way to generate a table of contents is to apply the predefined heading paragraph styles, such as "Heading 1", to the paragraphs that you want to include in your table of contents. After you apply these styles, you can then create a table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id5876949				0	gu	Updating a Table of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	gu	Click in your document where you want to create the table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120211.xhp\" name=\"Index/Table\"\>\<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153746				0	gu	Select "Table of Contents" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146856				0	gu	Set the options that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146872				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153148				0	gu	Updating a Table of Contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153183				0	gu	Right-click in the table of contents and choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147066				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - All Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Creating a Form Letter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159257				0	gu	\<variable id=\"form_letters\"\>\<variable id=\"form_letters_main\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/form_letters_main.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Form Letter\"\>Creating a Form Letter\</link\>\</variable\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3150502				0	gu	To create a form letter, you need a text document that contains fields for address data, and an address database. Then you combine or merge the address data and the text document to either print the letters or send them by e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10653				0	gu	The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/mailmerge00.xhp\"\>Mail Merge Wizard\</link\> helps you to create form letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10664				0	gu	To create a form letter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Mail Merge Wizard\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10672				0	gu	You see the Mail Merge Wizard dialog. The following is an example of one of many possible ways to navigate the wizard's pages:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10676				0	gu	Select \<emph\>Start from a template\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10685				0	gu	Select \<item type=\"literal\"\>Business Correspondence\</item\> in the left list, and then \<item type=\"literal\"\>Modern letter\</item\> in the right list. Click OK to close the Templates dialog, and click Next in the wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BD				0	gu	On the next step of the wizard, click the \<emph\>Select Address List\</emph\> button to check that you are using the correct address list. Select an address block type and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	gu	Next follows the \<emph\>Create a salutation\</emph\> step. Deselect the \<emph\>Insert personalized salutation\</emph\> box. Under \<emph\>General salutation\</emph\>, select the salutation that you want on top of all letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Saving Text Documents in HTML Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>text documents; publishing in HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; creating from text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>homepage creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;in HTML format\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	gu	\<variable id=\"send2html\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/send2html.xhp\" name=\"Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\"\>Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149825				0	gu	You can save a $[officename] Writer document in HTML format, so that you can view it in a web browser. If you want, you can associate a page break with a specific heading paragraph style to generate a separate HTML page each time the style appears in the document. $[officename] Writer automatically creates a page containing hyperlinks to each of these pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	gu	When you save a text document in HTML format, any graphics in the document are saved in JPEG format. The name of the HTML document is added as a prefix to the name of the graphic file. The JPEG images are saved in the same folder as the HTML document and are referenced with <IMG> tags in the HTML code.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155868				0	gu	Apply one of the default $[officename] heading paragraph styles, for example, "Heading 1", to the paragraphs where you want to generate a new HTML page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3156100				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create HTML Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Style \</emph\>box, select the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles, for example, "Heading 1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3153407				0	gu	Enter a path and a name for the HTML document, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Using Styles From Another Document or Template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145086				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>formatting styles; importing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; importing from other files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;styles from other files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading;styles from other files\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145086				0	gu	\<variable id=\"load_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/load_styles.xhp\" name=\"Using Styles From Another Document or Template\"\>Using Styles From Another Document or Template\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	gu	You can import styles from another document or template into the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3155910				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN10703				0	gu	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon to open the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070B				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Load styles\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149632				0	gu	Use the check boxes at the bottom of the dialog to select the style types that you want to import. To replace styles in the current document that have the same name as the ones you are importing, select \<emph\>Overwrite\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Using Shortcut Keys ($[officename] Writer Accessibility)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151169				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>keyboard; accessibility $[officename] Writer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] Writer\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151169				0	gu	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Using Shortcut Keys ($[officename] Writer Accessibility)\"\>Using Shortcut Keys ($[officename] Writer Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155186				0	gu	To open a context menu, press Shift+F10. To close a context menu, press Escape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Insert\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149630				0	gu	Press the right arrow key until the \<emph\>Section\</emph\> icon is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145100				0	gu	Press the down arrow key, and then press the right arrow key to set the width of the section that you want to insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154849				0	gu	Press the right arrow key until the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> icon is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	gu	Press the down arrow key, and then use the arrow keys to select the number of columns and rows to include in the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Using Master Documents and Subdocuments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145246				0	gu	\<variable id=\"globaldoc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/globaldoc.xhp\"\>Using Master Documents and Subdocuments\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149806				0	gu	A master document lets you manage large documents, such as a book with many chapters. The master document can be seen as a container for individual \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer files. The individual files are called subdocuments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150096				0	gu	When you print a master document, the contents of all subdocuments, indexes, and any text that you entered are printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153400				0	gu	You can create a table of contents and index in the master document for all of the subdocuments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155180				0	gu	When you add a document to a master document or create a new subdocument, a link is created in the master document. You cannot edit the content of a subdocument directly in the master document, but you can use the Navigator to open any subdocument for edit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Counting Words				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686				0	gu	\<variable id=\"words_count\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/words_count.xhp\" name=\"Counting Words\"\>Counting Words\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D1				0	gu	If you want to count only some text of your document, select the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3149821				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Word Count\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E2				0	gu	To get some more statistics about the document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties - Statistics\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3147418				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100400.xhp\" name=\"File - Properties - Statistics\"\>File - Properties - Statistics\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Conditional Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155619				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>matching conditional text in fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>if-then queries as fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional text; setting up\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; conditional text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;conditions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155619				0	gu	\<variable id=\"conditional_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text\"\>Conditional Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	gu	You can set up fields in your document that display text when a condition that you define is met. For example, you can define the conditional text that is displayed in a series of reminder letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	gu	Setting up conditional text in this example is a two-part process. First you create a variable, and then you create the condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153175				0	gu	To define a conditional variable:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153185	62			0	gu	The first part of the example is to define a variable for the condition statement. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645				0	gu	To define a condition and the conditional text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145659				0	gu	The second part of the example is to define the condition that must be met, and to insert a placeholder for displaying the conditional text in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193				0	gu	Place the cursor where you want to insert the conditional text in your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	gu	Type \<emph\>Reminder EQ "3"\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box. In other words, the conditional text will be displayed when the variable in the field that you defined in the first part of this example is equal to three.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155969				0	gu	The quotation marks enclosing the "3" indicate that the variable that you defined in the first part of this example is a text string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150446				0	gu	Type the text that you want to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box. There is almost no limit to the length of the text that you can enter. You can paste a paragraph into this box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150473				0	gu	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155073				0	gu	To display the conditional text:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155086				0	gu	In this example, the conditional text is displayed when the value of the conditional variable is equal to 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155110				0	gu	Place your cursor in front of the field that you defined in the first part of this example, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155168				0	gu	If the field does not automatically update, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145714				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"List of conditional operators\"\>List of conditional operators\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Rearranging a Document by Using the Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149973				0	gu	\<variable id=\"arrange_chapters\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/arrange_chapters.xhp\" name=\"Rearranging a Document by Using the Navigator\"\>Arranging Chapters in the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147795	59			0	gu	You can move headings and subordinate text up and down in a document text by using the Navigator. You can also promote and demote heading levels. To use this feature, format the headings in your document with one of the predefined heading paragraph styles. To use a custom paragraph style for a heading, choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>, select the style in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>box, and then double-click a number in the \<emph\>Levels \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145652	62			0	gu	To quickly move the text cursor to a heading in the document, double-click the heading in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155461				0	gu	To dock the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, drag the title bar to the edge of the workspace. To undock the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, double-click its frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151184				0	gu	To Move a Heading Up or Down in the Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151206	71			0	gu	On the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>, click the\<emph\> Navigator\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id5211883\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_navigator.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5211883\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151238	72			0	gu	On the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Content View \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id3156338\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20244.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156338\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	63			0	gu	Drag a heading to a new location in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155139	75			0	gu	Click a heading in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list, and then click the \<emph\>Promote Chapter\</emph\>\<image id=\"img_id4217546\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20174.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4217546\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or \<emph\>Demote Chapter \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id6505788\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20171.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6505788\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145758	64			0	gu	To move the heading without the subordinate text, hold down \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\> while you drag or click the \<emph\>Promote Chapter \</emph\>or \<emph\>Demote Chapter \</emph\>icons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155402				0	gu	To Promote or Demote the Level of a Heading				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155424	77			0	gu	Select the heading in the \<emph\>Navigator \</emph\>list. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081C				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Promote Level \</emph\>\<image id=\"img_id5564488\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20172.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5564488\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or \<emph\>Demote Level \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id3159363\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20173.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159363\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155525				0	gu	To Change the Number of Heading Levels That Are Displayed				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151352	79			0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Heading Levels Shown \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id3151310\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20236.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151310\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>, and then select a number from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147684				0	gu	\<variable id=\"captions_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\"\>Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147395				0	gu	You can include chapter numbers in captions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147408				0	gu	Ensure that the text in your document is organized by chapters, and that the chapter titles and, if you want, the section titles, use one of the predefined heading paragraph styles. You must also assign a numbering option to the heading paragraph styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Caption\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145567				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01041100.xhp\" name=\"Caption dialog\"\>AutoCaption dialog\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145574				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Chapter numbering\"\>Chapter numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Defining Different Headers and Footers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155920				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>headers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mirrored page layout\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155920				0	gu	\<variable id=\"header_pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Defining Different Headers and Footers\"\>Defining Different Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	gu	You can use different headers and footers on different pages in your document, so long as the pages use different page styles. $[officename] provides several predefined page styles, such as \<emph\>First page\</emph\>, \<emph\>Left page\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right page\</emph\>, or you can create a custom page style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	gu	For example, you can use page styles to define different headers for even and odd pages in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150929				0	gu	Open a new text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon in the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	gu	Right-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146889				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150714				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, right-click "Left Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147086				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	gu	Double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles to apply the style to the current page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145284	43			0	gu	Enter text or graphics in the header for the Left Page style. After the next page is added to your document, enter text or graphics in the header for the Right Page style. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	હાઈફનેશન				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	gu	\<variable id=\"using_hyphen\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_hyphen.xhp\" name=\"Hyphenation\"\>Hyphenation\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918	31			0	gu	By default, $[officename] moves words that do not fit on a line to the next line. If you want, you can use automatic or manual hyphenation to avoid this behavior: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155864				0	gu	Automatic hyphenation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147414				0	gu	Automatic hyphenation inserts hyphens where they are needed in a paragraph. This option is only available for paragraph styles and individual paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832				0	gu	To automatically hyphenate text in a paragraph:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148850				0	gu	Right-click in a paragraph, and choose \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104				0	gu	Click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>\<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153121				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149629				0	gu	To automatically hyphenate text in multiple paragraphs:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	gu	If you want to automatically hyphenate more than one paragraph, use a paragraph style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	gu	For example, enable the automatic hyphenation option for the "Default" paragraph style, and then apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to hyphenate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149867				0	gu	Right-click the paragraph style that you want to hyphenate, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Hyphenation\</emph\> area, select the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156250				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3145400				0	gu	Apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to hyphenate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145417				0	gu	Manual Hyphenation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154400				0	gu	You can insert a hyphen where you want on a line, or let $[officename] search for the words to hyphenate, and then offer a suggested hyphenation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	gu	To quickly insert a hyphen, click in the word where you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Hyphen(-).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154244				0	gu	If you insert a manual hyphen in a word, the word is only hyphenated at the manual hyphen. No additional automatic hyphenation is applied for this word. A word with a manual hyphen will be hyphenated without regard to the settings on the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154847				0	gu	To manually hyphenate text in a selection:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154869				0	gu	Select the text that you want to hyphenate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Language - Hyphenation\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting a Calc Chart into a Text Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152999				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>charts;copying from Calc into Writer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; charts from $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents;inserting Calc charts\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152999				0	gu	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_fromchart\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Calc Chart into a Text Document\"\>Inserting a Calc Chart into a Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3155890				0	gu	You can insert a copy of a chart that is not updated when you modify the chart data in the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3149054				0	gu	Open the text document that you want to copy the chart to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	gu	Open the spreadsheet containing the chart that you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	gu	In the spreadsheet, click the chart. Eight handles appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	gu	Drag the chart from the spreadsheet to the text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3145102				0	gu	You can resize and move the chart in the text document as you would any object. To edit the chart data, double-click the chart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149689				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; defining entries in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; defining entries in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entries; defining in indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149689				0	gu	\<variable id=\"indices_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_enter.xhp\" name=\"Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries\"\>Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156380				0	gu	Click in a word, or select the words in your document that you want to use as an index entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147409				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\>, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147119				0	gu	Defining Table of Contents Entries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150230				0	gu	To use a custom paragraph style as a table of contents entry:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150933				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Numbering\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150964				0	gu	Select the paragraph style that you want to include in your table of contents in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150523				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Level\</emph\> list, click the hierarchical level that you want to apply the paragraph style to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153730	17			0	gu	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You can now apply the style to headings in your document and include them in your table of contents. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
