helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	gu	You can combine numbered lists into a single consecutively numbered list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149452				0	gu	To combine consecutive numbered lists:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3154479				0	gu	Select all of the paragraphs in the lists.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155870				0	gu	To create a numbered list from non-consecutive paragraphs:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417				0	gu	Hold down Ctrl and drag a selection in the first numbered paragraph. You only have to select one character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	gu	Continue to hold down Ctrl, and drag a selection in each numbered paragraph of the lists you want to combine.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Adding Input Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155916				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>text; input fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields; input fields in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input fields in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;input fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;input fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916	1			0	gu	\<variable id=\"fields_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields_enter.xhp\" name=\"Adding Input Fields\"\>Adding Input Fields\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	gu	An input field is a variable that you can click in a document to open a dialog where you can edit the variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150708				0	gu	To quickly open all input fields in a document for editing, press Ctrl+Shift+F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Deleting Tables or the Contents of a Table				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149489				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>deleting; tables or table contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; deleting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149489				0	gu	\<variable id=\"table_delete\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_delete.xhp\" name=\"Deleting Tables or the Contents of a Table\"\>Deleting Tables or the Contents of a Table\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918				0	gu	You can delete a table from your document, or delete the contents of the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155863				0	gu	To delete a whole table, click in the table, and then choose \<emph\>Table - Delete - Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	gu	To delete the contents of a table, click in the table, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A until all cells are selected, and then press Delete or Backspace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152887				0	gu	\<variable id=\"autocorr_except\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autocorr_except.xhp\" name=\"Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\"\>Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3154254	11			0	gu	You can prevent AutoCorrect from correcting specific abbreviations or words that have mixed capital letters and lowercase letters. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147786	19			0	gu	Type the abbreviation followed by a period in the \<emph\>Abbreviations (no subsequent capital) \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812	20			0	gu	Type the word in the \<emph\>Words with TWo INitial CApitals \</emph\>box and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3144875	17			0	gu	To quickly undo an AutoCorrect replacement, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. This also adds the word or abbreviation that you typed to the AutoCorrect exceptions list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Adding Numbering				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147418				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>numbering;paragraphs, on and off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; numbering on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbered lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;numbering\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147418	15			0	gu	\<variable id=\"using_numbered_lists2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_numbered_lists2.xhp\" name=\"Adding Numbering\"\>Adding Numbering\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	gu	Select the paragraph(s) that you want to add numbering to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149968	24			0	gu	On the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar, click the \<emph\>Numbering On/Off\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3153125\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_defaultnumbering.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153125\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149573				0	gu	To change the formatting and the hierarchy of a numbered list, click in the list, and then open the \<emph\>Bullets and Numbering\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153365				0	gu	To remove numbering, select the numbered paragraphs, and then click the \<emph\>Numbering On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists2.xhp	0	help	par_id3154246				0	gu	To change the formatting of a numbered list, click in the list, then choose \<emph\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Moving and Copying Text in Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919				0	gu	\<variable id=\"dragdroptext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/dragdroptext.xhp\" name=\"Moving and Copying Text in Documents\"\>Moving and Copying Text in Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	gu	Select the text that you want to move or copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Using Master Documents and Subdocuments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id1522873				0	gu	A master document lets you manage large documents, such as a book with many chapters. The master document can be seen as a container for individual \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer files. The individual files are called subdocuments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	gu	To create a master document: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153382				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	gu	To create a master document: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	gu	Use the Navigator for rearranging and editing the subdocuments in a master document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	gu	To open a subdocument for editing, double-click the name of the subdocument in the Navigator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155931				0	gu	To remove a subdocument from the master document, right-click the subdocument in the Navigator list and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. The subdocument file is not deleted, only the entry in the Navigator is removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149982				0	gu	To reorder the subdocuments in a master document, drag a subdocument to a new location in the Navigator list. You can also select a subdocument in the list, and click the \<emph\>Move down\</emph\> or \<emph\>Move up \</emph\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153022				0	gu	To add an index, such as a table of contents, right-click in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3148959\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20246.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148959\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	gu	To update an index in a master document, select the index in the Navigator, and then click the \<emph\>Update\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C40				0	gu	When you insert an object like a frame or a picture into a master document, do not anchor the object "to page". Instead, set the anchor "to paragraph" on the \<emph\>Format - (Object type) - Type\</emph\> tab page, and then set the object's position relative to "Entire Page" in the \<emph\>Horizontal\</emph\> and \<emph\>Vertical\</emph\> list boxes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153656				0	gu	To start each subdocument on a new page:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	gu	Ensure that each subdocument starts with a heading that uses the same paragraph style, for example "Heading 1".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	gu	In the master document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153907				0	gu	Right-click "Heading 1" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	gu	If you want each subdocument to start on an odd page, select \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>, and select "Right page" in the box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145205				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228				0	gu	To export a master document as a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> text document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150315				0	gu	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Export\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148580				0	gu	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> list, select a text document file format and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	About Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145576				0	gu	\<variable id=\"fields\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"About Fields\"\>About Fields\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154246				0	gu	Fields are used for data that changes in a document, such as the current date or the total number of pages in a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154262				0	gu	Viewing Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3150509				0	gu	Fields consist of a field name and the field content. To switch the field display between the field name or the field content, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"View - Fields\"\>\<emph\>View - Field Names\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153166				0	gu	ક્ષેત્ર ગુણધર્મો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3153180				0	gu	Most field types in a document, including database fields, store and display variable values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	gu	The following field types execute an action when you click the field:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	gu	સત્ર પ્રકાર				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147760				0	gu	ગુણધર્મ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147789				0	gu	જગ્યા રાખનાર				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812				0	gu	Opens a dialog to insert the object for which the placeholder was set.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216				0	gu	સંદર્ભ ઉમેરો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239				0	gu	Moves the mouse pointer to the reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147267				0	gu	મેક્રો ચલાવો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147290				0	gu	Runs a macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145614				0	gu	ઈનપુટ કરવાનું ક્ષેત્ર				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637				0	gu	Opens a dialog to edit the contents of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3151244				0	gu	Placeholder, hidden text, insert reference, variable, database, and user-defined fields display a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field in a document. To enable this feature, ensure that the \<emph\>Extended Tips \</emph\>option is selected in the \<emph\>Help\</emph\> menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155937				0	gu	Updating Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155963				0	gu	To update all of the fields in a document, press F9, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Select All\</emph\>, and then press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155984				0	gu	To update a field that was inserted from a database, select the field, and then press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155845				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting with Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Navigator;inserting hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155845				0	gu	\<variable id=\"hyperlinks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyperlinks.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	gu	You can insert a cross-reference as a hyperlink in your document using the Navigator. You can even cross-reference items from other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> documents. If you click the hyperlink when the document is opened in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, you are taken to the cross-referenced item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833				0	gu	Open the document(s) containing the items you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	gu	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	gu	In the list at the bottom of the Navigator, select the document containing the item that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	gu	In the Navigator list, click the plus sign next to the item that you want to insert as a hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	gu	Drag the item to where you want to insert the hyperlink in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	gu	The name of the item is inserted in the document as an underlined hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Updating Styles From Selections				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155915				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>Stylist, see Styles and Formatting window\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Styles and Formatting window; updating from selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; styles, from selections\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155915				0	gu	\<variable id=\"stylist_update\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_update.xhp\" name=\"Updating Styles From Selections\"\>Updating Styles From Selections\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3149838				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3156107				0	gu	Click the icon of the style category that you want to update.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>New Styles from Selection\</emph\> from the submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155856				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>table mode selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>proportional distribution of tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative distribution of table cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard;modifying the behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155856				0	gu	\<variable id=\"tablemode\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/tablemode.xhp\" name=\"Modifying the Behavior of Rows and Columns for Table\"\>Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149835				0	gu	When you insert or delete cells, rows or columns in a table, the \<emph\>Behavior of rows/columns\</emph\> options determine how the neighboring elements are affected. For example, you can only insert new rows and columns into a table with \<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> row and column dimensions if space permits.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id7344279				0	gu	Note that these properties are valid only for changes to the column width that are made using the keyboard. Using the mouse, you are free to make any column width changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149638				0	gu	\<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> - changes only affect the adjacent cell, and not the entire table. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cell becomes narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149613				0	gu	\<emph\>Fixed, proportional\</emph\> - changes affect the entire table, and wide cells shrink more than narrow cells. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cells become proportionally narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149864				0	gu	\<emph\>Variable\</emph\> - changes affect the table size. For example, when you widen a cell, the width of the table increases.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting a Graphic From a File				2002-02-02 02:02:02
