helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Removing Line Breaks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155916				0	gu	\<variable id=\"removing_line_breaks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/removing_line_breaks.xhp\"\>Removing Line Breaks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	gu	Use the AutoFormat feature to remove line breaks that occur within sentences. Unwanted line breaks can occur when you copy text from another source and paste it into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153413	3			0	gu	This AutoFormat feature only works on text that is formatted with the "Default" paragraph style. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, ensure that \<emph\>Combine single line paragraphs if length greater than 50%\</emph\> is selected. To change the minimum percentage for the line length, double-click the option in the list, and then enter a new percentage.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	gu	Select the text containing the line breaks that you want to remove.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153388				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoFormat - Apply\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
