helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	gu	You can perform a calculation on cells in one table and display the result in a different table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	gu	Open a text document, insert a table with multiple columns and rows, and then insert another table consisting of one cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	gu	Enter numbers into some of the cells of the large table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155532				0	gu	Place the cursor in the table with the single cell, and then press F2.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577				0	gu	Click in a cell in the larger table that contains a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3147776				0	gu	If you want, you can format the table to behave as normal text. Insert the table into a frame, and then anchor the frame as a character. The frame remains anchored to the adjacent text when you insert or delete text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
