helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150769				0	gu	To apply a color to a user interface element, ensure that the checkbox in front of the name is marked. To hide a user interface element, clear the check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155430				0	gu	Some user interface elements cannot be hidden.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145365				0	gu	In order to enhance cursor visibility, if the user sets the application background color between 40% and 60% gray, it is automatically changed to 40% gray.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01012000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	gu	The \<emph\>Automatic\</emph\> color setting changes the user interface element to the preset color from the color scheme.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
