helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151054				0	gu	નવો શબ્દકોશ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Dictionary\</emph\> section you can name a new user-defined dictionary or dictionary of exceptions and specify the language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:ED_DICTNAME\"\>Specifies the name of the new custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> The file extension "*.DIC" is automatically appended.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	gu	ભાષાઓ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3148920				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SFXDLG_NEWDICT:LB_DICTLANG\"\>By selecting a certain language you can limit the use of the custom dictionary.\</ahelp\> By selecting \<emph\>All\</emph\> the custom dictionary is used independently of the current language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153106				0	gu	Exceptions (-)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SFXPAGE_LINGU_PB_LINGU_DICS_EDIT_DIC\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary\</emph\> dialog, in which you can add to your custom dictionary or edit existing entries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436	75			0	gu	In the \<emph\>Edit custom dictionary \</emph\>dialog you have the option to enter new terms or edit existing entries. If you edit an exception dictionary, the dialog has the added facility of defining an exception for a word. During the spellcheck this exception is then listed as a suggestion.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	76			0	gu	When a dictionary is edited, a check is made on the status of the file. If the file is write-protected, it cannot be changed. The buttons \<emph\>New\</emph\> and \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> are then deactivated. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150116				0	gu	ચોપડી				2002-02-02 02:02:02
