helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3160463				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AlignLeft\"\>Aligns the left edges of the selected objects. If only one object is selected in Draw or Impress, the left edge of the object is aligned to the left page margin.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150146				0	gu	Objects are aligned to the left edge of the leftmost object in the selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Font Effects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153514				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020200.xhp\" name=\"Font Effects\"\>Font Effects\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS\"\>Specify the font effects that you want to use.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146924				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_FONTCOLOR\"\>Sets the color for the selected text. If you select\<emph\> Automatic\</emph\>, the text color is set to black for light backgrounds and to white for dark backgrounds.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC2				0	gu	To change the color of a text selection, select the text that you want to change, and click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC9				0	gu	If you click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon before you select text, the paint can cursor appears. To change the color of text, select the text with the paint can cursor. To change the color of a single word, double-click in a word. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CD6				0	gu	To undo the last change, right-click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CDA				0	gu	To exit the paint can mode, click once, or press the Escape key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3144766				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FontColor\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>\<variable id=\"textfarbe\"\>Click to apply the current font color to the selected characters. You can also click here, and then drag a selection to change the text color. Click the arrow next to the icon to open the \<emph\>Font color \</emph\>toolbar. \</variable\>\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_EFFECTS2\"\>Select the font effects that you want to apply.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148944				0	gu	The following capitalization effects are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	gu	Without - no effect is applied				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154280				0	gu	Capitals - changes the selected lowercase characters to uppercase characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148947				0	gu	Lowercase - changes the selected uppercase characters to lower characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	gu	Title font - changes the first character of each selected word to an uppercase character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154937				0	gu	Small capitals - changes the selected lowercase characters to uppercase characters, and then reduces their size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
