helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154380				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>importing; HTML with META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; importing META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; META tags in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tags; META tags\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	gu	When you export a file to an HTML document, the description and the user-defined file properties are included as META \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tags\"\>tags\</link\> between the HEAD tags of the exported document. META tags are not displayed in a Web browser, and are used to include information, such as keywords for search engines on your Web page. To set the properties of the current document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> or \<emph\>User Defined\</emph\> tabs, and then type the information you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	gu	The following file properties are converted to META tags when you export a file as an HTML document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3154935				0	gu	File Property				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	gu	<TITLE>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	gu	<META NAME="CLASSIFICATION" CONTENT="Field Content">				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	gu	<META NAME="KEYWORDS" CONTENT="Field Content">				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	gu	Inscription				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	gu	<META NAME="DESCRIPTION" CONTENT="Field Content">				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	gu	Info fields 1...4				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3157892				0	gu	<META NAME="Info field name" CONTENT="Field Content">				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	22			0	gu	When you import an HTML containing these META tags, the contents of the tags are added to the corresponding $[officename] file property box. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163822				0	gu	Import Tips				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155307				0	gu	When you import an HTML document, following META tags are automatically converted to $[officename] fields: <META HTTP-EQUIV="REFRESH"...> and <META NAME="..." ...> , where NAME equals to AUTHOR, CREATED, CHANGED, CHANGEDBY, DESCRIPTION, KEYWORDS or CLASSIFICATION.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3146146				0	gu	Scripts, comments, and META tags that are positioned directly before a TABLE tag are inserted in the first cell of the table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	gu	Scripts and META tags in the header of an HTML document are imported and anchored to the first paragraph in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163717				0	gu	Export Tips				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159180				0	gu	Notes and script fields at the beginning of the first paragraph in a document are exported to the header of an HTML document. If the document begins with a table, the first paragraph in the first cell of the table is exported to the header of the HTML document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
