helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_IMAPDLG_POLY\"\>Draws a polygonal hotspot in the graphic. Click this icon, drag in the graphic, and then click to define one side of the polygon. Move to where you want to place the end of the next side, and then click. Repeat until you have drawn all of the sides of the polygon. When you are finished, double-click to close the polygon. After, you can enter the \<emph\>Address and the Text\</emph\> for the hotspot, and then select the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> where you want the URL to open.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148577				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3156005\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_polygon.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156005\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02220000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147046				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_IMAPDLG_FREEPOLY\"\>Draws a hotspot that is based on a freeform polygon. Click this icon and move to where you want to draw the hotspot. Drag a freeform line and release to close the shape. After, you can enter the \<emph\>Address and the Text\</emph\> for the hotspot, and then select the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> where you want the URL to open.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
