helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153884				0	gu	\<variable id=\"00000130\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000130.xhp\" name=\"Index - Keyword Search in the Help\"\>Index - Keyword Search in the Help\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_COMBOBOX_TP_HELP_INDEX_CB_INDEX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Double-click an entry or type the word you want to find in the index.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	par_id3148668				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_PUSHBUTTON_TP_HELP_INDEX_PB_OPEN_INDEX\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to display the selected topic.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	gu	You can search for a specific topic by typing a word into the \<emph\>Search term\</emph\> text box. The window contains an alphabetical list of index terms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	par_id3145669				0	gu	If the cursor is in the index list when you type the search term, the display will jump directly to the next match. When you type a word in the \<emph\>Search term\</emph\> text box, the focus will jump to the best match in the index list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000130.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	gu	The index and full-text searches always apply to the currently selected \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> application. Select the appropriate application using the list box on the help viewer's toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	The %PRODUCTNAME Help Window				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153884				0	gu	\<variable id=\"00000110\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000110.xhp\" name=\"The %PRODUCTNAME Help Window\"\>The \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Help Window\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3147143	2			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:HelpOnHelp\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Provides an overview of the Help system\</ahelp\>The Help window shows the currently selected Help page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOX\"\>The \<emph\>Toolbar\</emph\> contains important functions for controlling the Help system\</ahelp\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3147089				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_INDEX\"\>Hides and shows the \<emph\>navigation pane\</emph\>\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_BACKWARD\"\>Moves back to the \<emph\>previous\</emph\> page\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_FORWARD\"\>Moves forward to the \<emph\>next\</emph\> page\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_START\"\>Moves to the \<emph\>first page\</emph\> of the current Help topic\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_PRINT\"\>\<emph\>Prints\</emph\> the current page\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_BOOKMARKS\"\>Adds this page to your bookmarks\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FE				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TOOLBOXITEM_SEARCHDIALOG\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Find on this page\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	gu	These commands can also be found in the context menu of the Help document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10922				0	gu	Help Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10926				0	gu	You can copy from the Help Viewer to the clipboard on your operating system with standard copy commands. For example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092C				0	gu	On a Help page, select the text that you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10933				0	gu	To search the current Help page:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10939				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Find on this Page\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10940				0	gu	The \<emph\>Find on this Page\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A22				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter the text that you want to find.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A48				0	gu	Select the search options that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A59				0	gu	To find the next occurrence of the search term on the page, click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10906				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:ComboBox:RID_DLG_SEARCH:ED_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the text that you want to search for or select a text entry in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN10993				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:CheckBox:RID_DLG_SEARCH:CB_WHOLEWORDS\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Finds complete words only.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN109AA				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:CheckBox:RID_DLG_SEARCH:CB_MATCHCASE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distinguishes between uppercase text and lowercase text.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C1				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:CheckBox:RID_DLG_SEARCH:CB_WRAPAROUND\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Searches the entire Help page, starting at the current position of the cursor.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN109D8				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:CheckBox:RID_DLG_SEARCH:CB_BACKWARDS\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Searches backwards from the current position of the cursor.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_idN109F5				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"sfx2:PushButton:RID_DLG_SEARCH:PB_FIND\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Finds the next occurrence of the search term.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149202				0	gu	Navigation Pane				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TABCONTROL\"\>The navigation pane of the Help window contains the tab pages \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Index\</emph\>, \<emph\>Find\</emph\> and \<emph\>Bookmarks\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_LISTBOX\"\>The list box located at the very top is where you can select other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Help modules.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Index\</emph\> and \<emph\>Find\</emph\> tab pages only contain the data for the selected \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000160.xhp\" name=\"Contents\"\>Contents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000130.xhp\" name=\"Index\"\>Index\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000140.xhp\" name=\"Find\"\>Find\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154188				0	gu	Allows you to carry out a full-text search. The search will include the entire Help contents of the currently selected \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154985				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000150.xhp\" name=\"Bookmarks\"\>Bookmarks\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156062				0	gu	Contains user-defined bookmarks. You can edit or delete bookmarks, or click them to go to the corresponding pages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Getting Support				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146873				0	gu	\<variable id=\"00000001\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000001.xhp\" name=\"Getting Support\"\>Getting Support\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150667				0	gu	You can find help and support on the OpenOffice.org website at \<link href=\"http://www.openoffice.org\"\>www.openoffice.org\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230				0	gu	For a summary of the current support services refer to the \<emph\>Readme\</emph\> file in the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> folder.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Managing Bookmarks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153244				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>Help; bookmarks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bookmarks; Help\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154349				0	gu	\<variable id=\"doc_title\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000150.xhp\" name=\"Managing Bookmarks\"\>Managing Bookmarks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3154840				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_EDIT_DLG_HELP_ADDBOOKMARK_ED_BOOKMARK_TITLE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays the name of the bookmarked page. You can also type a new name for the bookmark.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3149140				0	gu	\<image src=\"sfx2/res/favourite.png\" id=\"img_id3149549\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149549\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3145314				0	gu	Use the \<emph\>Add to Bookmarks\</emph\> icon to set a bookmark for the current page shown in the Help.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	gu	You can find the bookmarks on the \<emph\>Bookmarks\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_LISTBOX_TP_HELP_BOOKMARKS_LB_BOOKMARKS\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Double-clicking a bookmark or pressing the Return key opens the assigned page in Help. A right-click opens the context menu.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	gu	Use the Del key to delete a selected bookmark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	gu	The following commands are on the context menu of a bookmark:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573				0	gu	\<emph\>Display\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_BOOKMARKS_OPEN\" visibility=\"visible\"\>displays the selected help subject\</ahelp\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	gu	\<emph\>Rename\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_BOOKMARKS_RENAME\" visibility=\"visible\"\>opens a dialog for entering another name for the bookmark\</ahelp\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000150.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	gu	\<emph\>Delete\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_BOOKMARKS_DELETE\" visibility=\"visible\"\>deletes the bookmark selected \</ahelp\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150618				0	gu	The \<emph\>$[officename] Help system\</emph\> provides easy access to information and support. There are several ways to find what you are looking for in the \<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000110.xhp\" name=\"Help environment\"\>Help environment\</link\>: You can search for a specific keyword in the \<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000130.xhp\" name=\"Index\"\>Index\</link\>, carry out a full-text search under \<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000140.xhp\" name=\"Find\"\>Find\</link\>, or look through a hierarchical list of the \<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000160.xhp\" name=\"Topics\"\>Topics\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Find - The Full-Text Search				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148532				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>Find tab in Help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help; full-text search\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>full-text search in Help\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148523				0	gu	\<variable id=\"00000140\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/05/00000140.xhp\" name=\"Find - The Full-Text Search\"\>Find - The Full-Text Search\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3155599				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_COMBOBOX_TP_HELP_SEARCH_ED_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the search term here. The search is not case-sensitive.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3153323				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_PUSHBUTTON_TP_HELP_SEARCH_PB_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to start a full-text search for the term you entered.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_HELP_SEARCH_CB_FULLWORDS\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to carry out an exact search for the word you entered. Incomplete words will not be found.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_CHECKBOX_TP_HELP_SEARCH_CB_SCOPE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether to only search in document headings for the search term.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SFX2_PUSHBUTTON_TP_HELP_SEARCH_PB_OPEN_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays the entry selected in the list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3152552				0	gu	The full text search function in $[officename] Help allows you to find Help documents that contain any combination of search terms. To do this, type one or more words into the \<emph\>Search term\</emph\> text field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	gu	The \<emph\>Search term\</emph\> text field stores the words you entered last. To repeat a previous search, click the arrow icon and select the term from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	gu	Use the check box \<emph\>Find in headings only\</emph\> to limit the search to document headings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3147210				0	gu	The \<emph\>Complete words only\</emph\> check box allows you to perform an exact search. If this box is marked, incomplete words will not be found. Do not mark this check box if the search term you enter should also be found as part of a longer word.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\05\00000140.xhp	0	help	par_id3149732				0	gu	The index and full-text searches always apply to the currently selected %PRODUCTNAME application. Select the appropriate application using the list box on the help viewer's toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	ભાત સ્થિતિ ચાલુ/બંધ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"Design Mode On/Off\"\>Design Mode On/Off\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SwitchControlDesignMode\"\>Toggles the Design mode on or off. This function is used to switch quickly between \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Design\"\>Design\</link\> and User mode. Activate to edit the form controls, deactivate to use the form controls.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153528				0	gu	Please note the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171000.xhp\" name=\"Open in Design Mode\"\>\<emph\>Open in Design Mode\</emph\>\</link\> function. If \<emph\>Open in Design Mode\</emph\> is activated, the document is always opened in Design mode, regardless of the state in which it is saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	gu	If your form is linked to a database and you turn off the Design mode, the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Bar\"\>Form Bar\</link\> is displayed at the lower margin of the document window. You can edit the link to the database in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	PDF તરીકે ડિરેક્ટરીની નિકાસ કરો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146946				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Export Directly as PDF\"\>Export Directly as PDF\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3085157				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ExportDirectToPDF\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Exports the current document directly as PDF. No settings dialog is shown.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152363				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Show Draw Functions\"\>Show Draw Functions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertDraw\"\>Click to open or close the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>bar, where you can add shapes, lines, text, and callouts to the current document.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10849				0	gu	You can switch on and off the Drawing toolbar of Writer and Calc documents using an icon on the Standard toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089D				0	gu	You can show and hide the \<emph\>Visible Buttons\</emph\>. Click the arrow at the end of the toolbar to access the \<emph\>Visible Buttons\</emph\> command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	gu	Lets you select objects in the current document. To select an object, click the object with the arrow. To select more than one object, drag a selection frame around the objects. To add an object to a selection, press Shift, and then click the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143270				0	gu	લીટી				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Line\"\>Draws a straight line where you drag in the current document. To constrain the line to 45 degrees, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	gu	To enter text on a line, double-click the line and type or paste your text. The text direction corresponds to the direction you dragged to draw the line. To hide the line, select \<emph\>Invisible\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Line Style\</emph\> box on the \<emph\>Drawing Object Properties\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152922				0	gu	લંબચોરસ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147230				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Rect\"\>Draws a rectangle where you drag in the current document. To draw a square, hold down Shift while you drag. Click where you want to place a corner of the rectangle, and drag to the size you want.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153367				0	gu	ઉપવલયલ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159197				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Ellipse\"\>Draws an oval where you drag in the current document. Click where you want to draw the oval, and drag to the size you want. To draw a circle, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155308				0	gu	બહુકોણ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147214				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Polygon_Unfilled\"\>Draws a line composed of a series of straight line segments. Drag to draw a line segment, click to define the endpoint of the line segment, and then drag to draw a new line segment. Double-click to finish drawing the line. To create a closed shape, double-click the starting point of the line.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638				0	gu	Hold the Shift key while drawing a polygon to position new points at 45 degree angles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	gu	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05270000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points\"\>Edit Points\</link\> mode enables you to interactively modify the individual points of the polygon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153279				0	gu	વળાંક				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148878	57			0	gu	\<variable id=\"kurvetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bezier_Unfilled\"\>Draws a smooth Bezier curve. Click where you want the curve to start, drag, release, and then move the pointer to where you want the curve to end and click. Move the pointer and click again to add a straight line segment to the curve. Double-click to finish drawing the curve. To create a closed shape, double click the starting point of the curve.\</ahelp\> The arc of the curve is determined by the distance you drag. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148587				0	gu	મુક્ત રીતે રચાયેલી રેખા				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154163				0	gu	\<variable id=\"freihandtext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Freeline_Unfilled\"\>Draws a freeform line where you drag in the current document. To end the line, release the mouse button. To draw a closed shape, release the mouse button near the starting point of the line.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147259				0	gu	ચાપ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148482				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Arc\"\>Draws an arc in the current document. To draw an arc, drag an oval to the size you want, and then click to define the starting point of the arc. Move your pointer to where you want to place the endpoint and click. You do not need to click on the oval. To draw an arc that is based on a circle, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153924				0	gu	ઉપવલય ચાપ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156383				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Pie\"\>Draws a filled shape that is defined by the arc of an oval and two radius lines in the current document. To draw an ellipse pie, drag an oval to the size you want, and then click to define the first radius line. Move your pointer to where you want to place the second radius line and click. You do not need to click on the oval. To draw a circle pie, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154964				0	gu	વૃત્તખંડ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149106				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CircleCut\"\>Draws a filled shape that is defined by the arc of a circle and a diameter line in the current document. To draw a circle segment, drag a circle to the size you want, and then click to define the starting point of the diameter line. Move your pointer to where you want to place the endpoint of the diameter line and click. You do not need to click on the circle. To draw an ellipse segment, hold down Shift while you drag.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145150				0	gu	લખાણ:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158214				0	gu	લખાણ એનીમેશન				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826	63			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Text_Marquee\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts animated text with horizontal text direction into the current document. Drag a text box, and then type or paste your text. To assign an animation effect, choose \<emph\>Format - Text - Text Animation\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>\<variable id=\"lauftext\"\>Inserts animated text with horizontal text direction into the current document. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151274				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DrawCaption\"\>Draws a line that ends in a rectangular callout with horizontal text direction from where you drag in the current document. Drag a handle of the callout to resize the callout. To add text, click the edge of the callout, and then type or paste your text. To change a rectangular callout to a rounded callout, drag the largest corner handle when the pointer changes to a hand.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E50				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05270000.xhp\" name=\"Points\"\>Points\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E60				0	gu	Enables you to edit points on your drawing.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E75				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04140000.xhp\" name=\"From File\"\>From File\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E95				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/3dsettings_toolbar.xhp\"\>Extrusion On/Off\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10EA5				0	gu	Switches the 3D effects on and off for the selected objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149735				0	gu	ઊભા કોલઆઉટ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166437				0	gu	ઊભું લખાણ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01140000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_graphic_drawit.xhp\" name=\"Tips\"\>Tips for working with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>bar.\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	URL લાવો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149119				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/07010000.xhp\" name=\"Load URL\"\>Load URL\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	તારીખ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150040				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>forms; data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; forms and subforms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; subforms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subforms; description\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>Data\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242	2			0	gu	The\<emph\> Data \</emph\>tab page defines the form properties that refer to the database that is linked to the form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	gu	Defines the data source on which the form is based, or specifies whether the data can be edited by the user. Apart from the sort and filter functions, you will also find all the necessary properties to create a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154810				0	gu	માહિતી સ્રોતો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATASOURCE\"\>Defines the data source to which the form should refer.\</ahelp\> If you click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button, you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, where you can choose a data source.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146948				0	gu	વિગત				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURSORSOURCE\"\>Determines the content to be used for the form. The content can be an existing table or a query (previously created in the database), or it can be defined by an SQL-statement. Before you enter a content you have to define the exact type in \<emph\>Content type\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149657				0	gu	If you have selected either "Table" or "Query" in \<emph\>Content type\</emph\>, the box lists all the tables and queries set up in the selected database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148755				0	gu	સમાવિષ્ટ પ્રકાર				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURSORSOURCETYPE\"\>Defines whether the data source is to be an existing database table or query, or if the form is to be generated based on an SQL statement.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	gu	If you choose "Table" or "Query", the form will refer to the table or query that you specify under \<emph\>Content\</emph\>. If you want to create a new query or a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>, then you have to choose the "SQL" option. You can then enter the statement for the SQL query or the subform directly in the \<emph\>List content\</emph\> box on the Control properties Data tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158409				0	gu	SQL આદેશનું પૃથક્કરણ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ESCAPE_PROCESSING\"\>Specifies whether the SQL statement is to be analyzed by %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\> If set to Yes, you can click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button next to the \<emph\>Content\</emph\> list box. This will open a window where you can graphically create a database query. When you close that window, the SQL statement for the created query will be inserted to the \<emph\>Content\</emph\> list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156005				0	gu	ક્રમમાં ગોઠવો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3163712				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SORT_CRITERIA\"\>Specifies the conditions to sort the data in the form. The specification of the sorting conditions follows SQL rules without the use of the ORDER BY clause.\</ahelp\> For example, if you want all records of a database to be sorted in one field in an ascending order and in another field in a descending order, enter Forename ASC, Name DESC (presuming Forename and Name are the names of the data fields).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148616				0	gu	ફ્કત માહિતી ઉમેરો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153139				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATAENTRY\"\>Determines if the form only allows the addition of new data (Yes) or if it allows other properties as well (No).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	gu	If \<emph\>Add data only\</emph\> is set to "Yes", changing or deleting data is not possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157976				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAVIGATION\"\>Specifies whether the navigation functions in the lower form bar can be used.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	gu	The "Parent Form" option is used for subforms. If you choose this option for a subform you can navigate using the records of the main form if the cursor is placed in the subform. A subform is linked to the parent form by a 1:1 relationship, so navigation is always performed in the parent form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151051				0	gu	ચક્ર				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CYCLE\"\>Determines how the navigation should be done using the tab key.\</ahelp\> Using the tab key, you can move forward in the form. If you simultaneously press the Shift key, the navigation will follow the opposite direction. If you reach the last (or the first) field and press the tab key again, it can have various effects. Define the key control with the following options:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	gu	વિકલ્પ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157847				0	gu	This setting automatically defines a cycle which follows an existing database link: If the form contains a database link, the Tab key will, by default, initiate a change to the next or previous record on exit from the last field (see All Records). If there is no database link the next/previous form is shown (see Current Page).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	gu	All records				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3152972				0	gu	This option applies to database forms only and is used to navigate through all records. If you use the Tab key to exit from the last field of a form, the current record is changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020				0	gu	Active record				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3145301				0	gu	This option applies to database forms only, and is used to navigate within the current record. If you use the Tab key to exit from the last field of a form, the current record is changed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3146913				0	gu	Current page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150330				0	gu	On exit from the last field of a form, the cursor skips to the first field in the next form. This is standard for HTML forms; therefore, this option is especially relevant for HTML forms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155064				0	gu	વધારો માન્ય				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_ADDITIONS\"\>Determines if data can be added.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156054				0	gu	બદલવાનું માન્ય				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156377				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_EDITS\"\> Determines if the data can be modified.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149019				0	gu	Allow deletions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148995				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_DELETIONS\"\>Determines if the data can be deleted.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153714				0	gu	મુખ્ય ક્ષેત્રો ઉમેરો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_MASTERFIELDS\"\>If you create a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>, enter the data field of the parent form responsible for the synchronization between parent and subform.\</ahelp\> To enter multiple values, press Shift + Enter after each input line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	gu	The subform is based on an \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#sql\" name=\"SQL\"\>SQL\</link\> query; more specifically, on a \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Parameter Query\"\>Parameter Query\</link\>. If a field name is entered in the \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> box, the data contained in that field in the main form is read to a variable that you must enter in \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\>. In an appropriate SQL statement, this variable is compared to the table data that the subform refers to. Alternatively, you can enter the column name in the \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156089				0	gu	Consider the following example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017				0	gu	The database table on which the form is based is, for example, a customer database ("Customer"), where every customer has been given a unique number in a data field named "Cust_ID". A customer's orders are maintained in another database table. You now want to see each customer's orders after entering them into the form. In order to do this you should create a subform. Under \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> enter the data field from the customer database which clearly identifies the customer, that is, Cust_ID. Under \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\> enter the name of a variable which is to accept the data of the field Cust_ID, for example, x.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248				0	gu	The subform should show the appropriate data from the orders table ("Orders") for each customer ID (Customer_ID -> x). This is only possible if each order is uniquely assigned to one customer in the orders table. Alternatively, you can use another field called Customer_ID; however, to make sure that this field is not confused with the same field from the main form, the field is called Customer_Number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153537				0	gu	Now compare the Customer_Number in the "Orders" table with the Customer_ID from the "Customers" table, which can be done, for example, using the x variable with the following SQL statement:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	gu	SELECT * FROM Orders WHERE Customer_Number =: x (if you want the subform to show all data from the orders table)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3163727				0	gu	or:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153921				0	gu	SELECT Item FROM Orders WHERE Customer_Number =: x (if you want the subform from the orders table to show only the data contained in the "Item" field)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	gu	The SQL statement can either be entered in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> field, or you can create an appropriate parameter query, which can be used to create the subform.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150648				0	gu	ગૌણ ક્ષેત્રો ઉમેરો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149923				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SLAVEFIELDS\"\>If you create a subform, enter the variable where possible values from the parent form field can be stored.\</ahelp\> If a subform is based on a query, enter the variable that you defined in the query. If you create a form using an SQL statement entered in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> field, enter the variable you used in the statement. You can choose any variable name. If you want to enter multiple values, press Shift + Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114				0	gu	If, for example, you specified the Customer_ID database field as a parent field under \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\>, then you can define under \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\> the name of the variable in which the values of the Customer_ID database field are to be stored. If you now specify an SQL statement in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> box using this variable, the relevant values are displayed in the subform.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152778				0	gu	What is a subform?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155579				0	gu	Forms are created based on a database table or database query. They display the data in a visually pleasant fashion and can be used to enter data or edit data.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147094	34			0	gu	\<variable id=\"wozu\"\>If you require a form that can refer to the data in a table or query and can additionally display data from another table, you should create a subform. \</variable\> For example, this subform can be a text box that displays the data of another database table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157972				0	gu	A subform is an additional component of the main form. The main form can be called the "parent form" or "master". Subforms are needed as soon as you want to access more than one table from a form. Each additional table requires its own subform.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id4807275				0	gu	After creating a form, it can be changed into a subform. To do this, enter Design Mode, and open the Form Navigator. In the Form Navigator, drag a form (that will become a subform) onto any other form (that will become a master).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	gu	The user of your document will not see that a form has subforms. The user only sees a document in which data is entered or where existing data is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C2A				0	gu	Specify the Link master field from the data fields in the master form. In the subform, the Link slave field can be set as a field which will be matched to the contents of the Link master field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C2D				0	gu	When the user navigates through the data, the form always displays the current data record. If there are subforms defined, the contents of the subforms will be displayed after a short delay of approximate 200 ms. This delay enables you to quickly browse through the data records of the master form. If you navigate to the next master data record within the delay limit, the subform data need not be retrieved and displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SbaBrwInsert\"\>\<variable id=\"datenintext\"\>Inserts all fields of the marked record into the current document at the cursor position.\</variable\>\</ahelp\> The icon is only visible if the current document is a text document or a spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154186				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3147291\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbabrwinsert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147291\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	gu	Data to Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577	4			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>In the data source browser, select the record that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon. The record is inserted in the document at the cursor position, with the contents of each individual field of the record copied to a table column. You can also select multiple records and transfer them into the document by clicking the \<emph\>Data to Text \</emph\>icon. Each individual record is then written to a new row.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	5			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In the data source browser, select the records that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon, or drag-and-drop data from the data source browser into the document. This opens the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog. Select whether the data should be inserted as a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070100.xhp\" name=\"table\"\>table\</link\>, as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070200.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> or as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070300.xhp\" name=\"text\"\>text\</link\>.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	6			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The preferences you set in the\<emph\> Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog are saved and will be active the next time the dialog is called. This save process is independent of the database and can record the preferences for a maximum of 5 databases.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326				0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If data is inserted into the document as a table, the table properties are not saved along with the data in the document. If you select the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> function for formatting the table, $[officename] will note the name of the format template. This template will then be used automatically if you insert data as a table again, unless the preferences have been changed.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoFilter\"\>Filters the records based on the content of the currently selected data field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151234				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3147261\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfiltered.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147261\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155355				0	gu	Place the cursor in a field name whose content you want to filter and then click the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> icon. Only those records with content identical to the selected field name are visible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159234				0	gu	For example, to view all the customers from New York, click a field name with the entry "New York". AutoFilter then filters all customers from New York from the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577				0	gu	You can remove the current AutoFilter with the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sorting\"\>Remove Filter/Sorting\</link\> icon or with \<emph\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	7			0	gu	To filter with several field names simultaneously, click the \<emph\>Default Filter \</emph\>icon. The \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12090000.xhp\" name=\"Default Filter dialog\"\>Default Filter\</link\> dialog appears, in which you can combine several filter criteria.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147285				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DecrementLevel\"\>Moves the selected paragraph down one level in a numbering or bullets hierarchy.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3143267\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_outlineright.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3143267\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149096	3			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\> \<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>To Document Begin\</caseinline\> \<defaultinline\>First Page\</defaultinline\> \</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Combo Box/List Box Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159233				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>forms; Combo Box/List Box Wizard\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154094				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box/List Box Wizard\"\>Combo Box/List Box Wizard\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	gu	If you insert a combo box or a list box in a document, a wizard starts automatically. This wizard allows you to interactively specify which information is shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391				0	gu	The wizards for combo boxes and list boxes differ from each other in their final step. This is because the nature of control fields:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	gu	\<emph\>List Boxes\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	gu	In the case of a list box, the user selects one entry from a list of entries. These entries are saved in a database table and cannot be modified through the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	gu	As a general rule, the database table that contains the visible list entries in the form is not the table on which the form is based. The list boxes in a form work by using references; that is, references to the visible list entries are located in the form table (values table) and are also entered as such in the values table if the user selects an entry from the list and saves it. Through reference values, list boxes can display data from a table linked to the current form table. Thus the \<emph\>List Box Wizard\</emph\> allows two tables of a database to be linked, so that the control field can display a detailed list of a database field that is located in a different table from the one to which the form refers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	gu	In the other tables the required field is searched for by using the field names (ControlSource) and then the fields will be completed accordingly. If the field name is not found, the list will remain empty. When list fields contain linked columns, the first column of the other table will be used without a query being shown first.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	gu	If an article table contains, for example, the number of a supplier, the list box can use the "Supplier number" link to display the name of the supplier from the supplier table. On the \<emph\>Field links\</emph\> page the Wizard will ask you about all the settings required for this link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150977				0	gu	\<emph\>Combo Boxes\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	gu	In the case of combo boxes, users can select one entry from the list entries or enter text themselves. The entries, which are offered as a list from which users can select, may originate from any database table. The entries that users select or enter so that they can be saved can be saved either in the form only, or in a database. If they are saved in a database, they will be written to the database table on which the form is based.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	gu	Combo boxes can display the data of any table. A direct link between the current form table and the table whose values are to be displayed in the combo box (list table) is not required. Combo boxes do not work with references. If the user enters or selects a value and saves it, the value actually displayed will be entered in the form table. As there is no link between the form table and the list table, the \<emph\>Field Link\</emph\> table does not appear here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	gu	In the case of a list box, you select entries from the list, and these are saved in the list table. In the case of a combo box, you can add additional text that can be written to the current database table of the form (values table) and stored there as desired. For this function, the \<emph\>Combo Box Wizard\</emph\> has the \<emph\>Data Processing\</emph\> page as the last page, whereas in the case of list boxes this page does not exist. Here you can enter whether and where text that has been entered is to be saved in the values table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>formatted fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	127			0	gu	\<emph\>Formatting\</emph\>: You can set the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>property by clicking the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button in the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> line of the \<emph\>Properties: Formatted Field\</emph\> dialog. The \<emph\>Number Format\</emph\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	gu	If the formatted field is connected to the text field of a database, the entries in this field will be treated as text. If the formatted field is connected to a field of the database that can be displayed as a number, the input is treated as numbers. The date and time are also handled internally as numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150976	129			0	gu	\<emph\>Min. value\</emph\> and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>: You can enter the minimum and maximum numeric value for a formatted field. The min and max values determine the output of existing data (Example: Min. value is 5, the connected database field contains the integer value 3. The output is 5, but the value in the database is not modified) and the input of new data (Example: Max. value is 10 and you enter 20. The input is corrected and 10 is written in the database). If the fields are not filled in for \<emph\>Min. value \</emph\>and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>, no limits will be applied. For formatted fields that are connected to a database text field, these two values and the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> do not apply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	gu	\<emph\>Default value\</emph\>: This value is set for new records as the default value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\05090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154863				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/05090000.xhp\" name=\"Rotate\"\>Rotate\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\05090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149119				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleObjectRotateMode\"\>Rotates the selected object.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\05090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716	5			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>Select an object and click the\<emph\> Rotate\</emph\> icon on the\<emph\> Drawing\</emph\> toolbar. \</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>Select an object and click the Rotate icon on the Drawing toolbar. \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Select an object and click the\<emph\> Rotate\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing Object Properties\</emph\> toolbar.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> Drag a corner handle of the object in the direction you want to rotate it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
