helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Table Element Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150620				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170800.xhp\" name=\"Table Element Wizard\"\>Table Element Wizard\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170800.xhp	0	help	par_id3155354				0	gu	If you insert a table control in a document, the \<emph\>Table Element Wizard\</emph\> starts automatically. In this wizard, you can interactively specify which information is displayed in the table control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156183				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>database contents; inserting as tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156183	18			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_AS_TABLE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts data selected from the data source browser into the document as a table.\</ahelp\>In the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> option to insert the selected data into the document as a table. In the dialog, you can decide which database fields or columns are transferred, and how the text table is formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152918				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> area, use the arrow keys to select the columns of the database table that you want to apply to the text table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425	20			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_TBL_DB_COLUMN\"\>Specifies the database columns to be inserted into the text table.\</ahelp\> All database table columns that have not been accepted in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box are listed here. The entries are sorted alphabetically. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147577				0	gu	Table column(s)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_TABLE_COL\"\>Lists all database columns to be inserted into the document.\</ahelp\> A column will be assigned to each corresponding entry in the table. The entry order in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box determines the data order in the text table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146958				0	gu	>>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149750				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_ALL_TO\"\>Moves all listed database fields into the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box.\</ahelp\> All fields listed in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box are inserted into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153662	23			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_ONE_TO\"\>Moves the selected database field into the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box. \</ahelp\> You can also double click an entry to move it to the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box. All fields listed in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box are inserted into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149732				0	gu	<				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685	24			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_IMAGEBUTTON_DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL_IB_DBCOL_ONE_FROM\"\>Removes the selected database field from the\<emph\> Table column(s)\</emph\> list box\</ahelp\> The removed field is not inserted into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771				0	gu	<<				2002-02-02 02:02:02
