helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150476				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_OFA_HYPERLINK_NAME\"\>Assigns a name to an Internet URL or file.\</ahelp\> You can also enter search criteria for an Internet search site.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	gu	Possible search syntax is as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154673				0	gu	"Suite+Office"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148548				0	gu	Finds all pages that contain the words "Suite" AND "Office" at any position.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805				0	gu	"Suite,Office"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	gu	Finds all pages that contain "Suite" OR "Office".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	gu	Suite Office				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153346				0	gu	Finds all pages that contain the specified text. Search text without quotation marks will be sent directly to the specified search engine in the Internet. In most cases, a search engine combines a string of words with "OR," and finds pages in which at least one of the words appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	gu	Not all Internet \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#suchmaschine\" name=\"search engines\"\>search engines\</link\> support all logical combinations. It is recommended to use only one of the three options for linking search terms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/09050000.xhp\" name=\"Find\"\>Find\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
