helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154142				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Form Controls\"\>Form Controls\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151378				0	gu	\<variable id=\"formulartext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Config\"\>The Form Controls icon opens a toolbar with the tools that you need to create an interactive form.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can use the toolbar to add controls to a form in a text, spreadsheet, presentation, or HTML document, for example a button that runs a macro.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B21				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xforms.xhp\"\>XML Form documents\</link\> (XForms) use the same controls.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C39				0	gu	To add a control to a document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154918				0	gu	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the icon of the control that you want to add.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C4D				0	gu	In the document, drag to create the control. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C87				0	gu	Modifying a Control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	gu	Right-click the control and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>. A dialog opens where you can define the properties of the control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	gu	To specify a accelerator key for a control, add a tilde (~) in front of the character in the label for the control.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152792	135			0	gu	You can drag and drop controls from one document to another document. You can also copy and paste controls between documents. When you insert a control from another document, $[officename] analyzes the data source, content type, and content properties of the control so that the control fits the logical structure in the target document. For example, a control that displays contents from an address book continues to display the same contents after you copy the control to a different document. You can view these properties on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page of the \<emph\>Form properties\</emph\> dialog. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150470				0	gu	This icon switches the mouse pointer to the select mode, or deactivates this mode. The select mode is used to select the controls of the current form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153927				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CheckBox\"\>Creates a check box.\</ahelp\> Check boxes allow you to activate or deactivate a function in a form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153794				0	gu	લખાણ પેટી				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Edit\"\>Creates a text box.\</ahelp\> Text boxes are fields in which the user can enter text. In a form, text boxes display data or allow for new data input.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147547				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormattedField\"\>Creates a formatted field.\</ahelp\> A formatted field is a text box in which you can define how the inputs and outputs are formatted, and which limiting values apply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155346				0	gu	A formatted field has \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170002.xhp\" name=\"special control properties\"\>special control properties\</link\> (choose \<emph\>Format - Control\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148774				0	gu	દબાય તેવું બટન				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147046				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Pushbutton\"\>Creates a push button.\</ahelp\> This function can be used to execute a command for a defined event, such as a mouse click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	gu	You can apply text and graphics to these buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157844				0	gu	વિકલ્પ બટન				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RadioButton\"\>Creates an option button.\</ahelp\> Option buttons enable the user to choose one of several options. Option buttons with the same functionality are given the same name (\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"Name\"\>\<emph\>Name\</emph\>\</link\>\<emph\>property\</emph\>). Normally, they are given a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"group box\"\>group box\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ListBox\"\>Creates a list box.\</ahelp\> A list box lets users select an entry from a list. If the form is linked to a database and the database connection is active, the\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"List Box Wizard\"\>\<emph\>List Box Wizard\</emph\>\</link\> will automatically appear after the list box is inserted in the document. This wizard helps you create the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149407				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ComboBox\"\>Creates a combo box.\</ahelp\> A combo box is a single-line list box with a drop-down list from which users choose an option. You can assign the "read-only" property to the combo box so that users cannot enter other entries than those found in the list. If the form is bound to a database and the database connection is active, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box Wizard\"\>\<emph\>Combo Box Wizard\</emph\>\</link\> will automatically appear after you insert the combo box in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145618				0	gu	લેબલ ક્ષેત્ર				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Label\"\>Creates a field for displaying text.\</ahelp\> These labels are only for displaying predefined text. Entries cannot be made in these fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CF7				0	gu	Form Design				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B76				0	gu	Turns on and turns off the automatic form controls wizards.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id6403088				0	gu	These wizards help you to enter the properties of list boxes, table controls, and other controls.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149436				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170001.xhp\" name=\"Context Menu Commands\"\>Context Menu Commands\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11A56				0	gu	વિકલ્પ બટન				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11A75				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SpinButton\"\>Creates a spin button.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id710776				0	gu	If you add a spin button to a Calc spreadsheet, you can use the Data tab page to create a two-way link between the spin button and a cell. As a result, when you change the contents of a cell, the contents of the spin button are updated. Conversely, if you change the value of the spin button, the contents of the cell are updated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11ADB				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ScrollBar\"\>Creates a scrollbar.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CA3				0	gu	You can specify the following properties for a scrollbar:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CDA				0	gu	UI name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CE0				0	gu	Semantics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CE7				0	gu	Scroll value min				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CED				0	gu	Specifies the minimum height or the minimum width of a scrollbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CF4				0	gu	Scroll value max				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11CFA				0	gu	Specifies the maximum height or the maximum width of a scrollbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D07				0	gu	Specifies the default value of a scrollbar, used when the form is reset.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D14				0	gu	Specifies the orientation of a scrollbar, that is, horizontal or vertical.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D21				0	gu	Specifies the minimum amount by which you can scroll a scrollbar, for example, by clicking an arrow.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D2E				0	gu	Specifies the amount that a large step scrolls a scrollbar, for example, when you click between the scrollbar thumb and a scrollbar arrow.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D3B				0	gu	Specifies the delay in milliseconds between scrollbar trigger events. For example, the delay that occurs when you click an arrow button on the scrollbar and hold down the mouse button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D48				0	gu	Specifies the color of the arrows on the scrollbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D4F				0	gu	Visible Size				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D55				0	gu	Specifies the size of the scrollbar thumb in "value units". For example, a value of ("Scroll value max." minus "Scroll value min.") / 2 results in a scrollbar thumb that occupies half of the scrollbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D58				0	gu	To make the width of the scrollbar equal to the height of the scrollbar, set the Visible Size to zero.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11D63				0	gu	In a Calc spreadsheet, you can use the Data tab page to create a two-way link between a scrollbar and a cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148601				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Imagebutton\"\>Creates a button displayed as an image.\</ahelp\> Aside from the graphic representation, an image button has the same properties as a "normal" button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149596				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ImageControl\"\>Creates an image control. It can only be used to add images from a database.\</ahelp\> In the form document, double-click one of these controls to open the \<emph\>Insert Graphic\</emph\> dialog to insert the image. There is also a context menu (not in design mode) with commands for inserting and deleting the image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150318				0	gu	Images from a database can be displayed in a form, and new images can be inserted in the database as long as the image control is not write-protected. The control must refer to a database field of the image type. Therefore, enter the data field into the properties window on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156040				0	gu	Date field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151312				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DateField\"\>Creates a date field.\</ahelp\> If the form is linked to a database, the date values can be adopted from the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151302				0	gu	If you assign the "Dropdown" property to the date field, the user can open a calendar to select a date under the date field. This also applies to a date field within a Table Control field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154395				0	gu	Date fields can be easily edited by the user with the up arrow and down arrow keys. Depending on the cursor position, the day, month, or the year is can be increased or decreased using the arrow keys.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153112				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170003.xhp\" name=\"Specific Remarks on Date Fields\"\>Specific Remarks on Date Fields\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152369				0	gu	Time field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155399				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:TimeField\"\>Creates a time field.\</ahelp\> If the form is linked to a database, the time values for the form can be adopted from the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154764				0	gu	Time fields can be easily edited by the user with the up and down arrow keys. Depending on the cursor position, the hours, minutes, or the seconds are increased or decreased using the arrow keys.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156186				0	gu	Hide selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149438				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FileControl\"\>Creates a button that enables file selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145601				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:NumericField\"\>Creates a numerical field.\</ahelp\> If the form is linked to a database, the numerical values in the form can be adopted from the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145115				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CurrencyField\"\>Creates a currency field.\</ahelp\> If the form is linked to a database, the currency field contents for in the form can be adopted from the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148825				0	gu	Pattern field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150122				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PatternField\"\>Creates a pattern field.\</ahelp\> Pattern fields consist of an edit mask and a literal mask. The edit mask determines which data can be entered. The literal mask determines the contents of the pattern field when loading the form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152947				0	gu	Please note that pattern fields are not exported into HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145147				0	gu	સમૂહ પેટી				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154572				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:GroupBox\"\>Creates a frame to visually group several controls.\</ahelp\> Group boxes allow you to group option buttons in a frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148394				0	gu	If you insert a group frame into the document, the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01120000.xhp\" name=\"Group Element Wizard\"\>Group Element Wizard\</link\> starts, which allows you to easily create an option group.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150567				0	gu	\<emph\>Note:\</emph\> When you drag a group box over already existing controls and then want to select a control, you have to first open the context menu of the group box and choose \<emph\>Arrange - Send to Back\</emph\>. Then select the control while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615				0	gu	Group boxes are used only for a visual effect. A functional grouping of option fields can be made through the name definition: under the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"Name\"\>\<emph\>Name\</emph\>\</link\> properties of all option fields, enter the same name in order to group them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157996				0	gu	કોષ્ટક નિયંત્રણ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154579				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Creates a table control to display a database table.\</ahelp\> If you create a new table control, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170800.xhp\" name=\"Table Element Wizard\"\>Table Element Wizard\</link\> appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154697				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170004.xhp\" name=\"Special Information about Table Controls\"\>Special information about Table Controls\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11B3D				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_NAVIGATIONBAR\"\>Creates a navigation bar.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN11DB1				0	gu	The navigation bar allows you to move through the records of a database or a database form. The controls on this navigation bar work the same way as the controls on the default \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\"\>navigation bar\</link\> in $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146815				0	gu	આપોઆપ નિયંત્રણ પર પ્રકાશ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3109848	137			0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoControlFocus\"\>If\<emph\> Automatic Control Focus \</emph\>is activated, the first form control will be selected when you open the document. If the button is not activated, the text will be selected after opening. The \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170300.xhp\" name=\"Tab Order\"\>Tab Order\</link\> that you have specified determines which is the first form control.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	ફરીથી લાવો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07060000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153089				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>reloading; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; reloading\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading; reloading\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153089				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/07060000.xhp\" name=\"Reload\"\>Reload\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151315				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Reload\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Replaces the current document with the last saved version.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	gu	Any changes made after the last save will be lost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152551				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>submitting forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>get method for form transmissions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>post method for form transmissions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>General\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	gu	A form is a text document or spreadsheet with different form controls. If you create a form for a Web page, the user can enter data into it to send over the Internet. The data from the form controls of a form is transmitted to a server by specifying a URL and can be processed on the server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789				0	gu	Specifies a name for the form. This name is used to identify the form in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226				0	gu	Specifies the URL to which the data of the completed form is to be transmitted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	gu	Defines the target frame in which the loaded URL is to appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152551				0	gu	સોંપવા માટેનો પ્રકાર				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SUBMIT_METHOD\"\>Specifies the method to transfer the completed form information.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145065				0	gu	Using the "Get" method, the data of every control is transmitted as an environment variable. They are appended to the URL in the form "?Control1=Content1&Control2=Content2&..."; the character string is analyzed by a program on the recipient's server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	gu	Using the "Post" method, a document is created from the content of the form that is sent to the specified URL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	gu	સોંપવા માટે સંગ્રહ પધ્ધતિ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SUBMIT_ENCODING\"\>Specifies the type for encoding the data transfer.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419				0	gu	Data transfer of control information				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153717				0	gu	When sending a form, all controls available in $[officename] are taken into consideration. The name of the control and the corresponding value, if available, are transmitted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	gu	Which values are transmitted in each case depends on the respective control. For text fields, the visible entries are transmitted; for list boxes, the selected entries are transmitted; for check boxes and option fields, the associated reference values are transmitted if these fields were activated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	gu	How this information is transmitted depends on the selected transfer method (Get or Post) and the coding (URL or Multipart). If the Get method and URL encoding are selected, for example, value pairs in the form <Name>=<Value> are sent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3157909				0	gu	In addition to the controls that are recognized in HTML, $[officename] offers other controls. It should be noted that, for fields with a specific numerical format, the visible values are not transmitted but rather fixed default formats. The following table shows how the data of the $[officename]-specific controls is transmitted:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153698				0	gu	નિયંત્રણ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	gu	Value Pair				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153823				0	gu	Numeric field, currency field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734				0	gu	A decimal separator is always displayed as a period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	gu	Date field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	gu	The date format is sent in a fixed format (MM-DD-YYYY), regardless of the user's local settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	gu	Time field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153779				0	gu	The time format is sent in a fixed format (HH:MM:SS), regardless of the user's local settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	gu	Pattern field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	gu	The values of pattern fields are sent as text fields, that is, the value visible in the form is sent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	gu	Table control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	gu	From the table control, the individual columns are always transmitted. The name of the control, the name of the column, and the value of the column are sent. Using the Get method with URL encoding, the transmission is done in the form <Name of the table control>.<Name of the column>=<Value>, for example, with the value being dependent on the column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/02130000.xhp\" name=\"Decrease Indent\"\>Decrease Indent\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150247				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DecrementIndent\"\>Click the\<emph\> Decrease Indent \</emph\>icon to reduce the left indent of the current paragraph or cell content and set it to the previous tab position.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154186				0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If you previously increased the indentation for several collectively selected paragraphs, this command can decrease the indentation for all of the selected paragraphs. \</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>The cell content defers to the current value under \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cell - Alignment\"\>\<emph\>Format - Cell - Alignment\</emph\>\</link\>.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3150506\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_decrementindent.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150506\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If you click the\<emph\> Decrease Indent\</emph\> icon while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command key\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, the indent for the selected paragraph is moved by the default tab stop that has been set under \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040200.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Writer - General\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</emph\>\</link\> .\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02170000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Background color/Paragraph background 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147276				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3148538\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_backgroundcolor.png\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148538\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144439				0	gu	પાશ્વ ભાગનો રંગ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	To  Document End/Last Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154840	1			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\> \<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/10040000.xhp\" name=\"To  Document End\"\>To  Document End\</link\>\</caseinline\> \<defaultinline\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/10040000.xhp\" name=\"Last Page\"\>Last Page\</link\>\</defaultinline\> \</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:LastPage\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Moves to the last page of the document.\</ahelp\> This function is only active when you select the \<emph\>Page Preview\</emph\> function on the \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805				0	gu	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_gotoendofdoc.png\" id=\"img_id3153394\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153394\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\10040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\> \<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>To Document End\</caseinline\> \<defaultinline\>Last Page\</defaultinline\> \</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	રેકોર્ડ શોધો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146936				0	gu	\<variable id=\"datensatzsuche\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"Find Record\"\>Find Record\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147588				0	gu	\<variable id=\"suchentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RecSearch\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Searches database tables and forms.\</ahelp\>In forms or database tables, you can search through data fields, list boxes, and check boxes for specific values. \</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355				0	gu	When searching a table, the data fields of the current table are searched. When searching in a form, the data fields of the table linked with the form are searched.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	gu	The search described here is carried out by \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>. If you want to use the SQL server to search in a database, then you should use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12110000.xhp\" name=\"Form-based Filters\"\>Form-based Filters\</link\> icon on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Bar\"\>Form Bar\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	gu	The search function is also available for table controls. When calling the search function from a table control, you can search each column of the table control corresponding to the database columns of the linked database table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	gu	માટે શોધો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	gu	Specifies the type of search.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153683				0	gu	લખાણ:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORTEXT\"\>Enter the search term in the box or select it from the list.\</ahelp\> The text under the cursor is already copied into the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> combo box. Note that while running a search in a form, tabs and line breaks cannot be processed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539				0	gu	Your search terms will be saved as long as the table or the formula document is open. If you are running more than one search and you would like to repeat the search term, you can select a previously used search term from the combo box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662				0	gu	Field content is NULL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153543				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORNULL\"\>Specifies that fields will be found that contain no data.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153717				0	gu	Field content is not NULL				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORNOTNULL\"\>Specifies that fields will be found that contain data.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156153				0	gu	ક્યાં શોધવુ છે?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	gu	Specifies the fields for the search.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_LB_FORM\"\>Specifies the logical form in which you want the search to take place.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155434	107			0	gu	The\<emph\> Form \</emph\>combo box is only visible if the current document is a form document with more than one logical form. It does not appear during a search in tables or queries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	gu	Form documents may contain multiple logical forms. These are individual form components, which are each linked to a table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086				0	gu	The \<emph\>Form\</emph\> combo box contains the names of all logical forms for which controls exist.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159414				0	gu	બધા સત્રો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_ALLFIELDS\"\>Searches through all fields.\</ahelp\> If you are running a search in a table, all fields in the table will be searched. If you are running a search in a form, all fields of the logical form (entered under \<emph\>Form\</emph\>) will be searched. If you are running a search in a table control field, all columns that are linked to a valid database table field will be searched.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	gu	Note that the fields of the current logical form do not have to be identical to the fields of the form document. If the form document contains fields that point to multiple data sources (that is, multiple logical forms), the \<emph\>All Fields\</emph\> option will only search for the fields linked to data sources in the form document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150865				0	gu	એક જ ક્ષેત્ર				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SINGLEFIELD\"\>Searches through a specified data field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154365				0	gu	સુયોજનાઓ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158408				0	gu	Defines settings to control the search.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149809				0	gu	જગ્યા				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_POSITION\"\>Specifies the relationship of the search term and the field contents.\</ahelp\> The following options are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	gu	anywhere in the field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145744				0	gu	Returns all fields containing the search pattern anywhere in the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451				0	gu	beginning of field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	gu	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the beginning of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	gu	end of field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	gu	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the end of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	gu	entire field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127				0	gu	Returns all fields containing the search pattern as an exact match to the contents of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	gu	If the \<emph\>Wildcard expression\</emph\> check box is marked, this function is not available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_FORMATTER\"\>Specifies that all field formats are considered when searching in the current document.\</ahelp\> Field formats are all visible formats that are created using the following possibilities:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	gu	in table design mode for field properties,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488				0	gu	in data source view on column formatting,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152941				0	gu	in forms on control properties.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156736				0	gu	If the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> box is marked, the data source view of the table or form is searched using the formatting set there. If the box is not marked, the database is searched using the formatting saved in the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151280				0	gu	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	gu	You have a date field, which is saved in "DD.MM.YY" format in the database (for example, 17.02.65). The format of the entry is changed in the data source view to "DD. MMM YYYY" (17 Feb 1965). Following this example, a record containing February 17 is only found when the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> option is on:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145253				0	gu	Search Pattern				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3083279				0	gu	ચાલુ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155850				0	gu	"Feb" is returned, but not "2".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148590				0	gu	બંધ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	gu	"2" is returned, but not "Feb".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151321				0	gu	It is recommended that you always search using field formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401				0	gu	The following examples show possible issues when searching without field formatting. These issues depend on the database used and only occur for certain internal default formatting:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971				0	gu	Search Results				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154273				0	gu	Cause				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153836				0	gu	"5" returns "14:00:00" as a time				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156332				0	gu	Time fields are not defined for dBase databases and must be simulated. To internally display the time "14:00:00", a 5 is necessary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3157965				0	gu	"00:00:00" returns all records of a standard date field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146081				0	gu	The database stores a date value internally using a combined date/time field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	gu	"45.79" does not return "45.79" although the \<emph\>entire field\</emph\> option is selected under \<emph\>Position\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155518				0	gu	The view shown does not match what is stored internally. For example, if value 45.789 is stored in the database as a field of type Number/Double and the shown formatting is set to display only two decimals, "45.79" is only returned in searches with field formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148481				0	gu	In this case, standard formatting is formatting that refers to the internally stored data. It is not always visible to the user, especially if it is used for simulating data types (for example, time fields in dBase databases). This depends on the database used and the individual data type. Searching with field formatting is appropriate if you only want to find what is actually shown. This includes fields of type Date, Time, Date/Time and Number/Double.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507	31			0	gu	However, searching without \<emph\>Apply field format \</emph\>is appropriate for larger databases with no formatting issues, because it is faster.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153355				0	gu	If you are searching check boxes with \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\>, you will receive a "1" for marked check boxes, a "0" for unmarked check boxes, and an empty string for undefined (tristate) check boxes. If the search has been carried out without \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\>, you will see language-dependent default values "TRUE" or "FALSE".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150995	119			0	gu	If you use \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> when searching in list boxes, you find the text displayed in list boxes. If you do not use \<emph\>Apply field format,\</emph\> you will find the contents corresponding to the standard field format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150387				0	gu	કેસ સરખાવો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_CASE\"\>Specifies that upper and lower case are taken into consideration during the search.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145297				0	gu	ઊંધી દિશામાં શોધો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151249				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BACKWARD\"\>Specifies that the search process will run in reverse direction, from the last to the first record.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152484				0	gu	From top / From bottom				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_STARTOVER\"\>Restarts the search. A forward search restarts with the first record. A backwards search restarts with the last record.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163724				0	gu	વાઈલ્ડકાર્ડનું સમીકરણ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_WILDCARD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Allows a search with a * or ? wildcard.\</ahelp\> You can use the following wildcards:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146317				0	gu	Wildcards				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	gu	ઉદાહરણ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874				0	gu	for exactly one arbitrary character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	gu	"?loppy" returns "Floppy"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	gu	"M?ller" returns, for example, Miller and Moller				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156138				0	gu	for 0 or more arbitrary characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135				0	gu	"*-*" returns "ZIP-Drive" and "CD-ROM"				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	gu	"M*er" returns all entries starting with an "M" and ending in "er" (for example, Miller, Moller, Mather)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145762				0	gu	If you want to search for the actual characters ? or *, preface them with a backslash: "\\?" or "\\*". However, this is only necessary when \<emph\>Wildcard expression \</emph\>is enabled. When the option is not enabled, the wildcard characters are processed like normal characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147130				0	gu	નિયમિત સમીકરણ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_REGULAR\"\>Searches with regular expressions.\</ahelp\> The same regular expressions that are supported here are also supported in the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Find & Replace dialog\"\>Find & Replace dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154718				0	gu	Searching with regular expressions offers more options than searching with wildcard expressions. If you search with regular expressions, the following characters correspond to those used in searches with wildcards:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
