helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting Special Characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>characters; special\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; inserting special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>accents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>compose key to insert special characters\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	gu	\<variable id=\"insert_specialchar\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_specialchar.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Special Characters\"\>Inserting Special Characters\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	gu	This function allows you to insert special characters, such as check marks, boxes, and telephone symbols, into your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	gu	To view a selection of all characters, choose \<emph\>Insert - Special Character\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	gu	In the large selection field click the desired character or several characters in succession. The characters are displayed at the bottom of the dialog. When you close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>, all displayed characters in the selected font are inserted in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	gu	In any text input field (such as the input fields in the \<emph\>Find&Replace\</emph\> dialog) you can press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+S to call the \<emph\>Special Characters\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155630				0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>At present there are three ways of entering letters with accents directly from the keyboard. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>Sun Solaris:\</emph\> Using a Sun keyboard. First press the Compose key to the right of the space bar, then enter the first and second modifiers. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>Linux / NetBSD:\</emph\> Using the dead-keys. In an xterm window first press the (´) or (`) key. The character should not appear on the screen. Now press a letter, such as "e". The e is given an accent, é or è. If not, then check in the XF86Config file if a "nodeadkeys" XkbdVariant has been loaded there and replace it. You may also have set the environment variable SAL_NO_DEADKEYS, which deactivates the dead-keys. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>All Unix systems:\</emph\> (Alt Graph) as additional compose key. The (Alt Graph) key can work in $[officename] like the Compose key, if you set the environment variable SAL_ALTGR_COMPOSE. The (Alt Graph) key must trigger a mode_switch, so, for example, xmodmap -e "keysym Alt_R = Mode_switch" must be set. First press (Alt Graph), then the first modifier, then the second modifier. The characters are combined as described on a Solaris system in the file /usr/openwin/include/X11/Suncompose.h. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04100000.xhp\" name=\"Special Characters\"\>Special Characters\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect\"\>AutoCorrect\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Saving Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	gu	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	gu	Select the filter you want to delete and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Recording and Displaying Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	gu	\<variable id=\"redlining\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining.xhp\" name=\"Recording and Displaying Changes\"\>Recording and Displaying Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	gu	When several authors are working on the same text or spreadsheet, the review function records and displays who made the various changes. On the final edit of the document, it is then possible to look at each individual change and decide whether it should be accepted or rejected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	gu	For example: You are an editor and are delivering your latest report. But before publication the report must be read by the senior editor and the proofreader, and both will add their changes. The senior editor writes "clarify" after one paragraph and crosses out another entirely. The proofreader corrects the spelling of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	gu	The edited document comes back to you, and you can incorporate or ignore the suggestions of the two reviewers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	gu	Let's say you also e-mailed a copy of the report to a good friend and colleague who has done research on a similar topic in the past. You asked for a few suggestions, and the document is now returned by e-mail with your colleague's suggestions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	gu	As all your colleagues and the managers in your company work with $[officename], you can produce a final version of the document from the results you get back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Sending Documents as E-mail				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	gu	\<variable id=\"email\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/email.xhp\" name=\"Sending Documents as E-mail\"\>Sending Documents as E-mail\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	gu	Working in $[officename], you can send the current document as an e-mail attachment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Document as E-mail\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	gu	$[officename] opens your default e-mail program.\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\> If you want to send the current document with another e-mail program, you can select the program to use with \<emph\>Tools - Options - Internet - E-mail\</emph\>. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	gu	In your e-mail program, enter the recipient, subject and any text you want to add, then send the e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Changing the Title of a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156324				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>titles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;document titles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; changing titles\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156324				0	gu	\<variable id=\"change_title\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/change_title.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Title of a Document\"\>Changing the Title of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	gu	You can specify a title for your document. Some file manager utilities can display the titles next to the filenames of your documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	gu	How to change the title of the current document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Properties of\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	gu	Select the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	gu	Type the new title in the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100000.xhp\" name=\"Properties of\"\>Properties of\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Working With %PRODUCTNAME XML Filters 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10923				0	gu	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter.xhp\"\>Working With %PRODUCTNAME XML Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10927				0	gu	%PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\"\>stores documents in XML format\</link\>. You can create customized filters that convert the native OpenDocument XML file format used by %PRODUCTNAME into another format. These filters can be integrated into %PRODUCTNAME seamlessly so that you can save or load these formats transparently.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093A				0	gu	To create an XML filter, you must have a good understanding of XML and XSLT concepts. These concepts are beyond the scope of this help.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	gu	An XML filter contains \<emph\>stylesheets\</emph\> that are written in the XSLT language. The stylesheets define the transformation from the OpenDocument file format to another XML format through export and import filters. There are three types of XML filters:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10947				0	gu	\<emph\>Import Filters\</emph\> load external XML files and transform the format of the files into the OpenDocument XML file format. After you install an import filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10960				0	gu	\<emph\>Export Filters\</emph\> transform OpenDocument XML files and \<emph\>save\</emph\> the files to a different XML format. After you install an export filter, the name of the filter is added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070001.xhp\"\>Export dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10979				0	gu	\<emph\>Import/Export Filters\</emph\> load and save OpenDocument XML files into a different XML \<emph\>format\</emph\>. After you install these filters, the names of the filters are added to the list of file types in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\"\>File Open dialog\</link\> and the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\"\>File Save As dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B39				0	gu	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/Style/XSL/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible \<emph\>Stylesheet\</emph\> Language (XSL)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4E				0	gu	\<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/XML/\"\>World Wide Web Consortium Pages on Extensible Markup Language (XML)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting Hyperlinks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	gu	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	gu	You can insert hyperlinks in two ways: as text or as a button. In both cases, the visible text can be different from the URL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	7			0	gu	Display the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>. Type the visible text in the left field and the full URL in the right field, including http:// or file://.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	8			0	gu	Place the text cursor in the document at the point where you want to insert the hyperlink. Click the\<emph\> Hyperlink\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\>. The hyperlink is inserted as text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	gu	If you want to insert the hyperlink as a button, click and hold the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>As Button\</emph\> from the sub-menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3149763\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_hyperlinkdialog.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149763\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	30			0	gu	To use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> instead of the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> to define the hyperlink, click the icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	23			0	gu	To jump to a specific line in a text document, first enter a bookmark at that position (\<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>). 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076D				0	gu	To jump to a cell in a spreadsheet, first enter a name for the cell (\<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	gu	In the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> combo box, enter only the short form of the URL when jumping within the same document: If the bookmark is called \<emph\>Target\</emph\>, enter \<emph\>Target\</emph\>. To jump to another document, enter the complete URL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152887				0	gu	Hyperlinks can also be inserted by drag-and-drop from the Navigator. Hyperlinks can refer to references, headings, graphics, tables, objects, directories or bookmarks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	gu	If you wish to insert in a text a hyperlink that refers to Table 1, drag the entry Table 1 from the Navigator and drop it in the text. To do this, the \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink\</emph\> drag mode must be selected in the Navigator.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Turning off Automatic URL Recognition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	gu	\<variable id=\"autocorr_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/autocorr_url.xhp\" name=\"Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\"\>Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	gu	When you enter text, $[officename] automatically recognizes a word that may be a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\> and replaces the word with a hyperlink. $[officename] formats the hyperlink with direct font attributes (color and underline) the properties of which are obtained from certain Character Styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	gu	If you do not want $[officename] to automatically recognize URLs as you are typing, there are several ways of turning off this feature.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154306				0	gu	Undo URL Recognition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	gu	When you are typing and notice that a text has just been automatically converted into a hyperlink, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z to undo this formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235				0	gu	If you do not notice this conversion until later, select the hyperlink and choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152350				0	gu	Turn off URL Recognition				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	gu	Load a document of the type for which you want to modify the URL recognition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246				0	gu	If you want to modify the URL recognition for text documents, open a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	gu	In the \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	gu	If you unmark \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>, words will no longer be automatically replaced with hyperlinks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	gu	In $[officename] Writer there are two check boxes in front of \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>. The box in the first column is for later post-editing and the box in the second column is for AutoCorrect as you type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Executing SQL Commands				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	gu	\<variable id=\"data_enter_sql\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_enter_sql.xhp\" name=\"Executing SQL Commands\"\>Executing SQL Commands\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	gu	With the help of SQL commands you can control the database directly, and can also create and edit tables and queries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	gu	Not all database types support all SQL instructions. If necessary, find out which SQL commands are supported by your database system.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id9577929				0	gu	To execute an SQL statement directly				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id7923825				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open a database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id9448530				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - SQL\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Query\</emph\> window, choose \<emph\>View - Switch Design View On/Off\</emph\>. Edit the SQL command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3153223				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Using Digital Signatures				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063C				0	gu	Get a certificate				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	gu	Manage your certificates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	gu	If you are using Microsoft Windows, you can manage your certificates from the Control Panel applet "Internet Options" on the "Contents" tab page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id8311410				0	gu	Import your new root certificate into the Trusted Root Certification Authorities list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	gu	If you are using Solaris or Linux, you must install a recent version of Thunderbird, Mozilla Suite, or Firefox software to install some system files that are needed for encryption.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10720				0	gu	If you have created different profiles in Thunderbird, Mozilla, or Firefox, and you want %PRODUCTNAME to use one specified profile for certificates, then you can set the environment variable MOZILLA_CERTIFICATE_FOLDER to point to the folder of that specified profile.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id944242				0	gu	Open your Web browser's preferences dialog, select the Privacy & Security tab page, click on Certificates - Manage Certificates. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id6452223				0	gu	Import your new root certificate, then select and edit the certificate. Enable the root certificate to be trusted at least for web and email access. This ensures that the certificate can sign your documents. You may edit any intermediate certificate in the same way, but it is not mandatory for signing documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_id6486098				0	gu	When you have edited the new certificates, restart %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	gu	Signing a document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Digital Signatures\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10690				0	gu	A message box advises you to save the document. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to save the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN10698				0	gu	After saving, you see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/digitalsignatures.xhp\"\>Digital Signatures\</link\> dialog. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to add a public key to the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AE				0	gu	In the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/selectcertificate.xhp\"\>Select Certificate\</link\> dialog, select your certificate and click OK. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	gu	You see again the Digital Signatures dialog, where you can add more certificates if you want. Click OK to add the public key to the saved file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E0				0	gu	Signing the macros inside a document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E4				0	gu	Normally, macros are part of a document. If you sign a document, the macros inside the document are signed automatically. If you want to sign only the macros, but not the document, proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EA				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Digital Signature\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_send.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F2				0	gu	Apply the signature as described above for documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Assistive Tools in $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] assistive technology\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assistive technology in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen readers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	gu	\<variable id=\"assistive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"Assistive Tools in $[officename]\"\>Assistive Tools in $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	gu	$[officename] supports some assistive technology tools like screen magnification software, screen readers, and on-screen keyboards. Most of these tools communicate with $[officename] by means of the Java(TM) Access Bridge software, that uses the Java Accessibility API, a part of the Java runtime environment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	gu	Requirements to use assistive tools in $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	gu	Java Runtime Environment (JRE) version 1.4.1_01 and higher, or version 1.4.0_02 with the locale set to "en_us".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	gu	Most recent version of the software for your assistive tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	15			0	gu	On Windows systems, \<link href=\"http://www.sun.com/access/downloads/\" name=\"Java Access Bridge\"\>Java Access Bridge\</link\> software version 1.0.3 or higher 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	gu	On UNIX(R) systems, the GNOME 2 desktop environment with the Java Access Bridge software for GNOME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149795				0	gu	Supported Assistive Tools				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	gu	On Windows systems, $[officename] directly supports most on-screen keyboard software. Additional support for assistive tools is provided by the Java Access Bridge software. The following is a list of some assistive tools that use the Java Access Bridge software to exchange data with $[officename]:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	gu	ZoomText Screen Magnifier (version 7.11 or higher)(Windows)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	gu	Gnopernicus Screen Reader and Magnifier, using GNOME Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface (at-spi) and Java Accessibility API software				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	gu	GNOME On Screen Keyboard (GOK), using GNOME at-spi and Java Accessibility API software				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061				0	gu	Supported Input Devices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	gu	$[officename] provides the ability to use alternative input devices for access to all functions of $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045				0	gu	Screen magnification software allow users with low vision to work in $[officename] with caret and focus tracking.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	gu	On-screen keyboards enable users to perform almost all data input and commands with a mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	gu	Screen readers allow visually impaired users to access $[officename] with text-to-speech and Braille displays.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149808				0	gu	When accessibility support in $[officename] is enabled, the Java Runtime Environment is loaded, and increases the startup time for $[officename].				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Selecting the Maximum Printable Area on a Page				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149180				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>page formats; maximizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; maximizing page formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printers; maximum page formats\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180				0	gu	\<variable id=\"pageformat_max\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pageformat_max.xhp\" name=\"Selecting the Maximum Printable Area on a Page\"\>Selecting the Maximum Printable Area on a Page\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	gu	Not all printers can print a paper up to its edges. Most of them leave an unprinted margin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	gu	$[officename] offers a semi-automatic feature that enables you to print as close to the paper's edge as is possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	gu	Make sure that your printer has been setup under \<emph\>File - Printer Settings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	gu	Select the \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\> command, and go to the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	gu	Under \<emph\>Margins\</emph\> you can define the maximum or minimum possible value for the page margins (left, right, top, and bottom). Click into the respective spin box, then press the (Page Up) or (Page Down) key. The preview displays a dashed line around the printable range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> to close the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\" name=\"Printing\"\>Printing\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Dragging and Dropping Within a $[officename] Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;overview\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mouse; pointers when using drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links;by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147571				0	gu	\<variable id=\"dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop.xhp\" name=\"Dragging and Dropping Within a $[officename] Document\"\>Dragging and Dropping Within a $[officename] Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	gu	There are many options for moving or copying objects using drag-and-drop. Text sections, drawing objects, graphics, form controls, hyperlinks, cell ranges, and many more can be moved or copied with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	gu	Note that the mouse pointer displays a plus sign when copying and an arrow when creating a link or hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798				0	gu	માઉસ નિર્દેશક				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	gu	વર્ણન				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3159177				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3147573\" src=\"res/helpimg/movedata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147573\"\>Mouse pointer moving data\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154898				0	gu	Moving				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3149233\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149233\"\>Mouse pointer copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627				0	gu	Copying				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3159413\" src=\"res/helpimg/linkdata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159413\"\>Mouse pointer inserting link\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	gu	Creating a link				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3158407\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20238.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3158407\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	gu	If you drag objects out of the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/navigator.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>\<emph\>Navigator\</emph\>\</link\>, you can specify in the submenu of the Navigator's \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon whether to copy the object, insert it as a link or insert it as a hyperlink.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	gu	You can cancel a drag-and-drop operation in $[officename] at any time by pressing the Esc key before releasing the mouse button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	ભૂલ અહેવાલ સાધન				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616				0	gu	\<variable id=\"error_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/error_report.xhp\" name=\"Error Report Tool\"\>Error Report Tool\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	gu	The Error Report Tool gathers all necessary information that can help the program developers to improve the code, so that in later versions this error can possibly be avoided. Please help us to improve the software and send the generated error report.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538				0	gu	ભૂલના અહેવાલ માટેનું સાધન શરુ કરી રહ્યા છે				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154046				0	gu	અહેવાલ પૂરો કરી રહ્યા છે				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	gu	On the main Error Report Tool dialog, you can enter some additional information that may help the developers to localize the error. For example, if the error only appears after a change in your hardware or software environment, or if you clicked on a button, please include that information.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399				0	gu	Sending the Error Report				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	gu	The Error Report Tool uses the HTTP PUT / SOAP protocol to send the report data. You may optionally enter some descriptive text that will help us to identify the context of the program crash. Then click the \<emph\>Send\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	gu	You will not get an answer to your error report. If you need support, please visit the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\"\>support forum\</link\> on the Internet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	gu	You may choose to respond to questions that the developers may have about the reported error. Mark the check box if you allow to be contacted by e-mail, should additional information be required. By default this box is not marked, so you will not get any e-mail.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	gu	કઈ માહિતી મોકલાઈ?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	gu	The error report consists of several files. The main file contains information about the error type, operating system name and version, memory usage, and the description that you entered. You can click the \<emph\>Show Report\</emph\> button on the main dialog of the Error Report Tool to view what will get sent in the main file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	gu	In addition, relevant memory contents and stack traces are gathered by some system standard tools ("dbhhelp.dll" on Windows systems, "pstack" on UNIX systems). This information will be sent also.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Undoing Direct Formatting for a Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067F				0	gu	\<variable id=\"undo_formatting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/undo_formatting.xhp\"\>Undoing Direct Formatting for a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10683				0	gu	You can undo all formatting that has not been made by styles in a few steps.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10639				0	gu	Removing all Direct Formatting in a $[officename] Writer Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064A				0	gu	Removing all Direct Formatting in a $[officename] Calc Spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	gu	While pressing the Shift key click the first and then the last sheet tab to select all sheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	gu	Removing all Direct Formatting in a $[officename] Presentation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Outline\</emph\> tab to open outline view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\undo_formatting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B0				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01011000.xhp\"\>Undo Options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Setting up Printer, Fax and Fonts Under UNIX Based Platforms				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147834				0	gu	\<variable id=\"spadmin\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\" name=\"Setting up Printer, Fax and Fonts Under UNIX Based Platforms\"\>Setting up Printer, Fax and Fonts Under UNIX Based Platforms\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	gu	Under UNIX based platforms, the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> is provided to help you set up printers, faxes and fonts for use with the $[officename] software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	gu	Call the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	gu	Go to the {install_path}/program directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	gu	After it starts, the window of the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	gu	Following a server installation, the system administrator first logs on as with root privileges, and starts the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>. The administrator then creates a general printer configuration file called {install_path}/share/psprint/psprint.conf for all users. All changes are immediately available to all users.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159177				0	gu	Setting up Printers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	gu	Under UNIX based platforms, the $[officename] software only offers direct support for printers using the PostScript technology. Other printers must be set up as described in the section \<emph\>Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software\</emph\>. The $[officename] software automatically provides a printer with the default driver for each system queue. You can add additional printers as needed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148564				0	gu	Adding a Printer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	gu	Go to the {install_path}/program directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210				0	gu	Select the \<emph\>Create Printer\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	gu	Select the appropriate driver for your printer. If you are not using a PostScript printer or your model is not listed, use the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> driver or follow the steps below. You can also add new drivers using the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> button or delete unnecessary drivers using the \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> button. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	gu	Choose a command line that you can use to print on your printer (for example, lp -d my_queue). Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	gu	Give the printer a name and determine whether it should become the default printer. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	gu	To print a test page, click on \<emph\>Test Page\</emph\>. If the test page fails to print or is incorrectly printed, check all settings as described in \<emph\>Changing Printer Settings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146147				0	gu	Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	gu	When installing a non-PostScript printer, you must set your system so that PostScript can be converted into the language of the printer. We recommend using current PostScript conversion software such as Ghostscript (http://www.cs.wisc.edu/~ghost/).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154639				0	gu	You should set up the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> in that case. Also make sure that the page margins are set correctly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	gu	If you are using a printer using the PostScript technology, you should install a description file for the printer (PostScript Printer Definition - PPD) so that you can utilize the specific printer features like paper tray selection, duplex print function and all built-in fonts. You can also use the generic printer driver since it contains the most important data and is suitable for most printers. In that case, you will have to do without the paper tray selection and must correctly set the page margins.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976	128			0	gu	Some PPD files are installed as default files. If there is no matching PPD file for your printer, you will find various PPD files at http://www.adobe.com/products/printerdrivers/. You can also ask the manufacturer of your printer for PPD files. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147435				0	gu	Importing Drivers When Creating a New Printer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Import\</emph\> in the driver selection dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	347			0	gu	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> to select the directory where you unpacked the PPD files. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147443				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Selection of drivers\</emph\> list box, select the printer driver you want to install.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152885				0	gu	Deleting Drivers When Creating a New Printer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	gu	Select the printer driver.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149909				0	gu	Be sure that you do not delete the generic printer driver, and remember that drivers deleted from server installations are no longer available to other users who are using the same server installation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	gu	If the printer has more fonts built in than the usual PostScript fonts, you must also load the AFM files for these additional fonts. Copy the AFM files into the {install_path}/share/psprint/fontmetric directory or into the {install_path}/user/psprint/fontmetric directory. You can find AFM files, for example, at ftp://ftp.adobe.com/pub/adobe/type/win/all/afmfiles/.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148388				0	gu	Changing Printer Settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	gu	In the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>, select the printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog appears containing several tab pages. This is where you can make settings that are used according to the PPD file of the selected printer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148833				0	gu	Select the command on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. You can remove superfluous commands using the \<emph\>Remove\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154270				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Paper\</emph\> tab page, you can define the paper format and paper tray to be used as the default settings for this printer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Device\</emph\> tab page, you can activate the special options for your printer. If your printer can only print in black and white, choose "grayscale" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\>, otherwise choose "color". If switching to grayscale leads to unfavorable results, you can also select "color" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\> and see how the printer or PostScript emulator applies it. Furthermore, on this tab page you can set the precision with which colors are described as well as the PostScript level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	gu	The \<emph\>Font Replacement\</emph\> tab page allows you to select a printer font type available in the printer for each font type installed on your computer. This way you can reduce the data volume sent to the printer. Font replacement can be turned on or off for each printer individually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	gu	You should also set the page margins correctly on the \<emph\>Additional settings\</emph\> tab when using the generic printer driver so that your printout is not cropped. You can also enter a description in the Comments field, which will also be displayed on the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	gu	Some of these settings can also be set for the current printout in the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog or the \<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\> dialog in the $[officename] software with the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042				0	gu	Renaming or Deleting Printers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	gu	Select a printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	gu	To rename the selected printer, click \<emph\>Rename\</emph\>. Enter an appropriate name in the dialog that appears and click OK. The name must be unique and should be chosen so that you can recognize the printer and the application. Printer names must be assigned the same for all users because, when documents are exchanged, the selected printer remains unchanged if the recipient has it under the same name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	gu	To delete the selected printer, click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>. The default printer or a printer that has been created by the system administrator in a server installation cannot be removed using this dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147346				0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Selecting a Default Printer \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769				0	gu	To make the printer selected from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box the default printer, double-click its name or click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154204				0	gu	Using Fax Functionality				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463				0	gu	If you have installed a fax package such as Efax or HylaFax on your computer, you can send faxes with the $[officename] software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154575				0	gu	Go to the {install_path}/program directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146808				0	gu	Click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151070				0	gu	Select \<emph\>Connect a fax device\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150787				0	gu	Choose whether to use the default driver or another printer driver. If you are not using the default driver, select the appropriate driver. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	gu	Enter a command line with which to communicate with the fax in the following dialog. In the command line of each fax sent "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(PHONE)" by the telephone number of the recipient fax machine. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the PostScript code is transmitted in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135				0	gu	Assign a name to your new fax printer and determine whether the telephone numbers (see below) marked in the text should be removed from the printout, or not. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506				0	gu	You can now send faxes by printing to the printer that has just been created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148419				0	gu	Enter the fax number as text in the document. You can also enter a field that takes the fax number from your active database. In any case, the fax number must start with the characters @@# and end with @@. A valid entry would have the form @@#1234567@@.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826				0	gu	If these characters including the telephone number are not printed, activate the \<emph\>Fax number is removed from the printout\</emph\> option under \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. If no telephone number is entered in the document, a dialog prompting you for it will appear after the printout.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	gu	Remember to create one separate print job for each fax, otherwise, the first recipient will receive all the faxes. In the \<emph\>Tools - Mail Merge\</emph\> dialog select the \<emph\>Printer\</emph\> option and then select the \<emph\>Single print jobs\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146929				0	gu	Connecting a PostScript to PDF Converter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154989				0	gu	If a PostScript to PDF converter such as Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is installed on your computer, you can quickly create PDF documents in the $[officename] software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150524				0	gu	In spadmin, click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	gu	Select \<emph\>Connect a PDF converter\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	gu	Choose whether to use the default driver, the Acrobat Distiller driver or another driver. The driver "Generic Printer (T42 enabled)" prefers the type 42 fonts over type 3 fonts; this driver is a good choice for output to a software PostScript interpreter. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155128				0	gu	In the next dialog, enter a command line for the PostScript->PDF Converter. Enter the directory where the PDF files should be saved. If you do not provide a directory, the user's home directory will be used. In the command line "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(OUTFILE)" by the target file, the name of which is created from the document name. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the Postscript code is forwarded in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. If Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is in the search path, you can use one of the predefined command lines. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889				0	gu	Assign a name to your new PDF converter. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153064				0	gu	You can now create PDF documents by printing to the converter that has just been created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Selecting the Document Language				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	bm_id3083278				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>languages; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters; language selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>character styles;language selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; language selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraph styles; languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; default languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dictionaries, see also languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;languages, to selected text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083278				0	gu	\<variable id=\"language_select\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/language_select.xhp\" name=\"Selecting the Document Language\"\>Selecting the Document Language\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	gu	The language you select for your document determines the dictionary used for spellcheck, thesaurus and hyphenation, the decimal and thousands delimiter used and the default currency format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3153093				0	gu	The language you select applies to the whole document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	gu	Within the document, you can apply a separate language to any paragraph style. This has priority over the language of the whole document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	gu	You can assign a language to selected pieces of text in a paragraph, either by direct formatting or with a character style. This assignment has priority over the paragraph style and document language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	gu	Selecting a language for the whole document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	gu	Under \<emph\>Default languages for documents\</emph\>, select the document language for all newly created documents. If you mark \<emph\>For the current document only\</emph\>, your choice will only apply to the current document. Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152938				0	gu	Selecting a language for a Paragraph Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	gu	Place the cursor in the paragraph whose paragraph style you want to edit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367				0	gu	Open the context menu and select \<emph\>Edit Paragraph Style\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	gu	Select the \<emph\>Rules\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	gu	All paragraphs formatted with the current paragraph style will have the selected language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145801				0	gu	Applying a language directly to selected text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	gu	Select the text to which you want to apply a language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3159348				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	gu	Select the \<emph\>Rules\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154164				0	gu	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and proceed accordingly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154272				0	gu	Selecting a language for a Character Style				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649				0	gu	Open the Styles and Formatting window and click on the \<emph\>Character Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	gu	Click on the name of the character style to which you want to apply a different language.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150753				0	gu	Then open the context menu in the Styles and Formatting window and select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character Style\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150321				0	gu	Select the \<emph\>Rules\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	gu	Now you can apply the character style to your selected text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152483				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Format - Character - Font\"\>Format - Character - Font\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Printing in Black and White				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150125				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>printing; black and white\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>black and white printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>colors; not printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; printing in black\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150125				0	gu	\<variable id=\"print_blackwhite\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/print_blackwhite.xhp\" name=\"Printing in Black and White\"\>Printing in Black and White\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	gu	Printing text and graphics in black and white				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	gu	Click on \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. This opens the Properties dialog for your printer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	gu	Select the option to print in black and white. For further information, refer to the user's manual of your printer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	gu	The current document will be printed in black and white.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	gu	Printing in black and white in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573	12			0	gu	Under \<emph\>Quality,\</emph\> select either \<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> or \<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307				0	gu	When either of these options is selected, all presentations or drawings will be printed without color. If you only want to print in black for the \<emph\>current\</emph\> print job, select the option in \<emph\>File - Print - Options\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3149786	15			0	gu	\<emph\>Grayscale\</emph\> converts all colors to a maximum of 256 gradations from black to white. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610	16			0	gu	\<emph\>Black & white\</emph\> converts all colors into the two values black and white. All borders around objects are printed black. All text will be printed in black. A background set by \<emph\>Format - Page - Background\</emph\> will not be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	gu	Printing only text in black and white				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	gu	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer you can choose to print color-formatted text in black and white. You can specify this either for all subsequent text documents to be printed, or only for the current printing process.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150358				0	gu	Printing all text documents with black and white text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910	22			0	gu	Under \<emph\>Contents,\</emph\> mark \<emph\>Print black\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	gu	All text documents or HTML documents will be printed with black text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148920				0	gu	Printing the current text document with black and white text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\" name=\"Printing dialogs\"\>Printing dialogs\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_blackwhite.xhp	0	help	par_id3154146				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options dialog\"\>Tools - Options dialog\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157896				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>databases; text formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables in text format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; spreadsheets to text format\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154824				0	gu	\<variable id=\"data_dbase2office\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_dbase2office.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\"\>Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	gu	If you want to exchange data with a database that does not have an ODBC link and does not allow dBase import and export, you can use a common text format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	gu	To exchange data in a text format use the $[officename] Calc import/export filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	gu	Export the desired data from the source database in a text format. The CSV text format is recommended. This format separates data fields by using delimiters such as commas or semi-colons, and separates records by inserting line breaks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> and click the file to import.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id1977904				0	gu	Select "Text CSV" from the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> combo box. Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	gu	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Text Import\"\>\<emph\>Text Import\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Decide which data to include from the text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	gu	Once the data is in a $[officename] Calc spreadsheet, you can edit it as needed. Save the data as a $[officename] data source:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	gu	Save the current $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in dBase format in the folder of a dBase database. To do this, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>, then select the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> "dBase" and the folder of the dBase database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400				0	gu	Exporting in CSV Text Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	gu	You can export the current $[officename] spreadsheet in a text format which can be read by many other applications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	gu	In \<emph\>File type\</emph\> select the filter "Text CSV". Enter a file name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	gu	This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"dBase Export\"\>\<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, in which you can select the character set, field delimiter and text delimiter. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. A warning informs you that only the active sheet was saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Merging Versions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>documents; merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging; documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions;merging document versions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154230				0	gu	\<variable id=\"redlining_docmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging Versions\"\>Merging Versions\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	gu	When a document has been edited by more than one person, it is possible to merge the edited copies into the original. The only requirement is that the documents differ only and exclusively in the recorded changes - all other original text must be identical.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425				0	gu	Open the original document into which you want to merge all copies.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Merge Document\</emph\>. A file selection dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	gu	Select the copy of the document from the dialog. If there have been no subsequent changes to the original document, the copy is merged into the original.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	gu	If changes have been made to the original document, an error dialog appears that informs you that the merge is unsuccessful.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_docmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	gu	After you merge the documents you will see the recorded changes from the copy in the original document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
