helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Languages Using Complex Text Layout				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662				0	gu	\<variable id=\"ctl\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ctl.xhp\" name=\"Languages Using Complex Text Layout\"\>Languages Using Complex Text Layout\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	gu	Currently, $[officename] supports Hindi, Thai, Hebrew, and Arabic as \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#ctl\" name=\"CTL languages\"\>CTL languages\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3155420				0	gu	If you select the text flow from right to left, embedded Western text still runs from left to right. The cursor responds to the arrow keys in that Right Arrow moves it "to the text end" and Left Arrow "to the text start".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	gu	You can change the text writing direction directly be pressing one of the following keys:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	gu	The modifier-only key combinations only work when CTL support is enabled.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	gu	In multicolumn pages, sections or frames that are formatted with text flow from right to left, the first column is the right column and the last column is the left column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	gu	In $[officename] Writer text formatted in \<emph\>Thai language\</emph\> has the following features:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	gu	In paragraphs with justified alignment, the characters are stretched to flush the lines at the margins. In other languages the spaces between words are stretched.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909				0	gu	Use the Delete key to delete a whole composite character. Use the Backspace key to delete the last part of the previous composite character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809				0	gu	Use the Right or Left Arrow key to jump to the next or previous whole composite character. To position the cursor into a composite character, use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Table Design				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	gu	\<variable id=\"data_tabledefine\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\" name=\"Table Design\"\>Table Design\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	gu	This section contains information about how to create a new database table in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05010000.xhp\" name=\"design view\"\>design view\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288				0	gu	Open the database file of the database where you want a new table. Click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon. Choose \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\> to create a new table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798				0	gu	In the Design view, you can now create the fields for your table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349				0	gu	Enter new fields in rows from top to bottom. Click the \<emph\>Field Name\</emph\> cell and enter a field name for each data field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	gu	In the next cell to the right, define the \<emph\>Field Type\</emph\>. When you click in the cell, you can select a field type in the combo box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	gu	Each field can only accept data corresponding to the specified field type. For example, it is not possible to enter text in a number field. Memo fields in dBase III format are references to internally-managed text files which can hold up to 64KB text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	gu	You can enter an optional \<emph\>Description\</emph\> for each field. The text of the description will appear as a tip on the column headings in the table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	gu	ક્ષેત્ર ગુણધર્મો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	gu	Enter properties for each selected data field. Depending on the database type, some input facilities may not be available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> box, enter the default contents for every new record. This contents can be edited later.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Entry required\</emph\> box, specify whether or not the field may remain empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tabledefine.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	gu	For the \<emph\>Length\</emph\> box, a combo box may be shown that provides the available choices.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Accepting or Rejecting Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150247				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>changes; accepting or rejecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function;accepting or rejecting changes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150247				0	gu	\<variable id=\"redlining_accept\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_accept.xhp\" name=\"Accepting or Rejecting Changes\"\>Accepting or Rejecting Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	gu	When you edit a document in which others have made changes, you can accept or reject the changes individually or all together.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	gu	If you have put multiple copies of the document in circulation, first merge these into one document (see \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp#redlining_docmerge\"/\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	gu	Open the document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Accept or Reject\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	gu	Select a change on the \<emph\>List\</emph\> tab. The change is selected and displayed in the document and you can now enter your decision with one of the buttons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	gu	If one author has modified another author's change, you will see the changes hierarchically arranged with a plus sign for opening up the hierarchy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	gu	If the list of changes is too long, you can switch to the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> tab in the dialog and specify that you only want to see the changes of certain authors, or only the changes of the last day, or that you want the list to be restricted in some other way.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	gu	Color-coded entries display the result of the filter that is set. Entries in black can be accepted or rejected and match the filter criteria. Entries in blue do not themselves match the filter criteria, but have subentries that are included by the filter. Gray entries cannot be accepted or rejected and do not match the filter criterion. Green entries do match the filter but cannot be accepted or rejected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Saving Documents Automatically				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152924				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>documents; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;documents, automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backups;automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawings; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; saving automatically\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155536				0	gu	\<variable id=\"doc_autosave\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/doc_autosave.xhp\" name=\"Saving Documents Automatically\"\>Saving Documents Automatically\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410				0	gu	To create a backup file every time you save a document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	gu	Mark \<emph\>Always create backup copy\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3149797	6			0	gu	If the \<emph\>Always create backup copy\</emph\> option is selected, the old version of the file is saved to the backup directory whenever you save the current version of the file. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415				0	gu	The backup copy has the same name as the document, but the extension is .BAK. If the backup folder already contains such a file, it will be overwritten without warning.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149514				0	gu	To save recovery information automatically every n minutes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	gu	Mark \<emph\>Save AutoRecovery information every\</emph\> and select the time interval.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	gu	This command saves the information necessary to restore the current document in case of a crash. Additionally, in case of a crash %PRODUCTNAME tries automatically to save AutoRecovery information for all open documents, if possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_idN10838				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/error_report.xhp\"\>Error Report Tool\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Showing Navigation Pane of the Help				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>Help; navigation pane showing/hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;navigation pane in Help window\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indexes;showing/hiding Help index tab\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150178				0	gu	\<variable id=\"navpane_on\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/navpane_on.xhp\" name=\"Showing Navigation Pane of the Help\"\>Showing Navigation Pane of the Help\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	gu	In the Help window, you can show or hide the navigation pane as needed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3156411				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3153345\" src=\"sfx2/res/indexon_small.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153345\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	gu	On the toolbar of the \<emph\>Help\</emph\> window, click the left icon to show or hide the navigation pane.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\numbering_stop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Turning off Bullets and Numbering for Individual Paragraphs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\numbering_stop.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154186				0	gu	\<variable id=\"numbering_stop\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/numbering_stop.xhp\" name=\"Turning off Bullets and Numbering for Individual Paragraphs\"\>Turning off Bullets and Numbering for Individual Paragraphs\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\numbering_stop.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	gu	For the current paragraph or selected paragraphs you can switch off the automatic numbering or listing. Click the \<emph\>Numbering Off\</emph\> icon in the \<emph\>Bullets and Numbering\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\numbering_stop.xhp	0	help	par_id3144511	31			0	gu	If the cursor is located within a numbered or bulleted list, you can turn off automatic numbers or bullets for the current paragraph or selected paragraphs by clicking the \<emph\>Bullets On/Off \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Text Formatting\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\numbering_stop.xhp	0	help	par_id3148946	12			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>To remove numbering from a paragraph using the keyboard: \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\numbering_stop.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663	13			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Place the cursor at the beginning of a numbered paragraph and press the Backspace key. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\numbering_stop.xhp	0	help	par_id3150543	14			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The numbering of the paragraph disappears and is removed from the numbering sequence. Numbering resumes in the following paragraph. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\numbering_stop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123	15			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If you press the Enter key in an empty numbered paragraph, the numbering stops. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\numbering_stop.xhp	0	help	par_id3151043				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Bullets/Numbering\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	XML Form Documents (XForms)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	bm_id5215613				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>web documents;XForms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;XForms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XML Forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XForms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;XForms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;XForms\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E5				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xforms.xhp\"\>XML Form Documents (XForms)\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F5				0	gu	XForms are a new type of web form that was developed by the World Wide Web Consortium. The XForm model is defined in Extensible Markup Language (XML). The model uses separate sections to describe what a form does and what a form looks like. You can view the specification for XForms at: \<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/MarkUp/Forms/\"\>http://www.w3.org/MarkUp/Forms/\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	gu	Working with XForms				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074A				0	gu	In %PRODUCTNAME, an XForms document is a special type of Writer document. The Design Mode for an XForm document has additional toolbars and panes. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074D				0	gu	After you create and save an XForms document, you can open the document, fill out the form, and submit the changes to a server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	gu	To Create a New XForms Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070D				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - New - XML Form Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10714				0	gu	The XForms design window opens in an empty Writer document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10718				0	gu	Design your form.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071E				0	gu	Insert a control, select the default model in the property browser, and enter a binding statement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10722				0	gu	In the data navigator, add an element to the instance.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10726				0	gu	Load a new instance from an XML file and add controls to the relevant XML elements or attributes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10729				0	gu	To Open an XForms Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> and select the XForms document. An XForm document has the same extension as a Writer text document (*.odt).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	gu	To Edit an XForms Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073B				0	gu	Open the XForms document and use the following toolbars and windows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10757				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\"\>Form Controls toolbar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075F				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/xformsdata.xhp\"\>Data Navigator\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xforms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\"\>Form Navigator\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Creating Round Corners				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150040				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>corner roundings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rectangles with round corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>legends;rounding corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>round corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customizing;round corners\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	gu	\<variable id=\"round_corner\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/round_corner.xhp\" name=\"Creating Round Corners\"\>Creating Round Corners\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	gu	When you insert a rectangle or a callout box using the drawing functions and activate the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, you see a small frame at the upper left corner of the object. The frame indicates the amount by which the corners are rounded. When the frame is positioned at the top left corner, no rounding occurs. When the frame is positioned on the handle centered at the top of the object, the corners are rounded as much as possible. You adjust the degree of rounding by moving the frame between these two positions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3150774\" src=\"res/helpimg/hand01.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150774\"\>Mouse pointer as hand\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539				0	gu	If you place the cursor on the box it changes to a hand symbol. You can now drag the box to change the amount of rounding. An outline shows a preview of the result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Scripting %PRODUCTNAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	gu	\<variable id=\"scripting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/scripting.xhp\"\>Scripting %PRODUCTNAME\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	gu	You can assign custom scripts (macros) to menu items, icons, dialog controls, and events in %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072B				0	gu	%PRODUCTNAME internally supports the following scripting languages:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	gu	%PRODUCTNAME Basic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10739				0	gu	JavaScript				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073D				0	gu	BeanShell				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091F				0	gu	In addition, developers can use high-level languages, for example Java programming language, to control %PRODUCTNAME externally. See the API project at OpenOffice.org.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	gu	To assign a script to a new menu entry				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Menus\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093D				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Library\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	gu	You see entries for share (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), user (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	gu	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select a script.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10770				0	gu	A list of the script functions appears in the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> list box. Select a function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10783				0	gu	To assign a script to a key combination				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10787				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Keyboard\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A59				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Library\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A61				0	gu	You see entries for share (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), user (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A65				0	gu	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select a script.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A69				0	gu	A list of the script functions will appear in the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> list box. Select any function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A71				0	gu	Click the option button for %PRODUCTNAME or Writer (or whichever application is currently open). 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A74				0	gu	Selecting the option button sets the scope of the new key combination to be applicable in all of %PRODUCTNAME or only in documents of the current module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A78				0	gu	Select a key combination from the \<emph\>Shortcut keys\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078A				0	gu	To assign a script to an event				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078E				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Events\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A9E				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Library\</emph\> list box, scroll down and open the "%PRODUCTNAME Macros" entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AA6				0	gu	You see entries for share (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), user (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AAA				0	gu	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select a script.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AAE				0	gu	A list of the script functions will appear in the \<emph\>Assigned Macros\</emph\> list box. Select any function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AB6				0	gu	Select to save in %PRODUCTNAME or current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AB9				0	gu	This sets the scope of the new event assignment to be applicable in all of %PRODUCTNAME or only in documents of the current module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10791				0	gu	To assign a script to an event for an embedded object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10795				0	gu	Select the embedded object, for example a chart, in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10ADB				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Macro\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10ADF				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Macros\</emph\> list box, open the %PRODUCTNAME Scripts entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AE7				0	gu	You see entries for share (scripts in the share directory of your %PRODUCTNAME installation), user (scripts in the user directory), and the current document. Open any one of them to see the supported scripting languages.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AEB				0	gu	Open any scripting language entry to see the available scripts. Select a script.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AEF				0	gu	A list of the script functions will appear in the \<emph\>Existing macros in\</emph\> list box. Select any function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10798				0	gu	To assign a script to a hyperlink				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079C				0	gu	Position the cursor inside the hyperlink. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B15				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Hyperlink\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B19				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079F				0	gu	To assign a script to a graphic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A3				0	gu	Select the graphic in your document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B3B				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Picture - Macro\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	gu	To assign a script to a form control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AA				0	gu	Insert a form control, for example a button: Open the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon, drag open a button on your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B59				0	gu	With the form control selected, click \<emph\>Control\</emph\> on the Form Controls toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AD				0	gu	To assign a script to a control in the %PRODUCTNAME Basic dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B1				0	gu	Open the %PRODUCTNAME Basic dialog editor, then create a dialog with a control on it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\scripting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B7F				0	gu	Right-click the control, then choose \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Turning Extended Tips On and Off				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156414				0	gu	\<variable id=\"active_help_on_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/active_help_on_off.xhp\" name=\"Turning Extended Tips On and Off\"\>Turning Extended Tips On and Off\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	gu	\<emph\>Extended tips\</emph\> provide a brief description of the function of a particular icon, text box or menu command when you rest your cursor on that item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155339				0	gu	To turn Extended Tips on and off:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	gu	A check mark indicates that the extended tips are activated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	gu	To turn Extended Tips on temporarily:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	gu	Press the shortcut keys Shift+F1 to activate extended tips once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	gu	A question mark appears beside the mouse pointer. You can move this \<emph\>Help Mouse Pointer\</emph\> over all controls, icons and menu commands to obtain a description of the command. The \<emph\>Help Mouse Pointer\</emph\> is disabled the next time you click the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	gu	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	gu	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> from being modified, deleted or viewed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	gu	Protecting All Documents When Saving				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box. Save the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	gu	Open the document, entering the correct password. Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	gu	Information entered in \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\> is not encrypted. This includes the name of the author, creation date, word and character counts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294				0	gu	Protecting Revision Marking				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3161646				0	gu	With every change made in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, the review function records who made the change. This function can be turned on with protection, so that it can only be turned off when the correct password is entered. Until then, all changes will continue to be recorded. Acceptance or rejection of changes is not possible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter the correct password.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155113				0	gu	Protecting Frames, Graphics, and OLE Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153703				0	gu	You can protect the content, position and size of inserted graphics. The same applies to frames (in Writer) and OLE objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	gu	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> and/or \<emph\>Size\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153657				0	gu	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, unmark as appropriate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152992				0	gu	Protecting Drawing Objects and Form Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429	59			0	gu	The draw objects that you insert into your documents with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar can be protected from being accidentally moved or changed in size. You can do the same with form objects inserted with the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148815	61			0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Mark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	63			0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Unmark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	gu	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_table.xhp\" name=\"Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\"\>Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	gu	Open both the text document and the spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	gu	Select the sheet area you want to copy.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827				0	gu	Point to the selected area and press the mouse button. Keep the mouse button pressed for a moment, then drag the area into the text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	gu	Once the cursor is located in the place where you want to insert the sheet area, release the mouse button. The sheet area is inserted as an OLE object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047				0	gu	You can select and edit the OLE object at any time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	gu	To edit the OLE object, double-click on it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155389				0	gu	Alternatively, select the object and choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Edit\</emph\> or choose \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> from the context menu. You edit the object in its own frame within the text document, but you see the icons and menu commands needed for spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to open the source document of the OLE object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Changing Your Work Directory				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>work directory change\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>My Documents folder;changing work directory\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paths; changing work directory\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; changing paths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;work directory\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	gu	\<variable id=\"workfolder\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/workfolder.xhp\" name=\"Changing Your Work Directory\"\>Changing Your Work Directory\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	gu	When you start a dialog to open or save a document, $[officename] initially displays your work directory. To change this directory:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802	5			0	gu	Click \<emph\>My Documents \</emph\>and click the\<emph\> Edit button, or \</emph\>double-click on \<emph\>My Documents\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Select Path\</emph\> dialog, choose the work directory you want and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Paths\"\>Paths\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053D				0	gu	Creating an XML Filter for %PRODUCTNAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109A9				0	gu	When you create an XML filter for %PRODUCTNAME, you need to design an \<emph\>XSLT stylesheet\</emph\> that can convert to and from the OpenDocument XML file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B0				0	gu	For more information about the OpenDocument XML format, go to \<link href=\"http://xml.openoffice.org/\"\>http://xml.openoffice.org/\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C5				0	gu	If you want, you can include a \<emph\>template\</emph\> with your filter to apply %PRODUCTNAME styles to an XML document that you import.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CC				0	gu	You can also include the \<emph\>Document Type Definition\</emph\> (DTD) for the for the external XML format so you can validate the XML format, for example, when you test the filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10531				0	gu	To create an XML filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E0				0	gu	Create an XSLT transformation \<emph\>stylesheet\</emph\> that maps the elements of the external XML format to the elements of the OpenDocument XML file format and back again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E8				0	gu	Create a template that assigns %PRODUCTNAME styles to elements in the external XML format when you import a file in this format into %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	gu	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, create a text document, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109F4				0	gu	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109FC				0	gu	In the \<emph\>XML Filter\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and define the properties of the filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A03				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Filter Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the XML filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CA1				0	gu	This name is displayed in the \<emph\>XML Filter Settings\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A09				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Application\</emph\> box, select the %PRODUCTNAME application that the filter is for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0F				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Name of File Type\</emph\> box, enter the file type that the filter is for.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	gu	This name is displayed in the list of file types in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\>, \<emph\>Export\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialogs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A15				0	gu	In the \<emph\>File extension\</emph\> box, enter the extension for the exported file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1B				0	gu	To differentiate the file from other XML files, enter an extension other than *.xml.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1F				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page, define the transformation properties for the filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	gu	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DocType\</emph\> box, enter the document type identifier for the external file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D0E				0	gu	This identifier is used to detect the file type on import.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A2C				0	gu	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DTD\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the DTD for the external file format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D1F				0	gu	This DTD is used to validate the files on export.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A32				0	gu	In the \<emph\>XSLT for export\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from OpenDocument format to the external format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A38				0	gu	In the \<emph\>XSLT for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name to the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from the external format to OpenDocument format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A3E				0	gu	(Optional) In the \<emph\>Template for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and name of the template that defines the %PRODUCTNAME styles that are used in the imported file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A44				0	gu	The files that are specified on the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page are copied to the local %PRODUCTNAME users directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A4C				0	gu	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A56				0	gu	To test an XML filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A5A				0	gu	You can perform basic tests on a custom XML filter in %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A91				0	gu	The document is not altered by these tests. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A60				0	gu	Create or open a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A67				0	gu	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A6F				0	gu	In the list of filters, select the filter that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Text XSLTs\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A82				0	gu	To test an \<emph\>Export\</emph\> Filter, do one of the following in the \<emph\>Export\</emph\> area of the dialog:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DEB				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>, select the %PRODUCTNAME document that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DF7				0	gu	To test the current document, click \<emph\>Current Document\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A99				0	gu	To test an \<emph\>Import\</emph\> Filter, click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> area of the dialog, select a document, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E32				0	gu	To validate the transformed file against the specified DTD, click \<emph\>Validate\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Printing with Reduced Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	gu	\<variable id=\"print_faster\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/print_faster.xhp\"\>Printing faster with Reduced Data\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C8				0	gu	You can decide to reduce the data necessary to print your document. The settings can be defined differently for printing directly to the printer or for printing to a file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D6				0	gu	Click one of the following settings options: 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	gu	\<emph\>Printer\</emph\>\<emph\>- \</emph\>to define options for reducing data while printing directly to a printer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E2				0	gu	\<emph\>Print to file\</emph\>\<emph\>-\</emph\> to define options for reducing data while printing to a file				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	gu	Select any combination of the four options, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EF				0	gu	All documents that you print from now on will use the changed options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F3				0	gu	Print your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	gu	You can reduce data for transparency, for gradients, or for bitmaps. When you reduce the data, on many printers you will not see a reduction of printing quality. But the printing time is substantially shorter, and when you print to a file, the file size is much smaller.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\print_faster.xhp	0	help	par_idN10704				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010900.xhp\"\>Print options\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
