helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3148453				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Standard file format\</emph\> area, first select a document type, then select the file type for saving.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807	18			0	gu	From now on, if you save a document, the \<emph\>File type \</emph\>will be set according to your choice. Of course, you still can select another file type in the file save dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	gu	Opening Microsoft Office Files by Default				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153092				0	gu	Converting Many Microsoft Office Files into OpenDocument Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	gu	The \<emph\>Document Converter Wizard\</emph\> will copy and convert all Microsoft Office files in a folder into $[officename] documents in the OpenDocument file format. You can specify the folder to be read, and the folder where the converted files are to be saved.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3150486				0	gu	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01130000.xhp\" name=\"File - AutoPilot - Document Converter\"\>\<emph\>File - Wizards - Document Converter\</emph\>\</link\> to start the wizard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154319				0	gu	Macros in Microsoft Office and $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3154921				0	gu	Microsoft Office and $[officename] cannot run the same macro code. Microsoft Office uses VBA (Visual Basic for Applications) code, and $[officename] uses Basic code based on the $[officename] API (Application Program Interface) environment. Although the programming language is the same, the objects and methods are different.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	gu	If you use macros in one of the applications and want to use the same functionality in the other application, you must edit the macros. $[officename] can load the macros that are contained within Microsoft Office files and you can then view and edit the macro code in the $[officename] \<link href=\"text/shared/main0600.xhp\" name=\"Basic IDE\"\>Basic IDE\</link\> editor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	gu	You can choose to preserve or delete VBA macros				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	gu	Open a Microsoft Office document that contains VBA macro code. Change only the normal contents (text, cells, graphics), and do not edit the macros. Save the document as a Microsoft Office file type. Open the file in Microsoft Office, and the VBA macros will run as before.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_user.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	gu	You may delete the VBA macros from the Microsoft Office file on loading or on saving.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Drawing Lines in Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143206				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>arrows; drawing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indicator lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; drawing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; removing automatic lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting; lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic lines/borders in text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143206				0	gu	\<variable id=\"line_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/line_intext.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Lines in Text\"\>Drawing Lines in Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3144436				0	gu	You can incorporate lines into your text with custom angles, width, color, and other attributes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	gu	To define the line attributes and direction, use the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> drawing object as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400	41			0	gu	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Show Draw Functions \</emph\>icon to open the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar, and click the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> icon. The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol with a line beside it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	gu	In your document, click where the line should begin. Hold down the mouse button and drag to the point where you want the line to end. If you also hold down the Shift key, you can draw only horizontal, vertical, and diagonal lines.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361	43			0	gu	Release the mouse button once the line has the desired direction and length. You can then draw more lines. End this function by pressing the Esc key or by clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon from the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	gu	૪.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	gu	After clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon, you can select all of the lines at the same time by clicking each line while holding down the Shift key. This multiple selection enables you to assign all of them a common color, width or other attribute.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	gu	Create a horizontal line by applying the preset Paragraph Style \<emph\>Horizontal Line\</emph\>. Click into an empty paragraph, and double-click the \<emph\>Horizontal Line\</emph\> Style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. If the entry for horizontal lines is not visible in the list of Paragraph Styles, select "All Styles" in the lower listbox.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	gu	To undo an automatic border replacement once, choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E0				0	gu	To disable the automatic borders, choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect - Options\</emph\> and clear \<emph\>Apply border\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145787				0	gu	The lines and other drawing objects that you insert in text are not defined in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\>, and are therefore not exported directly into HTML format. Instead, they are exported as graphics.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154188				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Borders\"\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting and Editing Tab Stops				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144436				0	gu	\<variable id=\"tabs\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/tabs.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Tab Stops\"\>Inserting and Editing Tab Stops\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id1376079				0	gu	On the horizontal ruler you can see the tab stops for the current paragraph. If you want to change the tab stops, you should first consider the scope to which you want to change tab stops as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id274971				0	gu	Change the tab stops for all paragraphs using the current Paragraph Style: Right-click the paragraph to open the context menu, choose \<emph\>Edit Paragraph Style\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Tabs\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id5199133				0	gu	Change the tab stops for one or more paragraphs: Select the paragraphs, then click inside the ruler.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id6178167				0	gu	In the following, you find instructions for all above mentioned tasks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	27			0	gu	You can set a tab stop by clicking on the ruler or by selecting \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Tabs.\</emph\> Both methods affect the current paragraph or all selected paragraphs.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	gu	Click the ruler once to set a left-justified tab. Right-click a tab icon on the ruler to see the context menu in which you can change the tab type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	gu	To set several decimal tabs one after the other, keep clicking the icon to the left of the ruler until the desired tab type is shown, then click on the ruler.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153349				0	gu	પસંદગી				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153254				0	gu	વર્ણન:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	gu	Setting left tabs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	gu	Setting right tabs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3151043				0	gu	Setting decimal tabs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153091				0	gu	Setting centered tabs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3154150				0	gu	Double-click the ruler to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030300.xhp\" name=\"Paragraph\"\>\<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3154145				0	gu	Double-click the white area of the ruler to set one tab. The \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\> dialog appears with the \<emph\>Tabs\</emph\> tab page open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	gu	Moving Tabs on the Ruler				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145264				0	gu	Move individual tab stops on the ruler using the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156				0	gu	To move several tab stops on the ruler, press the Shift key before you click a tab. Drag one tab while continuing to press Shift to move that tab as well as all the tabs to the right of it. The spacing between those tabs remains the same.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3147349	23			0	gu	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you drag a tab on the ruler to move that tab and all the tabs to the right of it. This results in the spacing between those tabs changing proportionally to their distance from the margin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146146				0	gu	Changing the Properties of Tabs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145646				0	gu	To change tab type, click the tab you want to change on the ruler, then right-click to open the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729				0	gu	Deleting Tabs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3148879				0	gu	To delete a tab, hold down the mouse button while you drag the tab outside the ruler.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151074				0	gu	Changing the Defaults				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3151059				0	gu	If you want to change the settings of your default tab stops, you will find further information under \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Text Document - General\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Spreadsheet - General\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070500.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Drawing - General\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Draw - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070500.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Presentation - General\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options - (module name) - General\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	gu	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\> of the ruler allows you to change the displayed units of measurement. These changes are only valid until you exit $[officename], and they only apply to the ruler on whose context menu you made the change. If you want to change the ruler measurement units permanently, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - [Document type] - View\</emph\> and change the measurement unit there.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3148429				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/swriter/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Ruler\"\>Ruler\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\background.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149581				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select a background color or a background graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154097				0	gu	This background appears only in the print behind the cells not formatted elsewhere.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156180				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030600.xhp\" name=\"Background tab page\"\>\<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154136				0	gu	\<variable id=\"insert_bitmap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_bitmap.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\"\>Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	gu	Inserting Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	gu	A bitmap image can be inserted in $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236				0	gu	Select the file. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box you can restrict the selection to certain file types.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box if you want a link to the original file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	gu	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is marked, whenever the document is updated and loaded the bitmap image is reloaded. The editing steps that you have carried out in the local copy of the image in the document are re-applied and the image is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	gu	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is not marked, you are always working with the copy created when the graphic was first inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	gu	To embed graphics that were first inserted as links, go to \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Break Link\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303				0	gu	Editing Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	gu	When you select the bitmap image, the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar offers you the tools for editing the image. Only a local copy is edited in the document, even if you have inserted an image as a link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	gu	The \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar may look slightly different depending to the module you are using.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	gu	In $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Image, you can add text and graphics, select these objects together with the bitmap, and export the selection as a new bitmap image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153574				0	gu	Saving Bitmaps				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	gu	Select the bitmap image. You can also select additional objects, such as text, to be exported with the image by pressing the shift key while selecting or by opening a selection frame around all objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	gu	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> field, select the file format you want, for example GIF or JPEG.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	gu	If you only want to export the selected objects, mark the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150874				0	gu	If \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not marked, the entire page of the document is exported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417				0	gu	Enter a name for the file and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Pasting Contents in Special Formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10725				0	gu	\<variable id=\"pasting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pasting.xhp\"\>Pasting Contents in Special Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	gu	Contents that are stored on the clipboard can be pasted into your document using different formats. In %PRODUCTNAME you can choose how to paste the contents using a dialog or a drop-down icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	gu	The available options depend on the contents of the clipboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	gu	Pasting clipboard contents using an icon menu				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	gu	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard Bar to open the menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	gu	Select one of the options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	gu	If you do not like the result, click the \<emph\>Undo\</emph\> icon and then paste again with another option.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10762				0	gu	Pasting clipboard contents using a dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10769				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10771				0	gu	Select one of the options and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	gu	If you are in a spreadsheet and the contents of the clipboard are spreadsheet cells, then a different \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears. Use the \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog to copy cells using basic or advanced options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	gu	\<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>: swaps the rows and the columns of the cell range to be pasted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	gu	\<emph\>Link\</emph\>: pastes the cell range as a link. If the source file changes, the pasted cells change also.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	gu	The other options are explained in the help, when you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\> dialog from within %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BA				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Relative and Absolute Links				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>absolute hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; relative and absolute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks, see also links\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	gu	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_rel_abs\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp\" name=\"Relative and Absolute Links\"\>Relative and Absolute Links\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	gu	When you include hyperlinks, two factors must be taken into account: whether they are set as relative or absolute on saving, and whether or not the file is present.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3159158				0	gu	An absolute path such as "C:\\homepage\\graphics\\picture.gif" would no longer function on the provider server. Neither a server nor the computer of a reader needs to have a C hard drive: operating systems such as Unix or MacOS do not recognize drive letters, and even if the folder homepage\\graphics existed, your picture would not be available. It is better to use relative addressing for file links.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	gu	A link to a web page, for example, "www.sun.com" or "www.myprovider.com/mypage/index.htm" is an absolute link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450				0	gu	$[officename] also reacts differently, depending on whether the file referred to in the link exists, and where it is located. $[officename] checks every new link and sets a target and protocol automatically. The result can be seen in the generated HTML code after saving the source document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145317				0	gu	The following rules apply: A relative reference ("graphic/picture.gif") is only possible when both files exist on the same drive. If the files are on different drives in your local file system, the absolute reference follows the "file:" protocol ("file:///data1/xyz/picture.gif"). If the files are on different servers or if the target of the link is not available, the absolute reference uses the "http:" protocol ("http://data2/abc/picture.gif").				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	gu	Be sure to organize all files for your homepage on the same drive as the start file of the homepage. In this way, $[officename] can set the protocol and target so that the reference on the server is always correct.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_rel_abs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153897				0	gu	When you rest your mouse on a hyperlink, a help tip displays the absolute reference, since $[officename] uses absolute path names internally. The complete path and address can only be seen when you view the result of the HTML export, by loading the HTML file as "Text" or opening it with a text editor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Searching Tables and Form Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	bm_id4066896				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>finding;records in form documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;finding records\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching;tables and forms\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154186				0	gu	\<variable id=\"data_search\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_search.xhp\" name=\"Searching Tables and Form Documents\"\>Searching Tables and Form Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3153311\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_recsearch.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153311\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149178	65			0	gu	In spreadsheets and documents in which form controls are used, you can click the \<emph\>Find Record\</emph\> icon on the form bar to open a dialog to find any text and values. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	gu	You can search in one or in all data fields. You can select whether the text must be at the beginning, end or any location of the data field. You also can use the ? and * wildcards, as in the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog. You can find additional information about the database search function in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>labels; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>business cards; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>synchronizing;labels and business cards\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	gu	\<variable id=\"labels\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels.xhp\" name=\"Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\"\>Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	gu	Designing Business Cards Through a Dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798	70			0	gu	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Business Cards\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Business Cards\</emph\>\</link\> to open the\<emph\> Business Cards \</emph\>dialog, which allows you to choose how your business cards will look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147654				0	gu	Designing Labels and Business Cards				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	gu	You can design both labels and business cards through the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	gu	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010200.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Labels\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, define the label format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	gu	$[officename] Writer contains many formats of commercially available sheets for labels, badges, and business cards. You can also add other, user-defined formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Inscription\</emph\>, you can choose what you want written on the labels.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	gu	This often involves database fields, so that the labels can be printed with varying content, when sending "Form Letters" for example. It is also possible to have the same text printed on every label.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	85			0	gu	Use the \<emph\>Database \</emph\>and \<emph\>Table \</emph\>list boxes to select the database and table from which the data fields are obtained. Click on the arrow button to transfer the selected data field into the inscription area. Press Enter to insert a line break. You can also enter spaces and any other fixed text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> tab you can define your own label formats, not covered by the predefined formats. To do this, select "User" from the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list box. On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, you can specify whether all labels or only certain ones are to be created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, make sure that the \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> box is selected. If this is selected, a label only has to be entered (on the top left label) and edited once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	gu	As soon as you click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, you will see a small window with the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button. Enter the first label. When you click on the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button, the current individual label is copied to all the other labels on the sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767				0	gu	Click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\> to create a new document with the settings you have entered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Business Cards\"\>Business Cards\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Mobile Devices Filters for Pocket Device Appliances				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147143				0	gu	\<variable id=\"mobiledevicefilters\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/mobiledevicefilters.xhp\" name=\"Mobile Devices Filters for Pocket Device Appliances\"\>Mobile Devices Filters for Pocket Device Appliances\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	gu	You can save and open documents to and from several mobile devices file formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	gu	Currently the following filters are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	gu	AportisDoc for Palm OS compatible devices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	gu	Pocket Excel for Pocket PC compatible devices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	gu	Pocket Word for Pocket PC compatible devices				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	gu	Installing the Pocket PC filters under Windows will also install a DLL file that supports the synchronize software of your Pocket PC.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	gu	The Java Runtime Environment is required to use the mobile device filters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153665				0	gu	Installing the mobile devices filters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	gu	If you are using the Windows opearating system with ActiveSync installed, disconnect any Pocket PC device from ActiveSync.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153061				0	gu	Start the $[officename] Setup program:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E7				0	gu	Open the Windows \<emph\>Start\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>, double-click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>, select the %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION entry, click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	gu	In Setup, choose the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	gu	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry, then open the \<emph\>Mobile Device Filters\</emph\> entry. Select the filters you want to install.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>, \<emph\>Next\</emph\>, \<emph\>Install\</emph\>, \<emph\>Finish\</emph\> to install the filters and exit the Setup program.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154123				0	gu	Saving $[officename] documents for a mobile device				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	gu	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	gu	Opening mobile device documents in $[officename]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	gu	Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159196				0	gu	Synchronizing file types				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	gu	To convert Pocket PC formats to and from $[officename] formats, you must first change some options within ActiveSync. To do this, open the ActiveSync window and open its Options dialog. Perform the following steps:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149064				0	gu	Select the \<emph\>Rules\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Conversion Settings\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154145				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Device to Desktop\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	gu	Select \<emph\>Pocket Word Document - Pocket PC\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638	29			0	gu	In the drop down list of available conversions, select \<emph\>$[officename] Writer \</emph\>and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	gu	Repeat steps 4 and 5 for \<emph\>Pocket Excel Workbook\</emph\> selecting \<emph\>$[officename] Calc\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\mobiledevicefilters.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	gu	After these steps you can copy documents between $[officename] and your Pocket PC, either by the ActiveSync software or by the Windows Explorer. The filters will be applied to the document files automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394				0	gu	\<variable id=\"copy_drawfunctions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copy_drawfunctions.xhp\" name=\"Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\"\>Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	28			0	gu	In $[officename] it is possible to copy drawing objects between text, spreadsheets and presentation documents. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	gu	Select the drawing object or objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	gu	Copy the drawing object to the clipboard, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	gu	Switch to the other document and place the cursor where the drawing object is to be inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	gu	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573				0	gu	Inserting into a text document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	gu	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current paragraph. You can change the anchor by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar. This opens a popup menu where you can select the anchor type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	gu	Inserting into a spreadsheet				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	30			0	gu	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current cell. You can change the anchor between cell and page by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149456\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleanchortype.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149456\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156410				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>start parameters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>command line parameters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>parameters;command line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arguments in command line\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147009				0	gu	By starting the $[officename] software from the command line you can assign various parameters, with which you can influence the performance. The use of command line parameters is only recommended for experienced users.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	gu	For normal handling, the use of command line parameters is not necessary. A few of the parameters require a deeper knowledge of the technical background of the $[officename] software technology.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898				0	gu	Starting the $[officename] Software From the Command Line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156152				0	gu	Under Windows, select \<emph\>Run\</emph\> from the Windows Start menu, or open a Shell under UNIX® based platforms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472	6			0	gu	Under Windows, type the following text in the \<emph\>Open \</emph\>text field and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	gu	Under UNIX based systems, type the following line of text, then press \<emph\>Return\</emph\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147561	7			0	gu	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>{install}\\program\\soffice.exe {parameter} \</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>{install}/program/soffice {parameter} \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	gu	Replace \<emph\>{install}\</emph\> with the path to your installation of the $[officename] software (for example, \<emph\>C:\\Program Files\\Office\</emph\>, or \<emph\>~/office\</emph\>)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407				0	gu	Where required, replace \<emph\>{parameter}\</emph\> with one or more of the following command line parameters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	gu	Valid Command Line Parameters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
