helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\flat_icons.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Changing Icon Views				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\flat_icons.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145669				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>buttons; big/small\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views; icons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>icon sizes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;icon sizes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>large icons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>small icons\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\flat_icons.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145669				0	gu	\<variable id=\"flat_icons\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/flat_icons.xhp\" name=\"Changing Icon Views\"\>Changing Icon Size\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\flat_icons.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	gu	You can change the icon view between small and large icons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\flat_icons.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	gu	On the \<emph\>View\</emph\> tab page, select the \<emph\>Toolbar icon size\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\flat_icons.xhp	0	help	par_id3157909				0	gu	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting and Editing Buttons				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	gu	\<variable id=\"formfields\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/formfields.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Buttons\"\>Adding a Command Button to a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	gu	You can use the Form Controls toolbar to add checkboxes, buttons, tables showing data records, and other controls to a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077F				0	gu	To Add a Button to a Document 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	gu	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	gu	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A4				0	gu	The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	gu	In the document, drag to draw the button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	gu	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CD				0	gu	Specify the properties of the button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	gu	To change the button label, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and edit the text in the \<emph\>Label\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303	12			0	gu	To attach a macro to the button, click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab, and click the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button beside the button action that you want to run the macro. In the \<emph\>Assign Macro\</emph\> dialog, locate the macro that you want to use, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10814				0	gu	Close the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147350				0	gu	(Optional) Specify the properties of the form that the button belongs to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	gu	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Form\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	gu	The \<emph\>Form Properties\</emph\> dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	gu	Specify the properties for the form and then close the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156426				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>faxes; sending\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faxes;configuring $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sending; documents as faxes \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>configuring;fax icon\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156426				0	gu	\<variable id=\"fax\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/fax.xhp\" name=\"Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\"\>Sending Faxes and Configuring $[officename] for Faxing\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	gu	To send a fax directly from $[officename], you need a fax modem and a fax driver that allows applications to communicate with the fax modem.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410				0	gu	Sending a Fax Through the Print Dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	gu	Open the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog by choosing \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\> and select the fax driver in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135				0	gu	Clicking \<emph\>OK\</emph\> opens the dialog for your fax driver, where you can select the fax recipient.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	gu	Configuring $[officename] a Fax Icon				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822				0	gu	You can configure $[officename] so that a single click on an icon automatically sends the current document as a fax:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	gu	Select the fax driver from the \<emph\>Fax\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EB				0	gu	Click the arrow icon at the end of the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar. In the drop-down menu, choose \<emph\>Customize\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F6				0	gu	The \<emph\>Toolbar\</emph\>s tab page of the \<emph\>Customize\</emph\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FA				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	gu	Select the "Documents" category, then select the "Send Default Fax" command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10712				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Toolbars\</emph\> tab page, click the down arrow button to position the new icon where you want it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fax.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	gu	Your \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar now has a new icon to send the current document as a fax.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Registering and Deleting a Database 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	gu	\<variable id=\"data_register\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_register.xhp\"\>Registering and Deleting a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	gu	Data from any \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> can be registered to %PRODUCTNAME. To register means to tell %PRODUCTNAME where the data is located, how it is organized, how to get that data, and more. Once the database is registered, you can use the menu command \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to access the data records from your text documents and spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	gu	To register an existing database file:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E1				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and select the database file. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	gu	To remove a registered database from %PRODUCTNAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10719				0	gu	Select the database file and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
