helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	gu	You can define any object to be included in the list of available line ends.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	gu	Use the draw functions to create an object to be used as a line end.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	gu	In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Arrow Styles\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3149765				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and assign a name to the new arrow style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> to close the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
