helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Selecting Measurement Units				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>documents;measurement units in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>measurement units;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>units;measurement units\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>centimeters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inches\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distances\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;measurement units\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201				0	gu	\<variable id=\"measurement_units\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/measurement_units.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Measurement Units\"\>Selecting Measurement Units\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	gu	You can select separate measurement units for $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Writer/Web, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Impress and $[officename] Draw documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	gu	Open a document of the type for which you want to change the measurement units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	gu	In the left pane of the dialog, double-click the application for which you want to select the measurement unit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	gu	Double-click \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> if you want to select the measurement units for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	gu	Click on \<emph\>General\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	gu	On the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page, select the measurement unit. Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp\" name=\"Entering measurement units directly\"\>Entering measurement units directly\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Working with Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	gu	\<variable id=\"data_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tables.xhp\"\>Working with Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	gu	Data is stored in tables. As an example, your system address book that you use for your e-mail addresses is a table of the address book database. Each address is a data record, presented as a row in that table. The data records consist of data fields, for example the first and the last name fields and the e-mail field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	gu	Creating a New Table With the Table Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	gu	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new table using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/tablewizard00.xhp\"\>Table Wizard\</link\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	gu	Open the database file where you want to create the new table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	gu	In the database file window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Table\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	gu	Creating a New Table With the Design View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	gu	Open the database file where you want to create the new table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	gu	In the database file window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Create Table in Design View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	gu	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\"\>Table Design\</link\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	gu	Creating a New Table View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077C				0	gu	Some database types support table views. A table view is a query that is stored with the database. For most database operations, a view can be used as you would use a table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10782				0	gu	Open the database file where you want to create the new table view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	gu	In the database file window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078E				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Create Table View\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10795				0	gu	You see the View Design window, which is almost the same as the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\"\>Query Design window\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting Objects From the Gallery				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145136	1			0	gu	\<variable id=\"gallery_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/gallery_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Objects From the Gallery\"\>Inserting Objects From the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	gu	You can insert an object in a document either as a \<emph\>copy\</emph\> or as a \<emph\>link\</emph\>. A copy of an object is independent of the original object. Changes to the original object have no effect on the copy. A link remains dependent on the original object. Changes to the original object are also reflected in the link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	gu	Inserting an object as a copy				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154516				0	gu	Select an object using a single click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	gu	Drag the object into the document, or right-click to open the context menu and select \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and \<emph\>Copy\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061				0	gu	Inserting an object as a link				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150543				0	gu	Select an object using a single click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156282				0	gu	Inserting an object as a background graphic				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145607				0	gu	Select an object using a single click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3147289				0	gu	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Insert - Background - Page\</emph\> or \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145787				0	gu	Inserting an object as a texture (pattern) for another object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\gallery_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148617				0	gu	Select an object using a single click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Using the Filter Navigator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150322				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>filters; Navigator\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filter conditions;connecting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	gu	\<variable id=\"filternavigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/filternavigator.xhp\"\>Using the Filter Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3150322				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterNavigator\"\>To connect several filter conditions with Boolean OR, click the \<emph\>Filter navigation\</emph\> icon on the filter bar.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> window appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FILTER_NAVIGATOR\"\>The filter conditions that have been set appear in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. As soon as a filter is set, you see a blank filter entry at the bottom of the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\> . You can select this entry by clicking the word "Or". Once you have selected the blank filter entry, you can enter additional filter conditions in the form. These conditions are linked by Boolean OR to the previously defined conditions.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\filternavigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3145620				0	gu	The context menu can be called for each entry in the \<emph\>Filter navigator\</emph\>. \<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_FILTER_IS_NOT_NULL\"\>You can edit the filter conditions in this area directly as text. If you wish to check if a field has content or no content, you can select the filter conditions "empty" (SQL:"Is Null") or "not empty" (SQL: "Is not Null").\</ahelp\> It is also possible to delete the entry by using the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Integrating new UNO components				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149760				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>add-ons, see UNO components\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>UNO components;integrating new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;UNO components\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149760				0	gu	\<variable id=\"integratinguno\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/integratinguno.xhp\" name=\"Integrating new UNO components\"\>Integrating new UNO components\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	gu	Programmers can write and integrate their own UNO (Universal Network Objects) components to $[officename]. Those new components can be added to the $[officename] menus and toolbars; we call them "Add-Ons".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	gu	The integration of new components is supported by some tools and services. Details can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide. The three main steps are as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	3			0	gu	Register the new components within $[officename]. This can be accomplished using the tool \<item type=\"literal\"\>unopkg\</item\>, which can be found in {installpath}\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>/ \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\\\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>program.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	gu	Integrate the new components as services. The ProtocolHandler and JobDispatch services assist you; more information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	gu	Change the user interface (menus or toolbars). This can be done almost automatically by writing an XML text file that describes the changes. More information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	gu	The Add-Ons can extend the functionality of $[officename]. They are not related to the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Add-Ins\"\>Add-Ins\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Add-Ins\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> that provide new functions for $[officename] Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Applying Line Styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153884				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>separator lines; defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reference lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arrows; defining arrow lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>line styles; applying\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153884				0	gu	\<variable id=\"linestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/linestyles.xhp\" name=\"Applying Line Styles Using the Toolbar\"\>Applying Line Styles Using the Toolbar\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	gu	The \<emph\>Drawing Object Properties\</emph\> toolbar contains icons and combo boxes to define various line attributes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068	6			0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3144510\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatline.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3144510\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D6				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Arrow Styles\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id5858221\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_lineendstyle.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5858221\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to select an arrow style for the right and left ends of a line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	gu	Select a style from the \<emph\>Line Style\</emph\> box and specify the width in the \<emph\>Line Width\</emph\> box. A width of 0 corresponds to 1 pixel.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	gu	Select the line and arrow color in the \<emph\>Line Color\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Searching for Attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	bm_id5681020				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>fonts;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>font attributes;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes;finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>attributes; finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding; attributes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;Find & Replace mode\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	gu	\<variable id=\"find_attributes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/find_attributes.xhp\"\>Searching for Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	gu	You can search for text with attributes that are applied either by direct formatting or by styles. For example, if you search for the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> attribute, all instances of text that do not use the default font are found. All text that has a directly coded font attribute, and all text where a style switches the font attribute, are found.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	gu	If you want to find text with any font by name, click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\"\>Find & Replace\</link\> dialog of %PRODUCTNAME Writer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	gu	After you select the attributes that you want to search for, the \<emph\>Search for Styles\</emph\> box in the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>area of the %PRODUCTNAME Writer \<emph\>Find & Replace \</emph\>dialog changes to \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	gu	If you want to search for text in which attributes were set by using direct formatting and styles, select the \<emph\>Including Styles\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\find_attributes.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	gu	The search criteria for attributes are listed below the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
