helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152594				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>properties;files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files;properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;file properties\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152594				0	gu	\<variable id=\"viewing_file_properties\"\>\<variable id=\"viewing\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/viewing_file_properties.xhp\" name=\"Viewing File Properties\"\>Viewing File Properties\</link\>\</variable\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	gu	File properties, such as author name, subject, and keywords, help you manage and identify your documents. $[officename] also tracks file statistics, including the number of words and the number of pages in a document, and automatically adds the statistics as part of the file property.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834				0	gu	You can view file properties for the current document\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\> or for a document in the Windows File Open dialog \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233				0	gu	To view file properties for the current document:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3153311				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150443				0	gu	To view file properties for a document listed in the Windows File Open dialog				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	gu	Select a file in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	gu	Right-click and choose\<emph\> Properties\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting Charts				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910				0	gu	\<variable id=\"chart_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/chart_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Charts\"\>Inserting Charts\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7211218				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Insert Chart\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7236243				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Macro\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Fontwork For Graphical Text Art				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066D				0	gu	\<variable id=\"fontwork\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/fontwork.xhp\"\>Fontwork For Graphical Text Art\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068B				0	gu	You can use Fontwork to create graphical text art objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10691				0	gu	To create a Fontwork object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Fontwork Gallery\</emph\> dialog, select a Fontwork style and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	gu	Double-click the object to enter text edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	gu	Replace the default Fontwork text with your own text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A8				0	gu	Press Esc to exit text edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AE				0	gu	To edit a Fontwork object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B8				0	gu	The \<link href=\"text/shared/fontwork_toolbar.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar is displayed. If you do not see the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> toolbar, choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Fontwork\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BC				0	gu	Click an icon in the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN10839				0	gu	The following icons are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	gu	Fontwork Gallery - adds another Fontwork object				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C9				0	gu	Fontwork Shape - edits the shape				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	gu	Fontwork Same Letter Heights - changes the height of characters				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	gu	Fontwork Alignment - aligns the text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D9				0	gu	Fontwork Character Spacing - changes the character spacing and kerning				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CA				0	gu	To edit more Fontwork attributes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D5				0	gu	Select the properties from the \<emph\>Drawing Object Properties\</emph\> toolbar. You can change the line width, line color, fill color, fill style, and more.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\fontwork.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E7				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/fontwork_toolbar.xhp\"\>Fontwork toolbar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Drawing\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, if it is not already open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	gu	Drawing objects can be subsequently edited and modified. Drawing objects created in this way are vector graphics, which you can scale freely without any loss of quality.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	gu	To create a rectangle, click the rectangle icon and move your cursor to the place in the document where you want one corner of the rectangle to be. Press the mouse button and hold it down while dragging to the opposite corner of the rectangle. When you release the mouse button, the rectangle is inserted in the document. It is selected, and you can edit its properties through the context menu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626				0	gu	To scale the objects, first select them by clicking on them with the selection tool. You then see eight handles around the object. When you drag one of the four corner handles, the opposite corner remains fixed while the other three corners move. When you drag one of the side handles, the opposite side remains fixed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Information about the individual icons\"\>Information about the individual icons\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Editing Hyperlinks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153910				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; editing hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;hyperlink text/formats/URLs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>buttons;editing hyperlink buttons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL;changing hyperlink URLs\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910				0	gu	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Hyperlinks\"\>Editing Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	gu	Change the text of a hyperlink as follows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158432				0	gu	Change the URL of a hyperlink as follows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	gu	Option 1: As described above, open \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Dialog\"\>Hyperlink Dialog\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	gu	Option 2: Open \<link href=\"text/shared/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Bar\"\>Hyperlink Bar\</link\> (\<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>). Click on the hyperlink, do not release the mouse button and drag the hyperlink to the Hyperlink Bar. Edit the URL on the Hyperlink Bar and press the Return key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148686				0	gu	Change the attribute of all hyperlinks				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	gu	Open the Styles and Formatting window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10826				0	gu	Click the Character Styles icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	gu	Right-click the "Internet Link" or "Visited Internet Link" character style, and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	gu	In the dialog, select the new attributes, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147530				0	gu	Edit a hyperlink button				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361				0	gu	If the hyperlink is a button, click on the border to select it, or press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while clicking. Open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog through the context menu. You can edit the label text under "Caption," and modify the address in the "URL" field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Changing Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154285				0	gu	\<variable id=\"standard_template\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/standard_template.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Templates\"\>Changing Default Templates\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	gu	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customized Styles or other contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	gu	Modifying Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	gu	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	gu	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	gu	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947				0	gu	Resetting Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	gu	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	gu	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	gu	Using Custom Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	gu	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109				0	gu	Templates in the Template Folder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	gu	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialog before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	gu	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147315				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Templates\"\>Templates\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158421				0	gu	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)\"\>Shortcuts (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	gu	You can control \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> without using a mouse device, using only the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	gu	On each module's main help page (for example, the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer or \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc main help page) there is a link to access the keyboard shortcuts' help for that module.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	gu	In addition, under the keyword "Accessibility" you find step-by-step instructions about how to control the selected module without a mouse device.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166460				0	gu	Working with the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> user interface without mouse				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154749				0	gu	Activating menu bar, toolbars, windows, and document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	gu	Repeatedly pressing F6 switches the focus and circles through the following objects:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	gu	menu bar,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	gu	every toolbar from top to bottom and from left to right,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	gu	every free window from left to right,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	gu	document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	gu	Press Shift+F6 or Shift+Ctrl+Tab to switch through objects in the opposite direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152473				0	gu	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	gu	Press F10 to switch to the menu bar and back.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	gu	Escape closes an open submenu, a toolbar, or the current free window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3161656				0	gu	Calling a menu command				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	gu	Arrow down opens a selected menu. Any additional arrow down and up arrow move the selection through the menu commands. With right arrow you open any existing submenus.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	gu	Press Enter to execute the selected menu command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147086				0	gu	Executing an icon command				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922				0	gu	Press F6 repeatedly until the first icon on the toolbar is selected. Use the right and left arrows to select an icon on a horizontal toolbar. Similarly, use the up and down arrows to select an icon on a vertical toolbar. The Home key selects the first icon on a toolbar and the End key, the last.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	gu	If a toolbar is longer than can be displayed on screen, it shows an icon at the right or lower edge. Select the toolbar and press PageUp or PageDown to display the remaining icons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	gu	Special hints for toolbars				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	gu	Press the down arrow or right arrow to open the selected toolbar. This is equivalent to a mouse click. In the toolbar use the right arrow and left arrow keys. The Home and End keys select the first and last icon in the toolbar, respectively.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145365				0	gu	Close the toolbar with Esc. It is not possible to move the toolbar without a mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	gu	Selection from a combo box				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3148645\" src=\"res/helpimg/zellvor.png\" width=\"1.7602inch\" height=\"0.4898inch\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148645\"\>Combo box\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	gu	Select the combo box. Press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	gu	Use the down arrow or Page Down key to scroll down the combo box entries, or the up arrow or Page Up key to scroll upwards. The Home key takes you to the first entry and the End key takes you to the last entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	gu	Press Enter to execute the selected entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150685				0	gu	Selection in Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	gu	In several windows, dialogs, and in the table control field, there are tables to select data, for instance, in the right part of the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\" name=\"Data Source View\"\>Data Source View\</link\>. The following keys are used for selections in these tables:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	gu	Spacebar: switches from selection of the current row and cancellation of any selection, but not if the current cell is in edit mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150592				0	gu	Size and Position of Windows and Dialogs				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153221				0	gu	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
