helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153270				0	gu	Controlling the Dividing Lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158413	134			0	gu	Documents of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw, and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress can be split horizontally and vertically into separate views. Each view can show other parts of the document. Using the mouse, you can drag a dividing line from the scrollbar into the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	gu	Arrow keys: moves the current dividing line a big step in the arrow direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163668				0	gu	Shift+Arrow keys: moves the current dividing line a small step in the arrow direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148426				0	gu	Delete: deletes the current dividing line				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	gu	Shift+Delete: deletes both dividing lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150383				0	gu	Enter: fixes the current position of the dividing lines				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	gu	Escape: resets the current dividing line to its default position				2002-02-02 02:02:02
