helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	gu	On the \<emph\>Standard Bar\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10660				0	gu	The cursor changes to a paint bucket.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	gu	If you want to apply the formatting to more than one selection, double-click the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id209967\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatpaintbrush.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id209967\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. After you apply all the formatting, click the icon again.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	gu	Select or click the text or object that you want to apply the formatting to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	gu	The following table describes the formatting attributes that the \<emph\>Format Paintbrush\</emph\> can copy:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10691				0	gu	Type of Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10697				0	gu	ટિપ્પણી				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069E				0	gu	Nothing selected, but cursor is inside a text passage				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A4				0	gu	Copies the formatting of the current paragraph and the character formatting of the next character in the text flow direction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	gu	Text is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B1				0	gu	Copies the formatting of the last selected character and of the paragraph that contains the character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B8				0	gu	Frame is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BE				0	gu	Copies the frame attributes that are defined in Format - Frame dialog. The contents, size, position, linking, hyperlinks, and macros in the frame are not copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	gu	Object is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	gu	Copies the object formatting that is defined in the Format - Graphics or Format - Object dialogs. The contents, size, position, hyperlinks, and macros in the object are not copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	gu	Form control is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DF				0	gu	Drawing object is selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E5				0	gu	Copies all formatting attributes. In Impress and Draw, the text contents of the object is also copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F9				0	gu	Writer table or cells are selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	gu	Copies the formatting that is specified in Table, Text Flow, Borders, and Background tab pages in the Format - Table dialog. The paragraph and character formatting are also copied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	gu	Calc table or cells are selected				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\paintbrush.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070C				0	gu	Copies the formatting that is specified in the Format - Cells dialog as well as the formatting of the cell contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Viewing a Database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id2339854				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>opening;database files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;viewing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;viewing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A6				0	gu	\<variable id=\"data_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_view.xhp\"\>Viewing a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	gu	There are two different methods of viewing a database in %PRODUCTNAME.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CA				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open the database file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D1				0	gu	The \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> gives you full access to tables, queries, reports, and forms. You can edit the structure of your tables and change the contents of the data records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E3				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to view the registered databases.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_view.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EA				0	gu	The \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\"\>data source view\</link\> can be used to drag-and-drop table fields from registered databases into your documents and to produce mail merges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Accessibility in %PRODUCTNAME				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME features\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150502				0	gu	\<variable id=\"accessibility\"\>\<link name=\"Accessibility in %PRODUCTNAME\" href=\"text/shared/guide/accessibility.xhp\"\>Accessibility in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3154894				0	gu	The following accessibility features are part of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3153894				0	gu	Support of \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"external devices and applications\"\>external devices and applications\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	gu	Access to all functions by keyboard. The keys that replace the mouse actions are listed in the \<link name=\"%PRODUCTNAME Help\" href=\"text/shared/guide/keyboard.xhp\"\>\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Help\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	gu	Improved readability of screen contents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	gu	Zooming of on-screen user interface for menus, icons, and documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\accessibility.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	gu	Please note that accessibility support relies on Sun Microsystems Java technology for communications with assistive technology tools. This means that the first program startup may take a few seconds longer, because the Java runtime environment has to be started as well.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Recording Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>changes; recording\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording; changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments; on changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>settings;tracking changes\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	gu	\<variable id=\"redlining_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_enter.xhp\" name=\"Recording Changes\"\>Recording Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	gu	To start recording changes, open the document to be edited and choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Changes\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Changes\</emph\>\</link\> and then choose \<emph\>Record\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	gu	Now start making your changes. You will note that all new text passages that you enter are underlined in color, while all text that you delete remains visible but is crossed out and shown in color.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	gu	If you move to a marked change with the mouse pointer, you will see a reference to the type of change, the author, date and time of day for the change in the Help Tip. If the Extended Tips are also enabled, you will also see any available comments on this change.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156119				0	gu	Changes in a spreadsheet document are highlighted by a border around the cells; when you point to the cell you can see more detailed information on this change in the Help Tip.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	gu	You can enter a comment on each recorded change by placing the cursor in the area of the change and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Comment\</emph\>. In addition to Extended Tips, the comment is also displayed in the list in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230400.xhp\" name=\"Accept or Reject Changes\"\>\<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153542				0	gu	To stop recording changes, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> again. The check mark is removed and you can now save the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627				0	gu	In a text document, you can highlight all lines that you have changed with an additional colored marking. This can be in the form of a red line in the margin, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Version Management				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>versions; of a document\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; version management\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>version management\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154230				0	gu	\<variable id=\"redlining_versions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_versions.xhp\" name=\"Version Management\"\>Version Management\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	gu	The \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu contains a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01190000.xhp\" name=\"Versions\"\>\<emph\>Versions\</emph\>\</link\> command that enables you to save multiple versions of a document in the same file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149399				0	gu	You can choose to view individual versions of a document, or you can display the differences between versions with color markings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_versions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	gu	In the dialog to open a document, you can select from a combo box which version of this document you want to open.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143267				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Internet; Internet Explorer for displaying $[officename] documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] documents;viewing and editing in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	gu	\<variable id=\"activex\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/activex.xhp\" name=\"ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\"\>ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	gu	Under Windows only, you can view any $[officename] document in a window of the Microsoft Internet Explorer. Install the ActiveX control in the $[officename] Setup program.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156346				0	gu	Installing the ActiveX control				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	gu	Click the Start button on the Windows taskbar. Choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	gu	In the Control Panel, click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	gu	In the list, click %PRODUCTNAME, then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	gu	In the Installation Wizard, select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399				0	gu	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry and find the \<emph\>ActiveX Control\</emph\> entry. Open the sub menu of the icon and select to install the feature.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	8			0	gu	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> and \<emph\>Install\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	gu	Viewing $[officename] documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	gu	In Internet Explorer, browse to a web page that contains a link to a $[officename] Writer document, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	gu	Click the link to view the document in the Internet Explorer window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154072				0	gu	You may still right-click the link to save the file on your harddisk.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	gu	Editing $[officename] documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154367				0	gu	The $[officename] document inside the Internet Explorer shows a set of read-only toolbar icons.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Edit file\</emph\> icon in the document's toolbar to open a copy of the document in a new $[officename] window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	gu	Edit the copy of the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
