helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805				0	gu	You can copy a graphic from one document to another by drag-and-drop. If you plan to publish your document, please observe copyright laws and obtain the consent of the authors.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	gu	Open the document in which you want to insert the graphic object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	gu	Open the document from which you want to copy the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	gu	Click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, to select it without executing any hyperlinks it may refer to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	gu	Keep the mouse button pressed and wait a moment while the object is copied to an internal memory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	21			0	gu	Drag the graphic into the other document. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible side by side, first move the mouse pointer to the button of the target document while keeping the mouse button pressed. The document in question is then displayed and you can move the mouse pointer into the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	gu	Release the mouse button as soon as the gray text cursor indicates the position where you want to insert a copy of the picture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	gu	If the graphic is connected with a hyperlink, the hyperlink and not the graphic is inserted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10631				0	gu	\<variable id=\"imagemap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/imagemap.xhp\"\>Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	gu	An ImageMap allows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a picture in your document. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	gu	You can draw three types of hotspots: rectangles, ellipses, and polygons. When you click a hotspot, the URL is opened in the browser window or frame that you specify. You can also specify the text that appears when your mouse rests on the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10677				0	gu	To add a clickable hotspot to an image				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	gu	Position the cursor where you want the ImageMap in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>, select and insert a bitmap picture.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	gu	With the picture selected, choose \<emph\>Edit - ImageMap\</emph\>. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>, which displays the picture at the background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	gu	Use the icons in the ImageMap Editor to draw a hotspot shape, for example a rectangle, over the image at the background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	gu	Enter the "Address" URL that will be shown in a Web browser when the user clicks the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	gu	Optionally, enter the "Text" that will be shown as a tip when the user points the mouse to the hotspot.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B3				0	gu	Click the Apply button to apply your changes, and close the ImageMap Editor.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	gu	Save the document in the %PRODUCTNAME or HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	gu	You may save the ImageMap as a file and upload that file to a Web server, for example.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Adding Graphics to the Gallery				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927	49			0	gu	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_gallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_gallery.xhp\" name=\"Adding Graphics to the Gallery\"\>Adding Graphics to the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	gu	You can place a graphic from a document such as an HTML page in the Gallery by drag-and-drop.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	gu	Display the Gallery theme to which you want to add the graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	gu	Position the mouse pointer above the graphic, without clicking.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	gu	If the mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol, the graphic refers to a hyperlink. In this case, click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key to select it without executing the respective link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	gu	If the mouse pointer does not change to a hand symbol, you can simply click the graphic to select it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	gu	Once the graphic is selected, release the mouse button. Click again on the graphic image, keeping the mouse button pressed for more than two seconds. The graphic image is copied to the internal memory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772				0	gu	Without releasing the mouse button, drag the graphic into the Gallery.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Copying Graphics From the Gallery				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	gu	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_fromgallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics From the Gallery\"\>Copying Graphics From the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	gu	If you drag a graphic from the Gallery into a text, spreadsheet or presentation document, the graphic will be inserted there.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	gu	If you release the graphic \<emph\>directly on a draw object\</emph\>, please note the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	gu	If you move the graphic (drag it without pressing any key, in which case no additional symbol appears next to the mouse pointer), only the attributes are copied from the graphic and applied to the draw object on which you release the mouse button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Opening documents saved in other formats				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	gu	\<variable id=\"import_ms\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/import_ms.xhp\" name=\"Opening documents saved in other formats\"\>Opening documents saved in other formats\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	gu	You can open a document saved in another format by using the following procedure:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	5			0	gu	Select a format from the\<emph\> Files of type\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	gu	Select a file name and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898				0	gu	Converting all documents of a folder				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	gu	Open the wizard, which guides you through the operation, to copy and convert all documents from Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel or Microsoft PowerPoint into OpenDocument file format documents. You can select a source and target directory, specify whether to convert documents and/or templates, and more besides.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	gu	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01130000.xhp\" name=\"File - AutoPilot - Document Converter\"\>\<emph\>File - Wizards - Document Converter\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id4563127				0	gu	Opening HTML files in Writer				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id9207434				0	gu	Choose the file type "HTML Document" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer/Web. This is the default for HTML documents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id7215491				0	gu	All the options of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer/Web are now available to you, such as \<emph\>Show HTML source\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id2299874				0	gu	Choose "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id1727347				0	gu	All the options of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer are now available to you. Not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer offers for editing of documents can be saved in HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
