helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491	9			0	gu	The overwrite mode is enabled. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The text cursor is a blinking block. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>Click on the area to enable insert mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3154346				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/04/01010000.xhp\" name=\"Keyboard commands\"\>Keyboard commands\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting Data From Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152924				0	gu	\<variable id=\"copytext2application\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copytext2application.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Data From Text Documents\"\>Inserting Data From Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	gu	You can insert text into other document types, such as spreadsheets and presentations. Note that there is a difference between whether the text is inserted into a text frame, a spreadsheet cell, or into the outline view of a presentation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	gu	If you copy text to the clipboard, you can paste it with or without text attributes. Use the shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V to paste.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3143270\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_paste.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3143270\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	gu	To select the format in which the clipboard contents will be pasted, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard bar, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>, then select the proper format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	gu	If a text document contains headings formatted with the Heading Paragraph Style, choose \<emph\>File - Send - Outline to Presentation\</emph\>. A new presentation document is created, which contains the headings as an outline.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3145316				0	gu	If you want to transfer each heading together with its accompanying paragraphs, select the \<emph\>File - Send - AutoAbstract to Presentation\</emph\> command. You must have formatted the headings with a corresponding Paragraph Style to be able to see this command.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	gu	Copying Text Using Drag-and-Drop				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303				0	gu	If you select text and drag it into a spreadsheet with drag-and-drop, it will be inserted as text into the cell where you release the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	gu	If you drag text to the normal view of a presentation, an OLE object is inserted as a $[officename] plug-in.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	gu	If you drag the text to the outline view of a presentation, it will be inserted at the cursor location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Searching With a Form Filter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	bm_id8772545				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching; form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering; data in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;filtering in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; filtering data\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156042				0	gu	\<variable id=\"data_search2\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_search2.xhp\" name=\"Searching With a Form Filter\"\>Searching With a Form Filter\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	gu	Open a form document that contains database fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984	19			0	gu	On the \<emph\>Form Object\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Design Mode On/Off\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3147618\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_switchcontroldesignmode.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147618\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to turn off the design mode.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672	6			0	gu	On the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Form-Based Filters\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149807\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfilter.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149807\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The current document is displayed with its form controls as an empty edit mask. The \<emph\>Form Filter \</emph\>toolbar appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	gu	Enter the filter conditions into one or several fields. Note that if you enter filter conditions into several fields, all of the entered conditions must match (Boolean AND).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481	8			0	gu	More information about wildcards and operators can be found in \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExecute\"\>If you click the \<emph\>Apply Form-Based Filter\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the filter will be applied.\</ahelp\> You see the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar and can browse through the found records.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExit\"\>If you click on the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the form is displayed without a filter.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114	11			0	gu	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Apply Filter\"\>\<emph\>Apply Filter\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3144764\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_datafilterstandardfilter.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3144764\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar to change to the filtered view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3146898	12			0	gu	The filter that has been set can be removed by clicking \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sort\"\>\<emph\>Remove Filter/Sort\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3151318\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_removefiltersort.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151318\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Using Digital Signatures				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	hd_id2767418				0	gu	\<variable id=\"digital_signatures\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp\"\>Using Digital Signatures\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	gu	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can digitally sign your documents and macros. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10639				0	gu	To sign a document digitally, you need a personal key, the certificate. A personal key is stored on your computer as a combination of a private key, which must be kept secret, and a public key, which you add to your documents when you sign them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066D				0	gu	Save and sign the document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	gu	When you apply a digital signature to a document, a kind of checksum is computed from the document's content plus your personal key. The checksum and your public key are stored together with the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	gu	Open a signed document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	gu	When someone later opens the document on any computer with a recent version of %PRODUCTNAME, the program will compute the checksum again and compare it with the stored checksum. If both are the same, the program will signal that you see the original, unchanged document. In addition, the program can show you the public key information from the certificate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	gu	You can compare the public key with the public key that is published on the web site of the certificate authority.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	gu	Whenever someone changes something in the document, this change breaks the digital signature. After the change, there will be no sign that you see the original document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	hd_id9354228				0	gu	Security Warnings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id2372508				0	gu	When you receive a signed document, and the software reports that the signature is valid, this does not mean that you can be absolutely sure that the document is the same that the sender has sent. Signing documents with software certificates is not a perfectly secure method. Numerous ways are possible to circumvent the security features.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id7953123				0	gu	Example: Think about someone wants to camouflage his identity to be a sender from your bank. He can easily get a certificate using a false name, then send you any signed e-mail pretending he is working for your bank. You will get that e-mail, and the e-mail or the document within has the "valid signed" icon. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id6195257				0	gu	Do not trust the icon. Inspect and verify the certificates.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id8635517				0	gu	The validation of a signature is not a legally binding assurement of any kind.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id6075624				0	gu	On Windows operating systems, the Windows features of validating a signature are used. On Solaris and Linux systems, files that are supplied by Thunderbird, Mozilla or Firefox are used. You must ensure that the files that are in use within your system are really the original files that were supplied by the original developers. For malevolent intruders, there are numerous ways to replace original files with other files that they supply.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id6819971				0	gu	The messages about validation of a signature that you see in %PRODUCTNAME are the messages that the validation files return. The %PRODUCTNAME software has no way to ensure that the messages reflect the true status of any certificate. The %PRODUCTNAME software only displays the messages that other files that are not under control of %PRODUCTNAME report. There is no legal responsibility of %PRODUCTNAME that the displayed messages reflect the true status of a digital signature.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\contextmenu.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Using Context Menus				2002-02-02 02:02:02
