helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02000000.xhp\" name=\"Queries\"\>Queries\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499				0	gu	A "query" is special view of a table. Queries can display certain records or only a few fields per record and, if required, also sort those records. A query can apply to one table to multiple tables, if they are linked by common data fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	gu	Use queries to find records from data tables based on certain criteria. All queries created for a database are listed under the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> entry. Since this entry contains the database queries, it is also called the "query container".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153750				0	gu	Printing Queries				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149183				0	gu	To print a query or table:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	gu	Open a text document (or a spreadsheet document if you prefer the specific printing functions of this type of document).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	gu	Decide which columns = data fields you want to include. You can also click the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> button and select a corresponding formatting type. Close the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	gu	The query or table will be inserted into your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	gu	Print the document by choosing \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0212.xhp\" name=\"Sorting and Filtering Data\"\>Sorting and Filtering Data\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	gu	Allows you to sort and filter the data in a query table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	gu	With the \<emph\>Query Design\</emph\>, you can create and edit a query or view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Through Several Tables\"\>Query Through Several Tables\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151043				0	gu	The query result can contain data from several tables if these are linked to each other by suitable data fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159149				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Formulating Query Criteria\"\>Formulating Query Criteria\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910				0	gu	You can find out which operators and commands can be used to formulate the filter conditions for a query.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156212				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Executing Functions\"\>Executing Functions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	gu	You can perform calculations with the data of a table and store the results as a query result.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
