helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154347				0	gu	Auto				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_PUSHBUTTON_TAB_WIZ_TYPE_SELECT_PB_AUTO\"\>Enables automatic type recognition.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957	2			0	gu	This command opens the \<emph\>Relation Design \</emph\>window, which allows you to define relationships between various database tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_CTL_RELATIONTAB\"\>Here you can link together tables from the current database through common data fields.\</ahelp\> Click the \<emph\>New Relation\</emph\> icon to create the relationships, or simply drag-and-drop with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145316				0	gu	This function is only available if you are working with a relational database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235				0	gu	When you choose \<emph\>Tools - Relationships\</emph\>, a window opens in which all the existing relationships between the tables of the current database are shown. If no relationships have been defined, or if you want to relate other tables of the database to each other, then click the \<emph\>Add Tables\</emph\> icon. The \<link href=\"text/shared/02/14020100.xhp\" name=\"Add Tables\"\>Add Tables\</link\> dialog opens in which you can select the tables that you want.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152812				0	gu	If the \<emph\>Relation Design\</emph\> window is open, the selected tables cannot be modified, even in Table Design mode. This ensures that tables are not changed while the relations are being created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	gu	The selected tables are shown in the top area of the design view. You can close a table window through the context menu or with the Delete key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148922				0	gu	Primary key and other key				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149168				0	gu	If you want to define a relation among the different tables, you should enter a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#primaerschluessel\" name=\"primary key\"\>primary key\</link\> that clearly identifies a data field of the existing table. You can refer to the primary key from other tables to access the data of this table. All data fields referring to this primary key will be identified as an external key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147085				0	gu	All data fields referring to a primary key will be identified in the table window by a small key symbol.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153193				0	gu	Define relations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155430				0	gu	All existing relations are shown in the relations windows by a line that connects the primary and other key fields. You can add a relation by using drag-and-drop to drop the field of one table onto the field of the other table. A relation is removed again by selecting it and pressing the Delete key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149984				0	gu	Alternatively, you can also click the \<emph\>New Relation\</emph\> icon in the top area of the relation field and define the relation between two tables in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/05020100.xhp\" name=\"Relations\"\>\<emph\>Relations\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153093				0	gu	If you use $[officename] as the front-end for a relational database, the creation and deletion of relationships is not placed in an intermediate memory by $[officename], but is forwarded directly to the external database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856	15			0	gu	By double-clicking a connection line, you can assign certain properties to the relation. The \<emph\>Relations \</emph\>dialog opens.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
