helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	gu	Administrator				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_SYSUSR\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the name of the database administrator.\</ahelp\> The administrator name and password is assigned when you create an Adabas database. Apart from the administrator, two more users can access the Adabas database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149045				0	gu	Control User				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_CONUSR\"\>Enter the name of a user that you want to give limited control to modify some parameters of the database. Normally, the default settings for the name and the password of the control user are not changed.\</ahelp\> The control user does not affect the three-user limitation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153379				0	gu	Domain User				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153362				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_USR\"\>Enter the name of the domain user that is used by Adabas internally. Normally, the default settings for the name and password of the domain user are not changed.\</ahelp\> The domain user does not affect the three-user limit.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148674				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DOMAINPWD\"\>Enter a password.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144433				0	gu	Database settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145607				0	gu	Drives containing parts of the Serverdb are called DEVSPACEs. To improve performance, store each DEVSPACE on separate drives.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	gu	The file path for a DEVSPACE, including its file name, cannot exceed 40 characters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149064				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_SYSDEVSPACE\"\>Enter the path for the system DEVSPACE.\</ahelp\> The SYSDEVSPACE manages the configuration data for the database. The size of the SYSDEVSPACE depends on the size of the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154190				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_TRANSACTIONLOG\"\>Enter the path for the transaction log file.\</ahelp\> This file records all modifications that are made to the database during a transaction, and overwrites them when the transaction is completed. The TRANSACTIONLOG is also used for the rollback of a transaction.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DATADEVSPACE\"\>Enter the path for the data DEVSPACE.\</ahelp\> This file stores user data, such as tables and indexes, as well as the SQL catalog (schema info). The data contained in one user table is evenly distributed across all DATADEVSPACEs. The combined size of all DATADEVSPACEs corresponds to the size of the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	gu	The maximum size for a DATADEVSPACE in the limited version Adabas database is 100MB.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	gu	If the DATADEVSPACE reaches full capacity during a database operation, Adabas shuts down, increases the capacity of the DATADEVSPACE (up to 100 MB), and restarts the database. Saved data is not lost.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153091				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_PBDATADEVSPACE\"\>Locate the directory where you want to save the file, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150686				0	gu	Transaction file (MB)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_TRANSACTIONLOG_SIZE\"\>Enter the size of the transaction file in megabytes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157977				0	gu	Database size (MB)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150115				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_ADABAS_DATADEVSPACE_SIZE\"\>Enter the size of the database in megabytes here. The maximum size is 100 MB.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155415				0	gu	Database size (MB)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
