helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150207				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>3D rotation objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; to curves, polygons, 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extrusion objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	gu	\<variable id=\"3d_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/3d_create.xhp\" name=\"Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\"\>Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	gu	You can convert two dimensional (2D) objects to create different shapes. $[officename] can convert 2D objects to the following object types:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	gu	Curved object based on Bézier curves				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	gu	Polygon object consisting of straight line segments				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	gu	3D object with shading and a light source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	gu	3D rotation object with shading and a light source				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	gu	To convert an object to a curved shape:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	gu	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828				0	gu	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id1027558\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1027558\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object. You can also drag the control points of a handle to modify the shape of the curve.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153738				0	gu	To convert a 2D object to a polygon:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	gu	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon.\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368				0	gu	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id7219458\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.2201inch\" height=\"0.2201inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7219458\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153919				0	gu	To convert a 2D object to a 3D object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1088B				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Extrusion On/Off\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id2490920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_extrusiontoggle.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2490920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, or right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148828				0	gu	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> toolbar and the \<emph\>3D Settings\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	gu	To convert a text object to 3D, use the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3821222\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3821222\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145410				0	gu	To convert a 2D object to a 3D rotation object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	gu	A 3D rotation object is created by rotating the selected object around its vertical axis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151318				0	gu	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D Rotation Object\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3146125				0	gu	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the Line and Filling toolbar and the 3D Settings toolbar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149336				0	gu	You can rotate the 2D object before converting it to create a more complex shape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
