helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146121				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>objects;moving in slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;objects in slides\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	gu	\<variable id=\"move_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/move_object.xhp\" name=\"Moving Objects\"\>Moving Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	gu	You can move selected objects in your slide by dragging them, using the arrow keys, or by copying the objects and pasting them in another location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	gu	The arrow keys let you move objects more precisely than with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153415				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>vectorizing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; bitmaps to polygons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; converting to vector graphics\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vector graphics;converting bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153415				0	gu	\<variable id=\"vectorize\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/vectorize.xhp\" name=\"Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics\"\>Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155633				0	gu	A vector graphic can be resized without losing the quality of the graphic. In $[officename] Draw and Impress, you can convert a bitmap image into a vector graphic.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	gu	Select the bitmap image that you want to convert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	gu	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Polygon\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	gu	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149349				0	gu	Set the conversion options for the image, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. See \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13050200.xhp\" name=\"Convert to Polygon\"\>\<emph\>Convert to Polygon\</emph\>\</link\> for a description of the conversion options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147371				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13050200.xhp\" name=\"Convert to Polygon\"\>Convert to Polygon\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153191	1			0	gu	\<variable id=\"footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/footer.xhp\" name=\"Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\"\>Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8843043				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295	12			0	gu	On the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, select the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154654\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_texttoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154654\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	gu	Drag in the master page to draw a text object, and then type or paste your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155441				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> when you are finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150476				0	gu	You can also add fields, such as the date or page number, to a header or footer by choosing \<emph\>Insert - Fields\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3156320	18			0	gu	You can hide the header or footer on the current slide by choosing \<emph\>Format\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Modify Layout\"\>Slide\<emph\> Layout\</emph\>\</link\>, and clearing the \<emph\>Objects on background\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155848				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/04990000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Fields\"\>Insert Fields\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Creating a Flowchart				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150439				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>connectors; using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>flowcharts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>orgcharts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hot spots in flowcharts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>interactions; hot spots\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	gu	\<variable id=\"orgchart\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/orgchart.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Flowchart\"\>Creating a Flowchart\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153				0	gu	To create a flowchart:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3152482				0	gu	Select a tool from the \<emph\>Flowchart\</emph\> toolbar on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	gu	Drag a shape in your slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	gu	To add more shapes, repeat the last steps.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3146967	43			0	gu	Open the \<emph\>Connectors \</emph\>toolbar on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, and select a connector line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3149945				0	gu	Move the pointer over the edge of a shape so that the connection sites appear.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3146871				0	gu	Click a connection site, drag to a connection site on another shape, and then release.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3145824				0	gu	To add more connectors, repeat the last steps.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153036				0	gu	You now have the basic outline for your flowchart.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155255				0	gu	To add text to the shapes on your flowchart				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3145592				0	gu	Double-click the shape, and type or paste your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3154504				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, and drag a text object over the shape. Type or paste your text into the text object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153730				0	gu	To add a color fill to a shape:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3155930				0	gu	Select the shape, and choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150934				0	gu	To add some hot spots that call other slides:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3145300	57			0	gu	Assign \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06070000.xhp\" name=\"interactions\"\>interactions\</link\> to some objects on your slide. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_idN10898				0	gu	Select the object, then choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Interaction\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A0				0	gu	Select an interaction in the dialog. For example, select to go to the next slide when the user clicks the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153922				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10100000.xhp\" name=\"Connectors\"\>Connectors\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\orgchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10030200.xhp\" name=\"Glue points\"\>Glue points\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Loading Color, Gradient, and Hatching Lists				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154510				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>colors;loading lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>gradients;loading lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hatching;loading lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading;colors/gradients/hatchings\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154510				0	gu	\<variable id=\"palette_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/palette_files.xhp\" name=\"Loading Color, Gradient, and Hatching Lists\"\>Loading Color, Gradient, and Hatching Lists\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385	73			0	gu	You can use lists to organize colors, gradients, or hatching patterns. $[officename] provides several lists that you can load and use in your document. If you want, you can add or delete elements from a list, or even create custom lists. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	gu	To load a color list:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Colors\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3152896				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Load Color List\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	gu	Locate the color list that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. A color list file has the format [filename].soc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	gu	To save a color list, click the \<emph\>Save Color List\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149871				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>colors; default colors\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3149871				0	gu	The CMYK list is optimized for print colors, whereas the colors in the Web and the HTML lists are optimized for displays using a resolution of 256 colors.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150435				0	gu	To load a gradient list:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3150393				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3146322				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Load Gradients List\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946				0	gu	Locate the gradient list that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. A gradient list file has the format [filename].sog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740				0	gu	To save a gradients list, click the \<emph\>Save Gradients List\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153036				0	gu	To load a hatching list:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3155255				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Hatching\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3153004				0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Load Hatches List\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3154505				0	gu	Locate the hatches list that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. A hatches list file has the format [filename].soh.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3149881				0	gu	To save a hatches list, click the \<emph\>Save Hatches List\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3155437				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05210000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Area\"\>Format - Area\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>presentations;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>timings; rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide changes;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording;display times for slides\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	gu	\<variable id=\"rehearse_timings\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\" name=\"Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\"\>Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	1			0	gu	$[officename] assists you in defining the right rehearse timings for automatic slide changes. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	gu	Prepare the slides, start the show using a special icon, tell your imaginary audience what you want to tell for the first slide, then advance to the next slide and so on. $[officename] records the display time for each slide, so the next time you play the show with automatic slide changes, the timing will be as recorded.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	gu	Open a presentation, and switch to \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> View.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248				0	gu	If you want the whole presentation to auto-repeat, open the menu \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Slide Show Settings\"\>Slide Show Settings\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Editing Curves				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	gu	\<variable id=\"line_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Curves\"\>Editing Curves\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	gu	A curved line segment consists of two data points (endpoints) and two control points (handles). A control line connects a control point to a data point. You can change the shape of a curve by converting a data point to a different type, or by dragging the control points to a different location.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	gu	You can also modify the properties of the line by selecting the line and choosing \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	gu	To view the data points and control points of a curved line, select the line, and then click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the Drawing bar. The data points are represented by squares and the control points by circles. A control point might overlay a data point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145587				0	gu	To adjust a curved line segment:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	gu	Drag a data point to resize the line. If a control point overlies the data point, drag the control point until you can see the data point, and then drag the data point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	gu	Drag a control point. The curve pulls in the direction that you drag the control point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150431				0	gu	To split a curved line:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	gu	You can only split a curved line that has three or more data points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149941	60			0	gu	Select a data point, and then click the \<emph\>Split Curve \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150655				0	gu	To create a closed shape:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153080	63			0	gu	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Close Bézier\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145162				0	gu	To convert a data point on a curved line:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155925				0	gu	Click the data point you want to convert, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	gu	To convert the data point to a smooth point, click the \<emph\>Smooth Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	gu	To convert the data point to a symmetrical point, click the \<emph\>Symmetric Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145348				0	gu	To convert the data point to a corner point, click the \<emph\>Corner Point\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150471				0	gu	To add a data point:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156256	70			0	gu	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Insert Points\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3083280				0	gu	Click the line where you want to add the point, and drag a short distance.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154643				0	gu	If a data point does not have a control point, select the data point, and then click the \<emph\>Convert to Curve\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151186				0	gu	To delete a data point:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150261				0	gu	Click the point you want to delete.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3143230	76			0	gu	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Delete Points\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151174				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0227.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points bar\"\>Edit Points bar\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
