helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073	14			0	gu	In the presentation containing the slide(s) that you want to copy, choose\<emph\> View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3147401	5			0	gu	Select the slide(s), and then choose\<emph\> Edit - Copy\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3147298				0	gu	Change to the presentation where you want to paste the slide(s), and then choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156401				0	gu	Select the slide that you want the copied slide to follow, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\page_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150655				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/04110000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - File\"\>Insert - File\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Inserting Layers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	gu	\<variable id=\"layer_new\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layer_new.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Layers\"\>Inserting Layers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	gu	Right-click the layer tab area at the bottom.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Insert Layer\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	12			0	gu	Type a name for the layer in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	15			0	gu	In the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>area, set the options for the layer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964				0	gu	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The new layer automatically becomes the active layer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3154658				0	gu	To change the properties of a layer, click the name tab of the layer, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Layer\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_new.xhp	0	help	par_id3153814				0	gu	You cannot change the name of or delete a predefined \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw layer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150717				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>text; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sign conversion to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; text to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150717				0	gu	\<variable id=\"text2curve\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/text2curve.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\"\>Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	gu	You can convert text characters into curves that you can edit and resize as you would any drawing object. Once you convert text into a drawing object, you can no longer edit the content of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153965				0	gu	To convert text into a drawing object:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3146963				0	gu	Select the text that you want to convert, and do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	gu	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	gu	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the border of the text object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746				0	gu	If your text contains more than one character, the converted text becomes a grouped object. Double-click the group to edit individual objects. Press Esc when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336				0	gu	Now, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar. Click the object. You can see all the Bézier points of the object. On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> bar, you can find various icons for editing, inserting and deleting points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Changing the Slide Background Fill				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150199				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide masters; changing backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slides;changing backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150199	33			0	gu	\<variable id=\"background\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/background.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Slide Background Fill\"\>Changing the Slide Background Fill\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155067				0	gu	You can change the background color or the background fill of the current slide or all of the slides in your document. For a background fill, you can use hatching, a gradient, or a bitmap image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148701				0	gu	If you want to change the background fill for all of the slides, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>. To change the background fill of a single slide, choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150534				0	gu	To use a color, gradient, or hatching pattern for the slide background				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149942				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Hatching\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148725	51			0	gu	In the \<emph\>Fill \</emph\>area, do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150866				0	gu	Select \<emph\>Gradient\</emph\>, and then click a gradient style in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150338				0	gu	Select \<emph\>Hatching\</emph\>, and then click a hatching style in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150021				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Load\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145244				0	gu	To use an image for the slide background				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148394				0	gu	You can display an entire image as a slide background, or you can tile the image to produce a patterned background.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156064				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Hatching\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3145356	59			0	gu	In the \<emph\>Fill \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>, and then click an image in the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150757	60			0	gu	If you want to use a custom image for the slide background, close the \<emph\>Page Setup \</emph\>dialog, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Bitmaps \</emph\>tab, and then click \<emph\>Import\</emph\>. Locate the image you want to import and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When you return to the \<emph\>Background \</emph\>tab, the image you imported will be in the \<emph\>Bitmap \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150263	62			0	gu	To display the entire image as the background, clear the \<emph\>Tile \</emph\>check box in the \<emph\>Position \</emph\>area, and then select \<emph\>AutoFit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149756				0	gu	To tile the image on the background, select \<emph\>Tile\</emph\>, and set the \<emph\>Size\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> options for the image.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154934				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Load\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3158403				0	gu	This modification is only valid for the current presentation document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10820				0	gu	To save a new slide master as a template				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10827				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\> to change the slide master.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> to close the master view.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083F				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> to save the document as a template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10847				0	gu	Enter a name for the template. Do not change the category from "My Templates". Click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084A				0	gu	Now you can use the Presentation Wizard to open a new presentation based on your new template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Printing Presentations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	gu	\<variable id=\"printing\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/printing.xhp\" name=\"Printing Presentations\"\>Printing Presentations\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154486				0	gu	Default printer settings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385				0	gu	To set the default printing options for $[officename] Impress, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153914				0	gu	Setting printer options for the current presentation				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	gu	These settings override the default printer options in \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - Print\</emph\> for the current print job only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id7197790				0	gu	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id2901394				0	gu	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151389				0	gu	Printing a range of slides				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3146318				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	gu	Hold down Shift, and click the range of slides that you want to print.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Creating Animated GIF Images				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153188				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>cross-fading; creating cross-fades\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>GIF images; animating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animated GIFs\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153188				0	gu	\<variable id=\"animated_gif_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_gif_create.xhp\" name=\"Creating Animated GIF Images\"\>Creating Animated GIF Images\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	gu	You can animate drawing objects, text objects, and graphic objects (images) on your slides to make your presentation more interesting. $[officename] Impress provides you with a simple animation editor where you can create animation images (frames) by assembling objects from your slide. The animation effect is achieved by rotating through the static frames that you create.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	gu	If you create a bitmap animation (animated GIF), you can assign a delay time to each frame, and specify the number of times the animation is played.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150250				0	gu	To create an animated GIF:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148703	59			0	gu	Select an object or group of objects that you want to include in your animation and choose\<emph\> Insert - Animated Image\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086	97			0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Apply Object \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"sd/res/get1obj.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Note Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to add a single object or a group of objects to the current animation frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150860	98			0	gu	Click the \<emph\>Apply Objects Individually \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3149355\" src=\"sd/res/getallob.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149355\"\>Tip Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to create a separate animation frame for each of the selected objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148391	61			0	gu	In the \<emph\>Animation Group \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap object\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	gu	Use the animation timeline to specify the duration for displaying a frame and the number of times an animation sequence is presented (looping).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644				0	gu	Enter a frame number in the \<emph\>Image Number\</emph\> box (left box).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150756	63			0	gu	Enter the number of seconds you want the frame to display in the \<emph\>Duration \</emph\>box (middle box).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182				0	gu	Repeat the last two steps for each frame in your animation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177	100			0	gu	You can preview your animation by using the controls to the left of the \<emph\>Image Number \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939	65			0	gu	Select the number of times you want the animation sequence to repeat in the \<emph\>Loop count \</emph\>box (right box).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145421				0	gu	Select an alignment option for the objects in the \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	About Layers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149018				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>layers; definition\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	gu	\<variable id=\"layers\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layers.xhp\" name=\"About Layers\"\>About Layers\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	3			0	gu	Layers are available in $[officename] Draw, not in $[officename] Impress. Layers allow you to assemble elements on a page that are related. Think of layers as individual workspaces that you can hide from view, hide from printing, or lock. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id7036957				0	gu	Layers do not determine the stacking order of objects on your page, except for the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer which is always in front of other layers. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id1614734				0	gu	The stacking order of objects on your page is determined by the sequence in which you add the objects. You can rearrange the stacking order by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id398876				0	gu	The areas on a layer that do not contain objects are transparent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	gu	$[officename] Draw provides three default layers:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073				0	gu	દેખાવ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	gu	નિયંત્રણો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	gu	લીટીઓનુ માપ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156397				0	gu	You cannot delete or rename the default layers. You can add your own layers by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Layer\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	gu	The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer is the default workspace. The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer determines the location of title, text, and object placeholders on your page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	gu	The \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer can be used for buttons that have been assigned an action, but that should not be printed. Set the layer's properties to not printable. Objects on the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer are always in front of objects on other layers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	gu	The \<emph\>Dimension Lines\</emph\> layer is where you draw, for example, the dimension lines. By switching the layer to show or hide, you can easily switch these lines on and off.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507				0	gu	You can lock a layer to protect its contents, or hide a layer and its contents from view or from printing. When you add a new layer to a page, the layer is added to all of the pages in your document. However, when you add an object to a layer, it is only added to the current page. If you want the object to appear on all of the pages, add the object to the master page (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Master\</item\>).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Selecting Underlying Objects				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154492				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>objects; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting; hidden objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>covered objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>underlying objects\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154492				0	gu	\<variable id=\"select_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/select_object.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Underlying Objects\"\>Selecting Underlying Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	gu	To select an object that is covered by other objects, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click through the objects until you reach the underlying object. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift when you click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	gu	To select an object that is covered by another object using the keyboard, press Tab to cycle through the objects on the slide. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, press Shift+Tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
