helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_HEADER\"\>Includes the column labels in the first row of a cell range.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:ED_COPY_AREA\"\>Select the check box, and then select the cell range where you want to display the filter results.\</ahelp\> You can also select a named range from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272				0	gu	Regular expression				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_REGEXP\"\>Allows you to use wildcards in the filter definition.\</ahelp\> For a list of the regular expressions that $[officename] supports, click \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"here\"\>here\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	gu	If the \<emph\>Regular Expressions\</emph\> check box is selected, you can use regular expressions in the Value field if the Condition list box is set to '=' EQUAL or '<>' UNEQUAL. This also applies to the respective cells that you reference for an advanced filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149958				0	gu	No duplication				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_UNIQUE\"\>Excludes duplicate rows in the list of filtered data.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154018				0	gu	Keep filter criteria				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_FILTER:BTN_DEST_PERS\"\>Select the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> check box, and then specify the destination range where you want to display the filtered data. If this box is checked, the destination range remains linked to the source range. You must have defined the source range under \<emph\>Data - Define range\</emph\> as a database range.\</ahelp\> Following this, you can reapply the defined filter at any time as follows: click into the source range, then choose \<emph\>Data - Refresh Range\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	gu	Data range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	gu	Displays the cell range or the name of the cell range that you want to filter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	DATE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155511				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>DATE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155511				0	gu	\<variable id=\"date\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_date.xhp\"\>DATE\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150474				0	gu	DATE(year; month; day)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3152815				0	gu	\<emph\>Year\</emph\> is an integer between 1583 and 9956 or 0 and 99.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155817				0	gu	\<emph\>Month\</emph\> is an integer between 1 and 12 indicating the month.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	gu	If the values for month and day are higher, they are carried over to the next digit. If you enter =DATE(00;12;31) the result will be "12/31/00." If, on the other hand, you enter =DATE(00;13;31) the result will be "1/31/01."				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147477				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Merge Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149785				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05060000.xhp\" name=\"Merge Cells\"\>Merge Cells\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Combines the selected cells into a single cell or splits merged cells.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	gu	The merged cell receives the name of the first cell of the original cell range. Merged cells cannot be merged a second time with other cells. The range must form a rectangle, multiple selection is not supported.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149665				0	gu	If the cells to be merged have any contents, a security dialog is shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Hide				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030300.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147265				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; hiding functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding; rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding; columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows;hiding\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147265				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05030300.xhp\" name=\"Hide\"\>Hide\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Hide\"\>Hides selected rows, columns or individual sheets.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645	3			0	gu	Select the rows or columns that you want to hide, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Row - Hide \</emph\>or\<emph\> Format - Column - Hide\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	gu	You can hide a sheet by selecting the sheet tab and then choosing \<emph\>Format - Sheet - Hide\</emph\>. Hidden sheets are not printed unless they occur within a \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080000.xhp\" name=\"print range\"\>print range\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	gu	A break in the row or column header indicates whether the row or column is hidden.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	gu	To display hidden rows, columns or sheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id8337046				0	gu	Select the range that includes the hidden objects. You can also use the box in the corner above row 1 and beside column A. For sheets, this step is not necessary.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05030300.xhp	0	help	par_id5532090				0	gu	Choose \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05030400.xhp\" name=\"Format - Row/Column - Show\"\>Format - Row/Column - Show\</link\> or \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05050300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sheet - Show\"\>Format - Sheet - Show\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	gu	Select the database and the table or query containing the data that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151041				0	gu	Database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
