helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	gu	\<variable id=\"reihenfuellentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillSeries\"\>Automatically generate series with the options in this dialog. Determine direction, increment, time unit and series type.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976				0	gu	Before filling a series, first select the cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748				0	gu	To automatically continue a series using the assumed completion rules, choose the \<emph\>AutoFill\</emph\> option after opening the \<emph\>Fill Series\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147435				0	gu	Direction				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	gu	Determines the direction of series creation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155418				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_BOTTOM\"\>Creates a downward series in the selected cell range for the column using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_RIGHT\"\>Creates a series running from left to right within the selected cell range using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_TOP\"\>Creates an upward series in the cell range of the column using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_LEFT\"\>Creates a series running from right to left in the selected cell range using the defined increment to the end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147344				0	gu	Series Type				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257	15			0	gu	Defines the series type. Choose between \<emph\>Linear, Growth, Date \</emph\>and \<emph\>AutoFill\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148488				0	gu	Linear				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_ARITHMETIC\"\>Creates a linear number series using the defined increment and end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149210				0	gu	Growth				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150364				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_GEOMETRIC\"\>Creates a growth series using the defined increment and end value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149528				0	gu	Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150887				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SCDLG_FILLSERIES:BTN_DATE\"\>Creates a date series using the defined increment and end date.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202				0	gu	AutoFill				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3155811				0	gu	AutoFill tries to complete a value series by using a defined pattern. The series 1,3,5 is automatically completed with 7,9,11,13, and so on. Date and time series are completed accordingly; for example, after 01.01.99 and 15.01.99, an interval of 14 days is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148700				0	gu	Unit of Time				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	par_id3153308				0	gu	In this area you can specify the desired unit of time. This area is only active if the \<emph\>Date\</emph\> option has been chosen in the \<emph\>Series type\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148868				0	gu	Day				2002-02-02 02:02:02
