helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159079				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152766				0	gu	To find the length of the combined distance to school of all children at Joe's birthday party (scroll up, please) who are in second grade, enter the following formula in B16:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150596				0	gu	Enter "2" in row 14 under "Grade". The sum (1950) of the distances to school of all the children who are in second grade is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155614				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>EXPONDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exponential distributions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155614				0	gu	DVAR				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154418				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBVARIANZ\"\>DVAR returns the variance of all cells of a database field in all records that match the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\> The records from the example are treated as a sample of data. A representative result cannot be obtained from a sample population of less than one thousand.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156138				0	gu	DVAR(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151257				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153701				0	gu	To find the variance of the weight of all children of the same age of the above example (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153798				0	gu	In row 14, under Age, enter 7, 8, 9, and so on, one after the other. You will see as a result the variance of the weight values for all children of this age.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153880				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>EXPONDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exponential distributions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153880				0	gu	DVARP				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155119				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DBVARIANZEN\"\>DVARP calculates the variance of all cell values in a database field in all records that match the specified search criteria.\</ahelp\> The records are from the example are treated as an entire population.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153776				0	gu	DVARP(Database; Database Field; Search Criteria)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147099				0	gu	To find the variance of the weight for all children of the same age at Joe's birthday party (scroll up, please), enter the following formula in B16:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146902				0	gu	In row 14, under Age, enter 7, 8, 9, and so on, one after the other. The variance of the weight values for all children of this age attending Joe's birthday party appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
