helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151341				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060118.xhp\" name=\"Forward to Financial Functions Part Three\"\>Financial Functions Part Three\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150026				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>PPMT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150026				0	gu	PPMT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146942				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KAPZ\"\>Returns for a given period the payment on the principal for an investment that is based on periodic and constant payments and a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146878				0	gu	PPMT(Rate;Period;NPER;PV;FV;Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151228				0	gu	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148887				0	gu	Period: the amortizement period. P=1 for the first and P=NPER for the last period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148436				0	gu	\<emph\>NPER\</emph\> is the total number of periods, during which annuity is paid.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153035				0	gu	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present cash value in sequence of payments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3144744				0	gu	Type (optional): defines the due date. F=1 for payment at the beginning of a period and F=0 for payment at the end of a period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148582				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154811				0	gu	How high is the periodic monthly payment at an annual interest rate of 8.75% over a period of 3 years? The cash value is 5,000 currency units and is always paid at the beginning of a period. The future value is 8,000 currency units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139				0	gu	CUMPRINC				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150140				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUMKAPITAL\"\>Returns the cumulative interest paid for an investment period with a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148733				0	gu	CUMPRINC(Rate;NPER;PV;S;E;Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864				0	gu	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150007				0	gu	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present cash value in sequence of payments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145167				0	gu	Type (optional): the due date of the payment at the beginning or at the end of the period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154502				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153570				0	gu	What are the payoff amounts if the yearly interest rate is 5.5% for 36 months? The cash value is 15,000 currency units. The payoff amount is calculated between the 10th and 18th period. The due date is at the end of the period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149884				0	gu	CUMPRINC(5.5%/12;36;15000;10;18;0) = -3669.74 currency units. The payoff amount between the 10th and 18th period is 3669.74 currency units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150019				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>CUMPRINC_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150019				0	gu	CUMPRINC_ADD				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145246				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_CUMPRINC\"\> Calculates the cumulative redemption of a loan in a period.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3157970				0	gu	CUMPRINC_ADD(Rate;NPER;PV;Start period;End period;Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145302				0	gu	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> defines the interest rate per period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150269				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150661				0	gu	Rate: 9.00 per cent per annum (9% / 12 = 0.0075), Duration: 30 years (payment periods = 30 * 12 = 360), NPV: 125000 currency units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155512				0	gu	How much will you repay in the second year of the mortgage (thus from periods 13 to 24)?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149026				0	gu	In the first month you will be repaying the following amount:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
