helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147314				0	gu	\<emph\>Price\</emph\>: The price of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145156				0	gu	\<emph\>Redemption\</emph\>: the redemption value of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3159218				0	gu	\<emph\>P\</emph\> is the number of interest payment periods per year.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147547				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151214				0	gu	A security is purchased on 2/15/1999. It matures on 11/15/2007. The rate of interest is 5.75%. The price is 95.04287 currency units per 100 units of par value, the redemption value is 100 units. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency = 2) and the basis is 0. How high is the yield?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154194				0	gu	=YIELD("2/15/1999"; "11/15/2007"; 0.0575 ;95.04287; 100; 2; 0) returns 0.065 or 6.5 per cent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150100				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>EXPONDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exponential distributions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150100				0	gu	YIELDDISC				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150486				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_YIELDDISC\"\>Calculates the annual yield of a non-interest-bearing security.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3159191				0	gu	YIELDDISC(Settlement;Maturity;Price;Redemption;Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146924				0	gu	Maturity: the date on which the security is sold.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151201				0	gu	\<emph\>Price\</emph\>: The price of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156049				0	gu	\<emph\>Redemption\</emph\>: the redemption value of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154139				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3163815				0	gu	A non-interest-bearing security is purchased on 2/15/1999. It matures on 3/1/1999. The price is 99.795 currency units per 100 units of par value, the redemption value is 100 units. The basis is 2. How high is the yield?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155187				0	gu	=YIELDDISC("2/15/1999"; "3/1/1999"; 99.795; 100; 2) returns 0.052823 or 5.2823 per cent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155140				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>EXPONDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exponential distributions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155140				0	gu	YIELDMAT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151332				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_YIELDMAT\"\>Calculates the annual yield of a security, the interest of which is paid on the date of maturity.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3159113				0	gu	YIELDMAT(Settlement;Maturity;Issue;Rate;Price;Basis)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151381				0	gu	Maturity: the date on which the security is sold.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151067				0	gu	\<emph\>Price\</emph\>: The price of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155342				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3163717				0	gu	A security is purchased on 3/15/1999. It matures on 11/3/1999. The issue date was 11/8/1998. The rate of interest is 6.25%, the price is 100.0123 units. The basis is 0. How high is the yield?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155311				0	gu	=YIELDMAT("3/15/1999"; "11/3/1999"; "11/8/1998"; 0.0625; 100.0123; 0) returns 0.060954 or 6.0954 per cent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149577				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;annuities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>annuities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PMT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149577				0	gu	PMT				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RMZ\"\>Returns the periodic payment for an annuity with constant interest rates.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147278				0	gu	PMT(Rate; NPER; PV; FV; Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147291				0	gu	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148641				0	gu	\<emph\>NPER\</emph\> is the total number of periods, during which annuity is paid.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156360				0	gu	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present cash value in sequence of payments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154920				0	gu	FV (optional): the desired value (future value) to be reached at the end of the periodic payments.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156434				0	gu	Type (optional): the due date for the periodic payments. Type=1 is payment at the beginning and Type=0 is payment at the end of each period.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152358				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	gu	What are the periodic payments at a yearly interest rate of 1.99% if the payment time is 3 years and the cash value is 25,000 currency units. There are 36 months as 36 payment periods, and the interest rate per payment period is 1.99%/12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155943				0	gu	PMT(1.99%/12;36;25000) = -715.96 currency units. The periodic monthly payment is therefore 715.96 currency units.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155799				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;annuities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>annuities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PMT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155799				0	gu	TBILLEQ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154403				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_TBILLEQ\"\>Calculates the annual return on a treasury bill ().\</ahelp\> A treasury bill is purchased on the settlement date and sold at the full par value on the maturity date, that must fall within the same year. A discount is deducted from the purchase price.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	gu	TBILLEQ(Settlement;Maturity;Discount)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153827				0	gu	Maturity: the date on which the security is sold.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150310				0	gu	\<emph\>Discount\</emph\>: the percentage discount on acquisition of the security.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150324				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153173				0	gu	Settlement date: March 31 1999, maturity date: June 1 1999, discount: 9.14 per cent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153520				0	gu	The return on the treasury bill corresponding to a security is worked out as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	gu	=TBILLEQ("3/31/99";"6/1/99"; 0.0914) returns 0.094151 or 9.4151 per cent.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151032				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;annuities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>annuities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PMT function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
