helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153561				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>tables; showing details\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080200.xhp\" name=\"Show Details\"\>Show Details\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowDetail\"\>Shows the details of the grouped row or column that contains the cursor. To show the details of all of the grouped rows or columns, select the outlined table, and then choose this command.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922	3			0	gu	To hide a selected group, choose \<emph\>Data -Outline –\</emph\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080100.xhp\" name=\"Hide Details\"\>\<emph\>Hide Details\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Trace Precedents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155628				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>cells; tracing precedents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula cells;tracing precedents\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030100.xhp\" name=\"Trace Precedents\"\>Trace Precedents\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153542				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowPrecedents\"\>This function shows the relationship between the current cell containing a formula and the cells used in the formula.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	gu	Traces are displayed in the sheet with marking arrows. At the same time, the range of all the cells contained in the formula of the current cell is highlighted with a blue frame.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	gu	This function is based on a principle of layers. For example, if the precedent cell to a formula is already indicated with a tracer arrow, when you repeat this command, the tracer arrows are drawn to the precedent cells of this cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Protect Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150541				0	gu	Protect Document				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145172				0	gu	\<variable id=\"dokumenttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToolProtectionDocument\"\>Protects the sheet structure of your document from modifications. It is impossible to insert, delete, rename, move or copy sheets.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Open the \<emph\>Protect document\</emph\> dialog with \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\>. Optionally enter a password and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	gu	The structure of protected spreadsheet documents can be changed only if the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> option is disabled. On the context menus for the spreadsheet tabs at the lower graphic border, only the menu item \<emph\>Select All Sheets\</emph\> can be activated. All other menu items are deactivated. To remove the protection, call up the command \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</emph\> again. If no password is assigned, protection is immediately removed. If you were assigned a password, the \<emph\>Remove Spreadsheet Protection\</emph\> dialog appears, in which you must enter the password. Only then can you remove the check mark specifying that protection is active.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	7			0	gu	A protected document, once saved, can only be saved again with the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> menu command. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155412				0	gu	You can create a password to protect your document against unauthorized or accidental modifications.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	9			0	gu	You can completely protect your work by combining both options from \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, including password entry. If you want to prevent the document from being opened by other users, select \<emph\>Save With Password \</emph\>and click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button. The \<emph\>Enter Password\</emph\> dialog appears. Consider carefully when choosing a password; if you forget it after you close a document you will be unable to access the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Statistical Functions Part One				2002-02-02 02:02:02
