helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149729				0	gu	DCOUNTA				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150142				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ANZAHL2\"\>Counts how many values are in the list of arguments.\</ahelp\> Text entries are also counted, even when they contain an empty string of length 0. If an argument is an array or reference, empty cells within the array or reference are ignored.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153111				0	gu	COUNTA(value1; value2; ... value30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150001	26			0	gu	\<emph\>value1; value2, ...\</emph\> are 1 to 30 arguments representing the values to be counted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150334				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156061				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_B\"\>Returns the probability of a sample with binomial distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149002	35			0	gu	\<emph\>number\</emph\> is the number of repetitions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148875	36			0	gu	\<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of success for one trial.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145352	37			0	gu	\<emph\>T_1\</emph\> defines the lower limit for the number of trials.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149538	38			0	gu	\<emph\>T_2\</emph\> (optional) defines the upper limit for the number of trials.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154633				0	gu	What is the probability with ten throws of the dice, that a six will come up exactly twice? The probability of a six (or any other number) is 1/6. The following formula combines these factors:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158416				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>PV function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>present values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; present values\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158416				0	gu	RSQ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154949				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_BESTIMMTHEITSMASS\"\>Returns the square of the Pearson correlation coefficient based on the given values.\</ahelp\> RSQ (also called determination coefficient) is a measure for the accuracy of an adjustment and can be used to produce a regression analysis.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155822				0	gu	RSQ(Data_Y; Data_X)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150470	47			0	gu	\<emph\>Data_Y\</emph\> is an array or range of data points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3153181	48			0	gu	\<emph\>Data_X\</emph\> is an array or range of data points.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156258				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155991	50			0	gu	=RSQ(A1:A20; B1:B20) calculates the correlation coefficient for both data sets in columns A and B.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145620				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>EXPONDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exponential distributions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
