helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3156304	99			0	gu	\<emph\>Alpha\</emph\> is the percentage of the marginal data that will not be taken into consideration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151180				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3156130	101			0	gu	=TRIMMEAN(A1:A50; 0.1) calculates the mean value of numbers in A1:A50, without taking into consideration the 5 percent of the values representing the highest values and the 5 percent of the values representing the lowest ones. The percentage numbers refer to the amount of the untrimmed mean value, not to the number of summands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
