helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3146992	128			0	gu	\<emph\>Successes\</emph\> is the number of possible results in the total population.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3148826	129			0	gu	\<emph\>N_population \</emph\>is the size of the total population.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150529				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154904	131			0	gu	=HYPGEOMDIST(2; 2; 90; 100) yields 0.81. If 90 out of 100 pieces of buttered toast fall from the table and hit the floor with the buttered side first, then if 2 pieces of buttered toast are dropped from the table, the probability is 81%, that both will strike buttered side first.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
