helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155928				0	gu	STANDARDIZE				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3149883				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_STANDARDISIERUNG\"\>Converts a random variable to a normalized value.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3150132				0	gu	STANDARDIZE(Number; mean; STDEV)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3159139	50			0	gu	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value to be standardized.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241	51			0	gu	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> is the arithmetic mean of the distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874	52			0	gu	\<emph\>STDEV\</emph\> is the standard deviation for the total population.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145351				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156067	54			0	gu	=STANDARDIZE(11; 10; 1) returns 1. The value 11 in a normal distribution with a mean of 10 and a standard deviation of 1 is as much above the mean of 10, as the value 1 is above the mean of the standard normal distribution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157986				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>EXPONDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exponential distributions\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157986				0	gu	NORMSINV				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151282				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_STANDNORMINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the standard normal cumulative distribution.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154195				0	gu	NORMINV(Number)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3148772	60			0	gu	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the probability to which the inverse standard normal distribution is calculated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150934				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
