helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147336				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>worksheet names\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; sheet names\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; renaming\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792				0	gu	\<variable id=\"umbenennentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RenameTable\"\>This command opens a dialog where you can assign a different name to the current sheet.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	gu	Names				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092	5			0	gu	You can also open the\<emph\> Rename Sheet \</emph\>dialog through the context menu by positioning the mouse pointer over a sheet tab at the bottom of the window and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>clicking while pressing Ctrl \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>clicking the right mouse button\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05050100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	gu	Alternatively, click the sheet tab while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key. Now you can change the name directly. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/00/00000099.xhp#winmanager\"/\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155628				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; optimal column widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; optimal widths\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>optimal column widths\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	gu	\<variable id=\"optitext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SetOptimalColumnWidthDi\"\>Defines the optimal column width for selected columns.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The optimal column width depends on the longest entry within a column. You can choose from the available \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp#metrik\" name=\"measurement units\"\>measurement units\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:METRICFIELD:RID_SCDLG_COL_OPT:ED_VALUE\"\>Defines additional spacing between the longest entry in a column and the vertical column borders.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05040200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_COL_OPT:BTN_DEFVAL\"\>Defines the optimal column width in order to display the entire contents of the column.\</ahelp\> The additional spacing for the optimal column width is preset to 0.1 in.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151384				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; inserting columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; inserting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02190200.xhp\" name=\"Column Break\"\>Column Break\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DeleteColumnbreak\"\>Removes a manual column break to the left of the active cell.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02190200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145173				0	gu	Position the cursor in the cell to the right of the column break indicated by a vertical line and choose \<emph\>Edit - Delete Manual Break - Column Break\</emph\>. The manual column break is removed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	WEEKDAY 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154925				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154925				0	gu	\<variable id=\"weekday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weekday.xhp\"\>WEEKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154228				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WOCHENTAG\"\>Returns the day of the week for the given date value.\</ahelp\> The day is returned as an integer between 1 (Sunday) and 7 (Saturday) if no type or type = 1 is specified. If type=2, numbering begins at Monday=1; and if type=3 numbering begins at Monday=0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149033				0	gu	WEEKDAY(Number; Type)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149046				0	gu	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a date value, is a decimal for which the weekday is to be returned.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154394				0	gu	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> determines the type of calculation. For Type =1, the weekdays are counted starting from Sunday (this is the default even when the Type parameter is missing). For Type =2, the weekdays are counted starting from Monday =1. For Type = 3, the weekdays are counted starting from Monday = 0.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153836				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150317				0	gu	WEEKDAY("6/14/2000") returns 4 (the Type parameter is missing, therefore the standard count is used. The standard count starts with Sunday as day number 1. June 14, 2000 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 4).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	gu	WEEKDAY("7/24/1996";2) returns 3 (the Type parameter is 2, therefore Monday is day number 1. July 24, 1996 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 3).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153525				0	gu	WEEKDAY("7/24/1996";1) returns 4 (the Type parameter is 1, therefore Sunday is day number 1. July 24, 1996 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 4).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150575				0	gu	WEEKDAY(NOW()) returns the number of the current day.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150588	171			0	gu	To obtain a function indicating whether a day in A1 is a business day, use the IF and WEEKDAY functions as follows: IF(WEEKDAY(A1;2)<6;"Business day";"Weekend")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	gu	\<variable id=\"gueltigkeit\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Validation\"\>Defines what data is valid for a selected cell or cell range.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12120000.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D1				0	gu	You can also insert a list box from the Controls toolbar and link the list box to a cell. This way you can specify the valid values on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\"\>Data\</link\> page of the list box properties window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
