helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153820				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>MEDIAN function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153820				0	gu	MEDIAN				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MEDIAN\"\>Returns the median of a set of numbers. In a set containing an uneven number of values, the median will be the number in the middle of the set and in a set containing an even number of values, it will be the mean of the two values in the middle of the set.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264				0	gu	MEDIAN(Number 1; Number 2; ...Number 30)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109				0	gu	\<emph\>Number 1; Number 2;...Number 30\</emph\> are values or ranges, which represent a sample. Each number can also be replaced by a reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144506				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	gu	for an even number: =MEDIAN(1; 5; 9; 20) returns the average of the two middle values 5 and 9, thus 7.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
