helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	gu	\<variable id=\"define_label_range\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04070400.xhp\"\>Define Label Range\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	gu	\<variable id=\"beschtext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DefineLabelRange\"\>Opens a dialog in which you can define a label range.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411				0	gu	The cell contents of a label range can be used like names in formulas - $[officename] recognizes these names in the same manner that it does the predefined names of the weekdays and months. These names are automatically completed when typed into a formula. In addition, the names defined by label ranges will have priority over names defined by automatically generated ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	gu	You can set label ranges that contain the same labels on different sheets. $[officename] first searches the label ranges of the current sheet and, following a failed search, the ranges of other sheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_COLROWNAMERANGES:ED_AREA\"\>Displays the cell reference of each label range.\</ahelp\> In order to remove a label range from the list box, select it and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04070400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149121				0	gu	Contains row labels				2002-02-02 02:02:02
