helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146755				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>TIMEVALUE function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146755				0	gu	\<variable id=\"timevalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_timevalue.xhp\"\>TIMEVALUE\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3148502				0	gu	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZEITWERT\"\>TIMEVALUE returns the internal time number from a text enclosed by quotes and which may show a possible time entry format.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3150794				0	gu	The internal number indicated as a decimal is the result of the date system used under $[officename] to calculate date entries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3150823				0	gu	TIMEVALUE("Text")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3152556	165			0	gu	\<emph\>Text\</emph\> is a valid time expression and must be entered in quotation marks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146815				0	gu	Examples 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146829	167			0	gu	TIMEVALUE("4PM") returns 0.67. When formatting in time format HH:MM:SS, you then get 16:00:00.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_timevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632	168			0	gu	TIMEVALUE("24:00") returns 1. If you use the HH:MM:SS time format, the value is 00:00:00.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
