helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Consolidating Data				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	gu	\<variable id=\"consolidate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/consolidate.xhp\" name=\"Consolidating Data\"\>Consolidating Data\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	gu	During consolidation, the contents of the cells from several sheets will be combined in one place.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	gu	Open the document that contains the cell ranges to be consolidated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154513				0	gu	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Consolidate\</item\> to open the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	gu	From the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\> box select a source cell range to consolidate with other areas.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	gu	If the range is not named, click in the field next to the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\>. A blinking text cursor appears. Type a reference for the first source data range or select the range with the mouse.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert the selected range in the \<emph\>Consolidation areas\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153816				0	gu	Select additional ranges and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> after each selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157983				0	gu	Specify where you want to display the result by selecting a target range from the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150215				0	gu	If the target range is not named, click in the field next to \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> and enter the reference of the target range. Alternatively, you can select the range using the mouse or position the cursor in the top left cell of the target range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813				0	gu	Select a function from the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> box. The function specifies how the values of the consolidation ranges are linked. The "Sum" function is the default setting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149315				0	gu	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to consolidate the ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	gu	વધારાના સુયોજનાઓ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147250				0	gu	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog to display additional settings:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156400				0	gu	Select \<emph\>Link to source data\</emph\> to insert the formulas that generate the results in the target range, rather than the actual results. If you link the data, any values modified in the source range are automatically updated in the target range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	gu	The corresponding cell references in the target range are inserted in consecutive rows, which are automatically ordered and then hidden from view. Only the final result, based on the selected function, is displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149945				0	gu	Under \<emph\>Consolidate by\</emph\>, select either \<emph\>Row labels\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column labels\</emph\> if the cells of the source data range are not to be consolidated corresponding to the identical position of the cell in the range, but instead according to a matching row label or column label.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	gu	To consolidate by row labels or column labels, the label must be contained in the selected source ranges.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150478				0	gu	The text in the labels must be identical, so that rows or columns can be accurately matched. If the row or column label does not match any that exist in the target range, it will be appended as a new row or column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147468				0	gu	The data from the consolidation ranges and target range will be saved when you save the document. If you later open a document in which consolidation has been defined, this data will again be available.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153039				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Consolidate\"\>Data - Consolidate\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Applying Multiple Operations				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147559				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>multiple operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-classified tables\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559				0	gu	\<variable id=\"multioperation\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multioperation.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Operations\"\>Applying Multiple Operations\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	gu	Multiple Operations in Columns or Rows				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189				0	gu	You produce toys which you sell for $10 each. Each toy costs $2 to make, in addition to which you have fixed costs of $10,000 per year. How much profit will you make in a year if you sell a particular number of toys?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145239				0	gu	Calculating With One Formula and One Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146888				0	gu	To calculate the profit, first enter any number as the quantity (items sold) - in this example 2000. The profit is found from the formula Profit=Quantity * (Selling price - Direct costs) - Fixed costs. Enter this formula in B5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3159115				0	gu	Mark the range D2:E11, and thus the values in column D and the empty cells alongside in column E.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149723				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355				0	gu	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column\</emph\> field and click cell B4. This means that: B4, the quantity, is the variable in the formula, which is replaced by the marked column values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148725				0	gu	Calculating with Several Formulas Simultaneously				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880				0	gu	Delete column E.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154675				0	gu	Enter the following formula in C5: = B5 / B4. You are now calculating the annual profit per item sold.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148885				0	gu	Select the range D2;F11, thus three columns.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154846				0	gu	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, mark cells B5 thru C5.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	gu	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Columns\</emph\> field and click cell B4.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3150862				0	gu	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will now see the profits in column E and the annual profit per item in column F.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139				0	gu	Multiple Operations Across Rows and Columns				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149949				0	gu	Calculating with Two Variables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154808				0	gu	Consider columns A and B of the sample table above. You now want to vary not just the quantity produced annually, but also the selling price, and you are interested in the profit in each case.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149731				0	gu	Expand the table shown above. D2 thru D11 contain the numbers 500, 1000 and so on, up to 5000. In E1 through H1 enter the numbers 8, 10, 15 and 20.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3152810				0	gu	Select the range D1:H11.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153620				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	gu	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Rows\</emph\> field and click cell B1. This means that B1, the selling price, is the horizontally entered variable (with the values 8, 10, 15 and 20).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154049				0	gu	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column\</emph\> field and click in B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the vertically entered variable.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155104				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12060000.xhp\" name=\"Multiple operations\"\>Multiple operations\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Applying AutoFilter				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	gu	\<variable id=\"autofilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autofilter.xhp\" name=\"Applying AutoFilter\"\>Applying AutoFilter\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	gu	The \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function inserts a combo box on one or more data columns that lets you select the records (rows) to be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	gu	Select the columns you want to use AutoFilter on.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>. The combo box arrows are visible in the first row of the range selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	gu	Run the filter by clicking the drop-down arrow in the column heading and choosing an item.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	gu	Only those rows whose contents meet the filter criteria are displayed. The other rows are filtered. You can see if rows have been filtered from the discontinuous row numbers. The column that has been used for the filter is identified by a different color for the arrow button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	12			0	gu	To display all records again, select the \<emph\>-all-\</emph\> entry in the AutoFilter combo box. If you choose \<emph\>-Standard-\</emph\>, the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog appears, allowing you to set up a standard filter. Choose \<emph\>-Top 10-\</emph\> to display the highest 10 values only. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	gu	To stop using AutoFilter, reselect all cells selected in step 1 and once again choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	gu	The arithmetic functions also take account of the cells that are not visible due to an applied filter. For example, a sum of an entire column will also total the values in the filtered cells. Apply the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\> function if only the cells visible after the application of a filter are to be taken into account.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040100.xhp\" name=\"Data - Filter - AutoFilter\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
