helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id4544816				0	gu	\<variable id=\"borders\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/borders.xhp\"\>User Defined Borders in Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2320017				0	gu	You can apply a variety of different lines to selected cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8055665				0	gu	Select the cell or a block of cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9181188				0	gu	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9947508				0	gu	In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7907956				0	gu	Choose the border options you want to apply and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1342204				0	gu	The options in the \<emph\>Line arrangement\</emph\> area can be used to apply multiple border styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
