helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149255				0	gu	Creating Your Own Scenarios				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704	16			0	gu	To create a scenario, select all the cells that provide the data for the scenario. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150364				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Scenarios\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Create Scenario\</emph\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	gu	Enter a name for the new scenario and leave the other fields unchanged with their default values. Close the dialog with OK. Your new scenario is automatically activated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664				0	gu	Using Scenarios				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	gu	Scenarios can also be selected in the Navigator:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	gu	In the Navigator, you see the defined scenarios with the comments that were entered when the scenarios were created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	gu	If you want to know which values in the scenario affect other values, choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Trace Dependents\</emph\>. You will see arrows to the cells that are directly dependent on the current cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Creating Scenarios\"\>Creating Scenarios\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Using AutoFormat for Tables				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155132				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>tables; AutoFormat function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;AutoFormat function for tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoFormat function;defining and applying formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; automatically formatting spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic formatting in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;AutoFormat function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;automatic formatting\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155132				0	gu	\<variable id=\"autoformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autoformat.xhp\" name=\"Using AutoFormat for Tables\"\>Applying Automatic Formatting to a Selected Cell Range\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401				0	gu	You can use the AutoFormat feature to quickly apply format a sheet or a selected cell range.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	gu	To apply an AutoFormat to a sheet or selected cell range				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CE				0	gu	Select the cells, including the column and row headers, that you want to format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	gu	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	gu	To select which properties to include in an AutoFormat, click \<emph\>More\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	gu	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	gu	The format is applied to the selected range of cells.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210				0	gu	If you do not see any change in color of the cell contents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Value Highlighting\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379				0	gu	To define an AutoFormat for spreadsheets				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	gu	You can define a new AutoFormat that is available to all spreadsheets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	gu	Format a sheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	gu	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Select All\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153815				0	gu	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A9				0	gu	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Add AutoFormat\</emph\> dialog, enter a name for the format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C3				0	gu	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3159203				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05110000.xhp\" name=\"Format - AutoFormat\"\>Format - AutoFormat\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Formatting Numbers as Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; for numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; entering without number formats \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell formats; text/numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	gu	\<variable id=\"text_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers as Text\"\>Formatting Numbers as Text\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	gu	You can format numbers as text in $[officename] Calc. Open the context menu of a cell or range of cells and choose \<emph\>Format Cells - Numbers\</emph\>, then select "Text" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list. Any numbers subsequently entered into the formatted range are interpreted as text. The display of these "numbers" is left-justified, just as with other text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	gu	If you have already entered normal numbers in cells and have afterwards changed the format of the cells to "Text", the numbers will remain normal numbers. They will not be converted. Only numbers entered afterwards, or numbers which are then edited, will become text numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765				0	gu	If you decide to enter a number directly as text, enter an apostrophe (') first. For example, for years in column headings, you can enter '1999, '2000 and '2001. The apostrophe is not visible in the cell, it only indicates that the entry is to be recognized as a text. This is useful if, for example, you enter a telephone number or postal code that begins with a zero (0), because a zero (0) at the start of a sequence of digits is removed in normal number formats.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150542				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150542				0	gu	\<variable id=\"html_doc\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/html_doc.xhp\" name=\"Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\"\>Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154124				0	gu	Saving Sheets in HTML				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	gu	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc saves all the sheets of a Calc document together as an HTML document. At the beginning of the HTML document, a heading and a list of hyperlinks are automatically added which lead to the individual sheets within the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	gu	Numbers are shown as written. In addition, in the <SDVAL> HTML tag, the exact internal number value is written so that after opening the HTML document with \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you know you have the exact values.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	gu	To save the current Calc document as HTML, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	gu	In the \<emph\>Save as type\</emph\> list box, in the area with the other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc filters, choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	gu	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149379				0	gu	Opening Sheets in HTML				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	gu	Choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	gu	All \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc options are now available to you. However, not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc offers for editing can be saved in HTML format.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"File - Save As\"\>File - Save As\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Only Copy Visible Cells				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	gu	\<variable id=\"cellcopy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellcopy.xhp\" name=\"Only Copy Visible Cells\"\>Only Copy Visible Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3148577				0	gu	Assume you have hidden a few rows in a cell range. Now you want to copy, delete, or format only the remaining visible rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	gu	$[officename] behavior depends on how the cells were made invisible, by a filter or manually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	gu	Method and Action				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150751				0	gu	પરીણામ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	gu	Cells were filtered by AutoFilters, standard filters or advanced filters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	gu	Only the visible cells of the selection are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3166427				0	gu	Cells were hidden using the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> command in the context menu of the row or column headers, or through an \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"outline\"\>outline\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	gu	All cells of the selection, including the hidden cells, are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Printing Sheets in Landscape Format				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet selections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing in landscape\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; landscape\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>landscape printing\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	gu	\<variable id=\"print_landscape\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_landscape.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\"\>Printing Sheets in Landscape Format\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149257				0	gu	In order to print a sheet you have a number of interactive options available under \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>. Drag the delimiter lines to define the range of printed cells on each page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	gu	To print in landscape format, proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150089	5			0	gu	The command is not visible if the sheet has been opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430				0	gu	Select the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab. Select the \<emph\>Landscape\</emph\> paper format and click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3150885				0	gu	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3156288				0	gu	Depending on the printer driver and the operating system, it may be necessary to click the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button and to change your printer to landscape format there.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404	9			0	gu	In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>dialog under \<emph\>Print range\</emph\>, select the pages to be printed:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3153305	10			0	gu	\<emph\>All\</emph\> - All sheets will be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699	11			0	gu	\<emph\>Pages\</emph\> - Enter the pages to be printed. The pages will also be numbered from the first sheet onwards. If you see in the Page Break Preview that Sheet1 will be printed on 4 pages and you want to print the first two pages of Sheet2, enter 5-6 here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_landscape.xhp	0	help	par_id3145076				0	gu	If under \<emph\>Format - Print ranges\</emph\> you have defined one or more print ranges, only the contents of these print ranges will be printed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
