helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090900.xhp	0	help	par_id3153624				0	gu	The following is a list of sample formulas in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090907.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	અપૂર્ણંાકો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090907.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155961				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090907.xhp\" name=\"Functions\"\>Functions\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090907.xhp	0	help	par_id3148489				0	gu	Here is an example of how to create functions with \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>. If you want to use the example in your own formula, copy it to the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window using the clipboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090907.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	gu	\<image id=\"img_id3148871\" src=\"res/helpimg/smzb7.png\" width=\"7.987cm\" height=\"2.768cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148871\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148839				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>attributes; additional information\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148839				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091300.xhp\" name=\"Attributes\"\>Attributes\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	gu	Additional information about attributes in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\> is found here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	par_id3146966				0	gu	The \<emph\>acute\</emph\>, \<emph\>bar\</emph\>, \<emph\>breve\</emph\>, \<emph\>check\</emph\>, \<emph\>circle\</emph\>, \<emph\>dot\</emph\>, \<emph\>ddot\</emph\>, \<emph\>dddot\</emph\>, \<emph\>grave\</emph\>, \<emph\>hat\</emph\>, \<emph\>tilde\</emph\> and \<emph\>vec\</emph\> attributes always have a fixed size and do not become wider (longer) if they are above a long symbol. By default, the attributes are centered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154557				0	gu	The only attributes which grow with the length of the symbol are \<emph\>overline\</emph\>, \<emph\>underline\</emph\> and \<emph\>overstrike\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03091300.xhp	0	help	par_id3151180				0	gu	For some character strings, it is possible that a line inserted with \<emph\>underline\</emph\> is too close to the character. In this case, an empty group can solve the problem: \<emph\>underline Q sub {}\</emph\> instead of \<emph\>underline Q\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	અપૂર્ણંાકો				2002-02-02 02:02:02
