helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154657				0	gu	How does one attach comments that don't appear in the document to a formula?				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_id3149499				0	gu	A comment begins with a double percent sign \<emph\>%%\</emph\>, and extends to the next line-end character (Enter key). Everything that lies in between is ignored and is not printed out. If there are percent signs in the text, they are treated as part of the text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D0				0	gu	Example:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\comment.xhp	0	help	par_idN105D3				0	gu	a^2+b^2=c^2 %% Pythagorean theorem.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
