helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154125				0	gu	Integers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	gu	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that contains the serial date number that is used to determine the month of the year.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770	9			0	gu	This function is the opposite of the \<emph\>DateSerial \</emph\>function. It returns the month in the year that corresponds to the serial date that is generated by \<emph\>DateSerial\</emph\> or \<emph\>DateValue\</emph\>. For example, the expression				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	gu	Print Month(DateSerial(1994, 12, 20))				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030104.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	gu	returns the value 20.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
