helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	gu	\<emph\>[Variant]:\</emph\> Variant variable type (contains all types, specified by definition). If a key word is not specified, variables are automatically defined as Variant Type, unless a statement from DefBool to DefVar is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	gu	Arrays are declared with the Dim statement. There are two methods to define the index range:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154662				0	gu	DIM text(20) as String REM 21 elements numbered from 0 to 20				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155604				0	gu	DIM text(5 to 25) as String REM 21 elements numbered from 5 to 25				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151274				0	gu	DIM text(-15 to 5) as String REM 21 elements (including 0)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774				0	gu	REM numbered from -15 to 5				2002-02-02 02:02:02
