helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	CreateUnoValue Function [Runtime]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150682				0	gu	\<bookmark_value\>CreateUnoValue function\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150682				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03132300.xhp\" name=\"CreateUnoValue Function [Runtime]\"\>CreateUnoValue Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	par_id3147291	2			0	gu	Returns an object that represents a strictly typed value referring to the Uno type system. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	gu	This object is automatically converted to an Any of the corresponding type when passed to Uno. The type must be specified by its fully qualified Uno type name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626				0	gu	The $[officename] API frequently uses the Any type. It is the counterpart of the Variant type known from other environments. The Any type holds one arbitrary Uno type and is used in generic Uno interfaces.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	gu	oUnoValue = CreateUnoValue( "[]byte", MyBasicValue ) to get a byte sequence.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	gu	If CreateUnoValue cannot be converted to the specified Uno type, and error occurs. For the conversion, the TypeConverter service is used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153524				0	gu	This function is intended for use in situations where the default Basic to Uno type converting mechanism is insufficient. This can happen when you try to access generic Any based interfaces, such as XPropertySet::setPropertyValue( Name, Value ) or X???Container::insertBy???( ???, Value ), from $[officename] Basic. The Basic runtime does not recognize these types as they are only defined in the corresponding service.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	gu	In this type of situation, $[officename] Basic chooses the best matching type for the Basic type that you want to convert. However, if the wrong type is selected, an error occurs. You use the CreateUnoValue() function to create a value for the unknown Uno type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150769				0	gu	You can also use this function to pass non-Any values, but this is not recommend. If Basic already knows the target type, using the CreateUnoValue() function will only lead to additional converting operations that slow down the Basic execution.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	gu	Integrated Development Environment (IDE)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
