helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153126				0	gu	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020403.xhp\"\>CurDir Function [Runtime]\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3156343				0	gu	Returns a variant string that represents the current path of the specified drive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	gu	CurDir [(Text As String)]				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154366				0	gu	Return values:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	gu	Strings				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3153193				0	gu	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any string expression that specifies an existing drive (for example, "C" for the first partition of the first hard drive).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133				0	gu	If no drive is specified or if the drive is a zero-length string (""), CurDir returns the path for the current drive. $[officename] Basic reports an error if the syntax of the drive description is incorrect, the drive does not exist, or if the drive letter occurs after the letter defined in the CONFIG.SYS with the Lastdrive statement.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020403.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	gu	This function is not case-sensitive.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
